xploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/`\\n- **Output Directory**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/`\\n\\n## Technical Investigation Required\\n\\n### 1. Backend Status\\n- Verify backend server is running on expected port (8001)\\n- Check if endpoint registration is correct\\n- Validate endpoint handler function exists and is accessible\\n\\n### 2. Frontend API Calls\\n- Review `getGeneratedFiles()` function in `frontend/src/services/api.js`\\n- Verify correct URL construction and parameters\\n- Check polling interval and frequency (currently set to 1000ms in App.jsx)\\n\\n### 3. Potential Root Causes\\n- Backend server not running or crashed\\n- Endpoint URL mismatch between frontend and backend\\n- CORS configuration issues\\n- Activity tracker database connectivity problems\\n- Missing dependencies or import errors in backend\\n\\n## Files to Examine\\n\\n### Backend Files\\n1. `backend/main.py` - Main FastAPI application\\n   - Line 717: `@app.get(\\"/api/activity/files\\")` endpoint definition\\n   - Activity tracker integration\\n   - Error handling\\n\\n2. Backend runtime dependencies:\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Activity tracking system\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - AgentRuntime class\\n\\n### Frontend Files\\n1. `frontend/src/services/api.js` - API service layer\\n   - `getGeneratedFiles()` function\\n   - API_BASE_URL configuration\\n\\n2. `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Main application component\\n   - Polling logic for file updates\\n   - Error handling display\\n\\n3. `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx` - Files display component\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. Frontend polls `/api/activity/files` endpoint at configured interval\\n2. Backend returns JSON response with generated files:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"files\\": [...],\\n     \\"count\\": 0\\n   }\\n   ```\\n3. UI displays files in the \\"Generated Files\\" section without errors\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **No 404 errors** when frontend polls files endpoint\\n2. **Correct response format** - JSON without BOM characters\\n3. **Files displayed** in UI when agents generate outputs\\n4. **Error handling** - Graceful degradation if backend temporarily unavailable\\n5. **Logging** - Clear error messages in both frontend console and backend logs\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- **No breaking changes** to existing API contract\\n- **Maintain backwards compatibility** with current frontend implementation\\n- **Minimal code changes** - focus on fixing the specific 404 issue\\n- **Preserve existing functionality** - don\'t break other endpoints\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Adding new features to file display\\n- Redesigning the UI layout\\n- Changing polling architecture to WebSockets\\n- Performance optimization beyond fixing the bug\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Backend is intended to run on port 8001\\n- Frontend is configured to connect to localhost:8001\\n- Activity tracker database exists and is accessible at `~/.ensemble/metrics.db`\\n- All required Python dependencies are installed\\n\\n## Acceptance Tests\\n\\n1. **Backend health check**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/status` returns 200 OK\\n2. **Files endpoint test**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/activity/files` returns JSON (not 404)\\n3. **Frontend test**: Open UI in browser, verify no 404 errors in console for `/api/activity/files`\\n4. **Integration test**: Generate a file via agent execution, verify it appears in UI without errors\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Root cause analysis** - Document why 404 was occurring\\n2. **Code fixes** - Implement solution in backend/frontend as needed\\n3. **Verification** - Test all affected endpoints work correctly\\n4. **Documentation** - Update any relevant docs about endpoint usage\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|n