{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:03:53", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-5efc0c93-c6bd-4a75-9798-5bab93cbafcf', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Agent Completion Visibility Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ncx6yQidAkiSqMnqNrdWJ4', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ncx6yQidAkiSqMnqNrdWJ4', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Completion Summary Visibility\\n\\n## Vision\\nMake agent completion results visible in the UI so users can see what each bot actually did. When agents complete, their summary should be prominently displayed - not hidden behind expandable sections.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nUser reports: \\"Bots show completed, but I don\'t see any UI changes. What was the status of the last task?\\"\\n\\nThe current system:\\n1. Agents produce structured outputs with `summary`, `self_analysis`, `deliverables` fields\\n2. These are stored in `result` data when agent completes  \\n3. BUT: The UI only shows \\"Completed\\" status - the actual summary is hidden in expandable detail sections\\n4. User cannot easily see what each agent accomplished without clicking through multiple levels\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Display agent completion summaries prominently in the Agent Tasks section\\n2. Show two-sentence summary of what each agent did when it completes\\n3. Make deliverables list visible for completed agents\\n4. Enhance Activity Feed to highlight completion summaries\\n5. Provide better communication between bots and user\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Agent Tasks Section Enhancement**\\n  - When agent status is \\"completed\\", show summary text prominently below the status\\n  - Display up to 2-3 key points from `result.summary` or `result.self_analysis`\\n  - Show count of deliverables (e.g., \\"Created 3 files\\") with option to expand\\n  - Add visual indication that detailed info is available (e.g., info icon)\\n\\n- **Activity Feed Enhancement**\\n  - For `agent_completed` activities, show summary text in the collapsed view\\n  - Make completion entries more informative without requiring expansion\\n  - Include deliverable count in activity entry\\n\\n- **Agent State Storage Enhancement**  \\n  - Ensure `summary`, `self_analysis`, and `deliverables` from agent output are stored in agent_states\\n  - These fields should be accessible via `/api/activity/states` endpoint\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time streaming of agent output (future enhancement)\\n- Notification system for completions\\n- Historical summary browsing\\n- Detailed cost/token display in summary\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n### Story 1: View Completion Summary\\n**As a** user monitoring agent progress  \\n**I want to** see a summary of what each agent accomplished when it completes  \\n**So that** I understand what happened without digging through logs\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- When agent status changes to \\"completed\\", a 1-2 sentence summary appears below the status badge\\n- Summary is visible without clicking or expanding anything\\n- If no summary is available, show \\"Completed successfully\\" or similar default\\n\\n### Story 2: See Deliverables at a Glance\\n**As a** user tracking project output  \\n**I want to** see what files/artifacts each agent produced  \\n**So that** I know what to look for in the Generated Files section\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Completed agents show deliverable count (e.g., \\"\\ud83d\\udcc1 3 deliverables\\")\\n- Clicking reveals the list of deliverable paths\\n- Links to corresponding entries in Generated Files section (if applicable)\\n\\n### Story 3: Activity Feed Context\\n**As a** user reviewing activity history  \\n**I want to** see completion context in the Activity Feed  \\n**So that** I can scan through and understand what happened without expanding each item\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Agent completion activities show first line of summary in preview\\n- Still expandable for full details\\n- Clear visual distinction for completion events\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Data Flow (Existing - needs exposure to UI)\\n```\\nAgent Output \\u2192 {\\n  status: \\"success\\",\\n  summary: \\"What was accomplished\\",\\n  self_analysis: \\"Performance reflection\\",\\n  deliverables: [\\"path1.md\\", \\"path2.py\\"],\\n  ...\\n}\\n\\n\\u2193 stored in \\u2193\\n\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_completed(result={...})\\nagent_states[agent_id] = { status: \\"completed\\", ... }\\n\\n\\u2193 exposed via \\u2193\\n\\nGET /api/activity/states \\u2192 { agent_states: { agent_id: {...} } }\\n```\\n\\n### Frontend Changes Needed\\n\\n**App.jsx - Agent Tasks Section:**\\n```jsx\\n// After status badge, add:\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.summary && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'12px\', color: \'#9ca3af\', marginTop: \'6px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcdd {state.summary.slice(0, 150)}...\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#6b7280\', marginTop: \'4px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcc1 {state.deliverables.length} deliverable(s)\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n```\\n\\n**ActivityFeed.jsx - Completion Display:**\\n```jsx\\ncase \'agent_completed\':\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {data.result?.summary && (\\n        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n          <strong>Summary:</strong> {data.result.summary}\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      {data.result?.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>Deliverables:</strong> {data.result.deliverables.length} file(s)\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      // ...existing detail expansion\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n```\\n\\n### Backend Changes Needed\\n\\n**backend/main.py - _execute_agent_background():**\\nEnsure result fields are stored in active_agents state:\\n```python\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"result\\"] = result\\n# ADD: Extract key summary fields for easy access\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"self_analysis\\"] = result.get(\\"self_analysis\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", [])\\n```\\n\\n**activity_tracker.py - record_agent_completed():**\\nExtract and store summary in agent_states:\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_completed(self, agent_id, agent_name, request_id, result=None):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    \\n    # Update agent state with summary info\\n    if agent_id in self.agent_states:\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\") if result else \\"\\"\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", []) if result else []\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Visibility**: Agent completion summaries visible without any clicks\\n2. **Informativeness**: User can understand what happened at a glance\\n3. **Non-disruptive**: Changes don\'t break existing functionality\\n4. **Graceful degradation**: Works when summary fields are missing (shows default text)\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Start a task and let agents complete\\n2. Verify summary text appears in Agent Tasks section for completed agents\\n3. Verify Activity Feed shows summary in agent_completed entries\\n4. Verify deliverable count displays correctly\\n5. Test with agents that don\'t return summary (should show fallback)\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Keep changes minimal - enhance existing components rather than replacing\\n- Use existing styling patterns for consistency\\n- Summary text should truncate gracefully if too long\\n- Consider adding \\"Show more\\" link for full self_analysis\\n\\n## Related Files\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Agent Tasks section (~lines 400-460)\\n- `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx` - renderActivityDetails function\\n- `backend/main.py` - _execute_agent_background function\\n- `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - record_agent_completed function\\n\\n## Priority: HIGH\\nThis directly impacts user experience and understanding of system behavior.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016jfNni96WL3MWbGvE2js7y', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: Agent Completion Visibility Implementation\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### Purpose\nEnhance the UI to provide clear, immediate visibility into agent task completions, allowing users to quickly understand the outcomes of agent interactions without unnecessary navigation.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n- **Frontend**: Reactive Component-Based Architecture\n- **Backend**: Event-Driven State Management\n- **Integration**: Real-Time State Synchronization\n\n### Core Design Principle\nMinimize user cognitive load by surfacing critical information (agent task summaries) directly in the primary view.\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React (existing)\n- **State Management**: React Context API\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (assuming current project styling)\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python (existing)\n- **Framework**: FastAPI (for potential API enhancements)\n- **State Management**: In-memory dictionary with thread-safe updates\n\n### Key Libraries\n- `react-icons` for visual indicators\n- `axios` for API communication\n- `python-dotenv` for configuration\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. Frontend Components\n- **AgentTasksSection**\n  - Responsible for rendering agent task statuses\n  - Displays completion summaries\n  - Shows deliverable counts\n  \n- **ActivityFeedComponent**\n  - Renders agent completion events\n  - Provides expanded/collapsed views of completion details\n\n### 2. Backend Components\n- **ActivityTracker**\n  - Manages agent state tracking\n  - Stores and retrieves agent completion information\n  \n- **StateManager**\n  - Handles state persistence and retrieval\n  - Provides API endpoints for state access\n\n## D. Data Flow\n\n```\nAgent Completion \n    ↓\nActivityTracker.record_agent_completed()\n    ↓\nUpdate active_agents and agent_states\n    ↓\nExpose via /api/activity/states\n    ↓\nFrontend Components Render\n    - AgentTasksSection\n    - ActivityFeed\n```\n\n## E. API Endpoint Design\n\n### GET /api/activity/states\n- **Response Structure**:\n```json\n{\n  "agent_states": {\n    "agent_id": {\n      "status": "completed",\n      "summary": "Two-sentence description of work",\n      "deliverables": ["path/to/file1", "path/to/file2"],\n      "timestamp": "ISO8601 timestamp"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## F. State Management Strategy\n- Use React Context for lightweight state management\n- Backend maintains immutable state dictionaries\n- Implement optimistic updates for responsive UI\n\n## G. Deployment Considerations\n- Zero-downtime deployment\n- Feature flag for gradual rollout\n- Backward compatibility with existing UI\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Frontend Tests\n- Snapshot testing for AgentTasksSection\n- Interaction tests for summary expansion\n- State rendering tests\n\n### Backend Tests\n- Unit tests for ActivityTracker\n- Integration tests for state persistence\n- API endpoint validation\n\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: Performance Overhead\n- **Mitigation**: Implement lazy loading, limit summary length\n  \n### Risk 2: Incomplete Agent Outputs\n- **Mitigation**: Graceful fallback to default messages\n\n## J. Alternative Approaches Considered\n1. Modal-based summaries (rejected - too intrusive)\n2. Separate summary page (rejected - requires extra navigation)\n\n## K. Open Questions\n- How verbose should default summaries be?\n- Should we implement a "show more" mechanism for longer summaries?\n\n## Architectural Decision Record\n\n### Key Decisions\n1. Surface summaries directly in existing components\n2. Minimal changes to existing architecture\n3. Leverage current state management infrastructure\n\n---\n\n**Implementation Priority**: HIGH\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium (2-3 sprint points)\n**Potential User Impact**: Significant improvement in task comprehension'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016jfNni96WL3MWbGvE2js7y', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_020353.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_020353.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses all requirements while maintaining system consistency. By focusing on minimal, targeted changes and leveraging existing infrastructure, the design redu...\n- Successfully conducted a comprehensive technical validation of the theme dropdown architecture. Applied systematic analysis across performance, security, scalability, and implementation feasibility di...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
