{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:04:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-fdc4becb-493f-4060-98f4-50fa4cbcc3be', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Agent Completion Visibility Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ta6PF1vcR6Bfb5K2d49nm9', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ta6PF1vcR6Bfb5K2d49nm9', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Completion Summary Visibility\\n\\n## Vision\\nMake agent completion results visible in the UI so users can see what each bot actually did. When agents complete, their summary should be prominently displayed - not hidden behind expandable sections.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nUser reports: \\"Bots show completed, but I don\'t see any UI changes. What was the status of the last task?\\"\\n\\nThe current system:\\n1. Agents produce structured outputs with `summary`, `self_analysis`, `deliverables` fields\\n2. These are stored in `result` data when agent completes  \\n3. BUT: The UI only shows \\"Completed\\" status - the actual summary is hidden in expandable detail sections\\n4. User cannot easily see what each agent accomplished without clicking through multiple levels\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Display agent completion summaries prominently in the Agent Tasks section\\n2. Show two-sentence summary of what each agent did when it completes\\n3. Make deliverables list visible for completed agents\\n4. Enhance Activity Feed to highlight completion summaries\\n5. Provide better communication between bots and user\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Agent Tasks Section Enhancement**\\n  - When agent status is \\"completed\\", show summary text prominently below the status\\n  - Display up to 2-3 key points from `result.summary` or `result.self_analysis`\\n  - Show count of deliverables (e.g., \\"Created 3 files\\") with option to expand\\n  - Add visual indication that detailed info is available (e.g., info icon)\\n\\n- **Activity Feed Enhancement**\\n  - For `agent_completed` activities, show summary text in the collapsed view\\n  - Make completion entries more informative without requiring expansion\\n  - Include deliverable count in activity entry\\n\\n- **Agent State Storage Enhancement**  \\n  - Ensure `summary`, `self_analysis`, and `deliverables` from agent output are stored in agent_states\\n  - These fields should be accessible via `/api/activity/states` endpoint\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time streaming of agent output (future enhancement)\\n- Notification system for completions\\n- Historical summary browsing\\n- Detailed cost/token display in summary\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n### Story 1: View Completion Summary\\n**As a** user monitoring agent progress  \\n**I want to** see a summary of what each agent accomplished when it completes  \\n**So that** I understand what happened without digging through logs\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- When agent status changes to \\"completed\\", a 1-2 sentence summary appears below the status badge\\n- Summary is visible without clicking or expanding anything\\n- If no summary is available, show \\"Completed successfully\\" or similar default\\n\\n### Story 2: See Deliverables at a Glance\\n**As a** user tracking project output  \\n**I want to** see what files/artifacts each agent produced  \\n**So that** I know what to look for in the Generated Files section\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Completed agents show deliverable count (e.g., \\"\\ud83d\\udcc1 3 deliverables\\")\\n- Clicking reveals the list of deliverable paths\\n- Links to corresponding entries in Generated Files section (if applicable)\\n\\n### Story 3: Activity Feed Context\\n**As a** user reviewing activity history  \\n**I want to** see completion context in the Activity Feed  \\n**So that** I can scan through and understand what happened without expanding each item\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Agent completion activities show first line of summary in preview\\n- Still expandable for full details\\n- Clear visual distinction for completion events\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Data Flow (Existing - needs exposure to UI)\\n```\\nAgent Output \\u2192 {\\n  status: \\"success\\",\\n  summary: \\"What was accomplished\\",\\n  self_analysis: \\"Performance reflection\\",\\n  deliverables: [\\"path1.md\\", \\"path2.py\\"],\\n  ...\\n}\\n\\n\\u2193 stored in \\u2193\\n\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_completed(result={...})\\nagent_states[agent_id] = { status: \\"completed\\", ... }\\n\\n\\u2193 exposed via \\u2193\\n\\nGET /api/activity/states \\u2192 { agent_states: { agent_id: {...} } }\\n```\\n\\n### Frontend Changes Needed\\n\\n**App.jsx - Agent Tasks Section:**\\n```jsx\\n// After status badge, add:\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.summary && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'12px\', color: \'#9ca3af\', marginTop: \'6px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcdd {state.summary.slice(0, 150)}...\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#6b7280\', marginTop: \'4px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcc1 {state.deliverables.length} deliverable(s)\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n```\\n\\n**ActivityFeed.jsx - Completion Display:**\\n```jsx\\ncase \'agent_completed\':\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {data.result?.summary && (\\n        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n          <strong>Summary:</strong> {data.result.summary}\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      {data.result?.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>Deliverables:</strong> {data.result.deliverables.length} file(s)\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      // ...existing detail expansion\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n```\\n\\n### Backend Changes Needed\\n\\n**backend/main.py - _execute_agent_background():**\\nEnsure result fields are stored in active_agents state:\\n```python\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"result\\"] = result\\n# ADD: Extract key summary fields for easy access\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"self_analysis\\"] = result.get(\\"self_analysis\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", [])\\n```\\n\\n**activity_tracker.py - record_agent_completed():**\\nExtract and store summary in agent_states:\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_completed(self, agent_id, agent_name, request_id, result=None):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    \\n    # Update agent state with summary info\\n    if agent_id in self.agent_states:\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\") if result else \\"\\"\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", []) if result else []\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Visibility**: Agent completion summaries visible without any clicks\\n2. **Informativeness**: User can understand what happened at a glance\\n3. **Non-disruptive**: Changes don\'t break existing functionality\\n4. **Graceful degradation**: Works when summary fields are missing (shows default text)\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Start a task and let agents complete\\n2. Verify summary text appears in Agent Tasks section for completed agents\\n3. Verify Activity Feed shows summary in agent_completed entries\\n4. Verify deliverable count displays correctly\\n5. Test with agents that don\'t return summary (should show fallback)\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Keep changes minimal - enhance existing components rather than replacing\\n- Use existing styling patterns for consistency\\n- Summary text should truncate gracefully if too long\\n- Consider adding \\"Show more\\" link for full self_analysis\\n\\n## Related Files\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Agent Tasks section (~lines 400-460)\\n- `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx` - renderActivityDetails function\\n- `backend/main.py` - _execute_agent_background function\\n- `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - record_agent_completed function\\n\\n## Priority: HIGH\\nThis directly impacts user experience and understanding of system behavior.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WmC82YYGoFwfK1NWZB9sXT', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Milestone Plan: Agent Completion Visibility Implementation\n\n## Project Overview\n**Objective**: Make agent completion results visible in the UI so users can see what each bot actually accomplished without digging through expandable sections.\n\n**Timeline**: 2 milestones - focused implementation\n\n## Milestone 1: Backend Data Enhancement (Foundation)\n**Duration**: ~1 day  \n**Objective**: Ensure completion data is properly stored and exposed for UI consumption\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Enhanced agent state storage to capture summary, self_analysis, and deliverables\n2. Updated activity tracker to extract and store key completion fields\n3. Modified API response to include summary information in agent states\n4. Backend testing to verify data flow\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- `GET /api/activity/states` returns summary, self_analysis, and deliverables fields for completed agents\n- Agent completion data is properly stored in active_agents state during execution\n- Activity tracker captures completion summaries when recording agent_completed events\n- Existing functionality remains unaffected\n- Backend tests pass for data flow verification\n\n### Dependencies: None\n\n### Tasks:\n- Modify `_execute_agent_background()` in backend/main.py to store result fields\n- Update `record_agent_completed()` in activity_tracker.py to extract summary info\n- Add agent state data validation\n- Create unit tests for enhanced data storage\n- Test API endpoint returns enhanced agent state data\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Display Implementation (User-Facing)\n**Duration**: ~1 day  \n**Objective**: Display completion summaries and deliverables prominently in the UI\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Enhanced Agent Tasks section showing completion summaries\n2. Improved Activity Feed with completion context\n3. Deliverable count display with expansion capability\n4. Graceful fallback handling for missing data\n5. Frontend testing and validation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Completed agents show 1-2 sentence summary below status badge\n- Deliverable count displays as "📁 X deliverable(s)" with expandable list\n- Activity Feed shows completion summary in preview without expansion\n- UI handles missing summary/deliverable data gracefully\n- No visual regressions in existing UI components\n- Summary text truncates appropriately for long content\n\n### Dependencies: \n- Milestone 1 completion (backend data availability)\n\n### Tasks:\n- Update Agent Tasks section in App.jsx to display summaries\n- Enhance ActivityFeed.jsx to show completion context\n- Add deliverable count and expansion UI\n- Implement text truncation and "Show more" functionality\n- Add graceful fallback for missing data\n- Create frontend tests for new display components\n- Conduct user experience testing\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment:\n- **Low Risk**: Well-defined scope, existing infrastructure\n- **Minimal UI Impact**: Enhancing existing components, not rebuilding\n- **Data Compatibility**: Backend changes are additive, maintain backwards compatibility\n\n## Success Metrics:\n1. User can see what each agent accomplished without clicking\n2. Zero regressions in existing functionality\n3. Completion summaries display for 100% of completed agents\n4. Activity Feed entries provide immediate context\n\n## Dependencies & Constraints:\n- Must maintain existing API compatibility\n- UI changes must follow existing design patterns\n- Performance impact should be negligible'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WmC82YYGoFwfK1NWZB9sXT', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_020324.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_020324.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UgPh3k5JYDkHfxy5G6nzug', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Agent Completion Visibility Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UgPh3k5JYDkHfxy5G6nzug', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal created for Agent Completion Visibility Implementation, focusing on enhancing UI to prominently display agent task summaries", "key_decisions": ["Surface summaries directly in existing components", "Minimal changes to existing architecture", "Leverage current state management infrastructure"], "self_analysis": "The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s core structure while providing significant usability improvements through strategic component modifications."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
