s\\n1. Display agent completion summaries prominently in the Agent Tasks section\\n2. Show two-sentence summary of what each agent did when it completes\\n3. Make deliverables list visible for completed agents\\n4. Enhance Activity Feed to highlight completion summaries\\n5. Provide better communication between bots and user\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Agent Tasks Section Enhancement**\\n  - When agent status is \\"completed\\", show summary text prominently below the status\\n  - Display up to 2-3 key points from `result.summary` or `result.self_analysis`\\n  - Show count of deliverables (e.g., \\"Created 3 files\\") with option to expand\\n  - Add visual indication that detailed info is available (e.g., info icon)\\n\\n- **Activity Feed Enhancement**\\n  - For `agent_completed` activities, show summary text in the collapsed view\\n  - Make completion entries more informative without requiring expansion\\n  - Include deliverable count in activity entry\\n\\n- **Agent State Storage Enhancement**  \\n  - Ensure `summary`, `self_analysis`, and `deliverables` from agent output are stored in agent_states\\n  - These fields should be accessible via `/api/activity/states` endpoint\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time streaming of agent output (future enhancement)\\n- Notification system for completions\\n- Historical summary browsing\\n- Detailed cost/token display in summary\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n### Story 1: View Completion Summary\\n**As a** user monitoring agent progress  \\n**I want to** see a summary of what each agent accomplished when it completes  \\n**So that** I understand what happened without digging through logs\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- When agent status changes to \\"completed\\", a 1-2 sentence summary appears below the status badge\\n- Summary is visible without clicking or expanding anything\\n- If no summary is available, show \\"Completed successfully\\" or similar default\\n\\n### Story 2: See Deliverables at a Glance\\n**As a** user tracking project output  \\n**I want to** see what files/artifacts each agent produced  \\n**So that** I know what to look for in the Generated Files section\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Completed agents show deliverable count (e.g., \\"\\ud83d\\udcc1 3 deliverables\\")\\n- Clicking reveals the list of deliverable paths\\n- Links to corresponding entries in Generated Files section (if applicable)\\n\\n### Story 3: Activity Feed Context\\n**As a** user reviewing activity history  \\n**I want to** see completion context in the Activity Feed  \\n**So that** I can scan through and understand what happened without expanding each item\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Agent completion activities show first line of summary in preview\\n- Still expandable for full details\\n- Clear visual distinction for completion events\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Data Flow (Existing - needs exposure to UI)\\n```\\nAgent Output \\u2192 {\\n  status: \\"success\\",\\n  summary: \\"What was accomplished\\",\\n  self_analysis: \\"Performance reflection\\",\\n  deliverables: [\\"path1.md\\", \\"path2.py\\"],\\n  ...\\n}\\n\\n\\u2193 stored in \\u2193\\n\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_completed(result={...})\\nagent_states[agent_id] = { status: \\"completed\\", ... }\\n\\n\\u2193 exposed via \\u2193\\n\\nGET /api/activity/states \\u2192 { agent_states: { agent_id: {...} } }\\n```\\n\\n### Frontend Changes Needed\\n\\n**App.jsx - Agent Tasks Section:**\\n```jsx\\n// After status badge, add:\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.summary && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'12px\', color: \'#9ca3af\', marginTop: \'6px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcdd {state.summary.slice(0, 150)}...\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#6b7280\', marginTop: \'4px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcc1 {state.deliverables.length} deliverable(s)\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n```\\n\\n**ActivityFeed.jsx - Completion Display:**\\n```jsx\\ncase \'agent_completed\':\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {data.result?.summary && (\\n        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n          <strong>Summary:</strong> {data.result.summary}\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      {data.result?.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>Deliverables:</strong> {data.result.deliverables.length} file(s)\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      // ...existing detail expansion\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n```\\n\\n### Backend Changes Needed\\n\\n**backend/main.py - _execute_agent_background():**\\nEnsure result fields are stored in active_agents state:\\n```python\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"result\\"] = result\\n# ADD: Extract key summary fields for easy access\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"self_analysis\\"] = result.get(\\"self_analysis\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", [])\\n```\\n\\n**activity_tracker.py - record_agent_completed():**\\nExtract and store summary in agent_states:\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_completed(self, agent_id, agent_name, request_id, result=None):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    \\n    # Update agent state with summary info\\n    if agent_id in self.agent_states:\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\") if result else \\"\\"\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", []) if result else []\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Visibility**: Agent completion summaries visible without any clicks\\n2. **Informativeness**: User can understand what happened at a glance\\n3. **Non-disruptive**: Changes don\'t break existing functionality\\n4. **Graceful degradation**: Works when summary fields are missing (shows default text)\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Start a task and let agents complete\\n2. Verify summary text appears in Agent Tasks section for completed agents\\n3. Verify Activity Feed shows summary in agent_completed entries\\n4. Verify deliverable count displays correctly\\n5. Test with agents that don\'t return summary (should show fallback)\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Keep changes minimal - enhance existing components rather than replacing\\n- Use existing styling patterns for consistency\\n- Summary text should truncate gracefully if too long\\n- Consider adding \\"Show more\\" link for full self_analysis\\n\\n## Related Files\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Agent Tasks section (~lines 400-460)\\n- `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx` - renderActivityDetails function\\n- `backend/main.py` - _execute_agent_background function\\n- `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - record_agent_completed function\\n\\n## Priority: HIGH\\nThis directly impacts user experience and understanding of system behavior.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WmC82YYGoFwfK1NWZB9sXT', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Milestone Plan: Agent Completion Visibility Implementation\n\n## Project Overview\n**Objective**: Make agent completion results visible in the UI so users can see what each bot actually accomplished without digging through expandable sections.\n\n**Timeline**: 2 milestones - focused implementation\n\n## Milestone 1: Backend Data Enhancement (Foundation)\n**Duration**: ~1 day  \n**Objective**: Ensure completion data is properly stored and exposed for UI consumption\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Enhanced agent state storage to capture summary, self_analysis, and deliverables\n2. Updated activity tracker to extract and store key completion fields\n3. Modified API response to include summary information in agent states\n4. Backend testing to verify data flow\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- `GET /api/activity/states` returns summary, self_analysis, and deliverables fields for completed agents\n- Agent completion data is properly stored in active_agents state during execution\n- Activity tracker captures completion summaries when recording agent_completed events\n- Existing functionality remains unaffected\n- Backend tests pass for data flow verification\n\n### Dependencies: None\n\n### Tasks:\n- Modify `_execute_agent_background()` in backend/main.py to store result fields\n- Update `record_agent_completed()` in activity_tracker.py to extract summary info\n- Add agent state data validation\n- Create unit tests for enhanced data storage\n- Test API endpoint returns enhanced agent state data\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Display Implementation (User-Facing)\n**Duration**: ~1 day  \n**Objective**: Display completion summaries and deliverables prominently in the UI\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Enhanced Agent Tasks section showing completion summaries\n2. Improved Activity Feed with completion context\n3. Deliverable count display with expansion capability\n4. Graceful fallback handling for missing data\n5. Frontend testing and validation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Completed agents show 1-2 sentence summary below status badge\n- Deliverable count displays as "📁 X deliverable(s)" with expandable list\n- Activity Feed shows completion summary in preview without expansion\n- UI handles missing summary/deliverable data gracefully\n- No visual regressions in existing UI components\n- Summary text truncates appropriately for long content\n\n### Dependencies: \n- Milestone 1 completion (backend data availability)\n\n### Tasks:\n- Update Agent Tasks section in App.jsx to display summaries\n- Enhance ActivityFeed.jsx to show completion context\n- Add deliverable count and expansion UI\n- Implement text truncation and "Show more" functionality\n- Add graceful fallback for missing data\n- Create frontend tests for new display components\n- Conduct user experience testing\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment:\n- **Low Risk**: Well-defined scope, existing infrastructure\n- **Minimal UI Impact**: Enhancing existing components, not rebuilding\n- **Data Compatibility**: Backend changes are additive, maintain backwards compatibility\n\n## Success Metrics:\n1. User can see what each agent accomplished without clicking\n2. Zero regressions in existing functionality\n3. Completion summaries display for 100% of completed agents\n4. Activity Feed entries provide immediate context\n\n## Dependencies & Constraints:\n- Must maintain existing API compatibility\n- UI changes must follow existing design patterns\n- Performance impact should be negligible'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WmC82YYGoFwfK1NWZB9sXT', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_020324.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_020324.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UgPh3k5JYDkHfxy5G6nzug', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Agent Completion Visibility Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UgPh3k5JYDkHfxy5G6nzug', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal created for Agent Completion Visibility Implementation, focusing on enhancing UI to prominently display agent task summaries", "key_decisions": ["Surface summaries directly in existing components", "Minimal changes to existing architecture", "Leverage current state management infrastructure"], "self_analysis": "The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s core structure while providing significant usability improvements through strategic component modifications."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DuRbSKfV6vP62nR9ifCsLd', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DuRbSKfV6vP62nR9ifCsLd', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: Agent Completion Visibility Implementation\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Purpose\\nEnhance the UI to provide clear, immediate visibility into agent task completions, allowing users to quickly understand the outcomes of agent interactions without unnecessary navigation.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Frontend**: Reactive Component-Based Architecture\\n- **Backend**: Event-Driven State Management\\n- **Integration**: Real-Time State Synchronization\\n\\n### Core Design Principle\\nMinimize user cognitive load by surfacing critical information (agent task summaries) directly in the primary view.\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React (existing)\\n- **State Management**: React Context API\\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (assuming current project styling)\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python (existing)\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI (for potential API enhancements)\\n- **State Management**: In-memory dictionary with thread-safe updates\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `react-icons` for visual indicators\\n- `axios` for API communication\\n- `python-dotenv` for configuration\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Frontend Components\\n- **AgentTasksSection**\\n  - Responsible for rendering agent task statuses\\n  - Displays completion summaries\\n  - Shows deliverable counts\\n  \\n- **ActivityFeedComponent**\\n  - Renders agent completion events\\n  - Provides expanded/collapsed views of completion details\\n\\n### 2. Backend Components\\n- **ActivityTracker**\\n  - Manages agent state tracking\\n  - Stores and retrieves agent completion information\\n  \\n- **StateManager**\\n  - Handles state persistence and retrieval\\n  - Provides API endpoints for state access\\n\\n## D. Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nAgent Completion \\n    \\u2193\\nActivityTracker.record_agent_completed()\\n    \\u2193\\nUpdate active_agents and agent_states\\n    \\u2193\\nExpose via /api/activity/states\\n    \\u2193\\nFrontend Components Render\\n    - AgentTasksSection\\n    - ActivityFeed\\n```\\n\\n## E. API Endpoint Design\\n\\n### GET /api/activity/states\\n- **Response Structure**:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent_states\\": {\\n    \\"agent_id\\": {\\n      \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n      \\"summary\\": \\"Two-sentence description of work\\",\\n      \\"deliverables\\": [\\"path/to/file1\\", \\"path/to/file2\\"],\\n      \\"timestamp\\": \\"ISO8601 timestamp\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## F. State Management Strategy\\n- Use React Context for lightweight state management\\n- Backend maintains immutable state dictionaries\\n- Implement optimistic updates for responsive UI\\n\\n## G. Deployment Considerations\\n- Zero-downtime deployment\\n- Feature flag for gradual rollout\\n- Backward compatibility with existing UI\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend Tests\\n- Snapshot testing for AgentTasksSection\\n- Interaction tests for summary expansion\\n- State rendering tests\\n\\n### Backend Tests\\n- Unit tests for ActivityTracker\\n- Integration tests for state persistence\\n- API endpoint validation\\n\\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Performance Overhead\\n- **Mitigation**: Implement lazy loading, limit summary length\\n  \\n### Risk 2: Incomplete Agent Outputs\\n- **Mitigation**: Graceful fallback to default messages\\n\\n## J. Alternative Approaches Considered\\n1. Modal-based summaries (rejected - too intrusive)\\n2. Separate summary page (rejected - requires extra navigation)\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n- How verbose should default summaries be?\\n- Should we implement a \\"show more\\" mechanism for longer summaries?\\n\\n## Architectural Decision Record\\n\\n### Key Decisions\\n1. Surface summaries directly in existing components\\n2. Minimal changes to existing architecture\\n3. Leverage current state management infrastructure\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Implementation Priority**: HIGH\\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium (2-3 sprint points)\\n**Potential User Impact**: Significant improvement in task comprehension"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN 