{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:05:41", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a6e50da0-5c35-43e8-b625-ffff72a1d513', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0197eZEtHcmqYVHrs9zTTg26', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Favorite Tacos Achievements System', 'description': 'Implement requirements for favorite tacos achievements system as documented in requirements.md file'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0197eZEtHcmqYVHrs9zTTg26', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "6e97bd3f", "message": "Created project: Favorite Tacos Achievements System", "summary": {"project_id": "6e97bd3f", "project_name": "Favorite Tacos Achievements System", "description": "Implement requirements for favorite tacos achievements system as documented in requirements.md file", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:05:33.157900", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:05:33.157900", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:05:33.157900", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Favorite Tacos Achievements System\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Jrcx3coPt1R5rLsanFWj8F', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Jrcx3coPt1R5rLsanFWj8F', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Favorite Tacos Achievements - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Favorite Tacos Achievements  \\n**Project ID:** 979fbaa1  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-15  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating achievement expansion\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the \\"Favorite Tacos\\" category to the existing ensemble agent achievements system. These achievements should be humorous, food-themed, and integrate seamlessly with the current achievement structure.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definition**: Create 10 new achievements themed around \\"Favorite Tacos\\" that are:\\n   - Humorous and entertaining\\n   - Themed around taco varieties, preparation, and enjoyment\\n   - Applicable to different agent classes\\n   - Consistent with existing achievement structure\\n\\n2. **System Integration**: Ensure new achievements:\\n   - Follow existing JSON schema format\\n   - Integrate with current achievement tracking system\\n   - Are properly categorized and triggered\\n   - Display correctly in the UI\\n\\n3. **Achievement Implementation**: \\n   - Add achievements to the existing achievement definition storage\\n   - Ensure trigger conditions are properly configured\\n   - Verify achievement icons and descriptions are appropriate\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content - 10 Favorite Tacos Achievements:**\\n\\n1. **\\"Al Pastor Perfectionist\\"**\\n   - Description: Executed 25 tasks with perfect timing and spice\\n   - Target: Code Writer, System Architect\\n   - Trigger: Complete 25 tasks with 100% success rate\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd50\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n2. **\\"Carnitas Coordinator\\"** \\n   - Description: Orchestrated a complex multi-agent task like slow-cooking perfection\\n   - Target: Development Manager, Executive Director\\n   - Trigger: Successfully coordinate 5+ agents in a single task\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc65\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n3. **\\"Fish Taco Fusion\\"**\\n   - Description: Seamlessly blended different technologies like coastal fusion cuisine\\n   - Target: System Architect, Code Writer\\n   - Trigger: Successfully integrate 3+ different tech stacks\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc1f\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n4. **\\"Breakfast Burrito Bootstrap\\"**\\n   - Description: Got the whole system up and running before the coffee kicked in\\n   - Target: Executive Director, Development Manager\\n   - Trigger: Complete a full project setup in under 10 minutes\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2f\\u2615\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n5. **\\"Crunchy Shell Stability\\"**\\n   - Description: Maintained system integrity despite multiple layers and pressure\\n   - Target: Bug Fixer, Code Tester\\n   - Trigger: Fix 10 bugs without introducing new ones\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcaa\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n6. **\\"Soft Shell Flexibility\\"**\\n   - Description: Adapted gracefully to changing requirements mid-task\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully pivot task approach based on user feedback\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83e\\udd38\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n7. **\\"Salsa Verde Validator\\"**\\n   - Description: Added that perfect tang to ensure quality standards\\n   - Target: Code Tester, Bug Fixer\\n   - Trigger: Achieve 95%+ test coverage on 5 projects\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\u2705\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n8. **\\"Hot Sauce Hero\\"**\\n   - Description: Brought the heat when things got challenging\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully recover from 3 failed executions in a row\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd25\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n9. **\\"Taco Tuesday Tradition\\"**\\n   - Description: Consistently delivered quality every single week\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Complete tasks successfully for 7 consecutive days\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcc5\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n10. **\\"Supreme Combination\\"**\\n    - Description: Loaded with everything - the ultimate multi-tool achievement\\n    - Target: Executive Director\\n    - Trigger: Use 10+ different tools in a single task execution\\n    - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83c\\udf1f\\n    - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changing the achievement system architecture\\n- Creating new achievement categories beyond \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n- UI changes beyond standard achievement display\\n- Achievement leaderboards or social features\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration**: Must work with existing:\\n   - Achievement tracking system (`/api/achievements` endpoints)\\n   - Backend achievement storage (JSON format)\\n   - Frontend achievement display components\\n   - Activity tracker for trigger detection\\n\\n2. **Format Compliance**: Follow existing schema:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"id\\": \\"achievement_id\\",\\n     \\"name\\": \\"Achievement Name\\", \\n     \\"description\\": \\"Achievement description\\",\\n     \\"agent_class\\": \\"target_agent_class\\",\\n     \\"category\\": \\"favorite_tacos\\",\\n     \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n     \\"trigger\\": {\\n       \\"event_type\\": \\"trigger_condition\\",\\n       \\"criteria\\": \\"specific_requirements\\"\\n     },\\n     \\"icon\\": \\"emoji_icon\\",\\n     \\"points\\": 10\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Storage**: Add to existing achievement definition files/database without disrupting current achievements\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 10 new achievements properly defined with \\"favorite_tacos\\" category\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions work correctly\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements display in UI with proper icons and descriptions\\n\\n2. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are humorous and taco-themed\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements span different agent classes appropriately\\n   - \\u2705 Difficulty levels are balanced (mix of common/rare/epic achievements)\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions are achievable but meaningful\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing achievement system\\n   - \\u2705 Proper JSON schema compliance\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement notifications work for new achievements\\n   - \\u2705 Data persists correctly\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Existing System**: Current achievement system is functional and can accept new achievements\\n2. **Schema Stability**: Existing achievement JSON schema will accommodate new entries\\n3. **Category Support**: System supports arbitrary category names like \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n4. **Icon Support**: Emoji icons are supported in the current UI\\n5. **Trigger Flexibility**: System can handle various trigger conditions for new achievements\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n1. **Analysis Phase**: Examine existing achievement definitions and storage structure\\n2. **Design Phase**: Create 10 achievement definitions following existing patterns\\n3. **Integration Phase**: Add achievements to the system storage\\n4. **Validation Phase**: Test that achievements trigger and display correctly\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Development Manager  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager to implement the favorite tacos achievements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WJXjorcLQkKoxbWWanbzwC', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '6e97bd3f', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements analyzed: 10 favorite tacos achievements to implement with humorous taco-themed content, integrating with existing achievement system. All specifications clearly documented.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WJXjorcLQkKoxbWWanbzwC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 75.7%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Conducting systematic directory analysis using multiple commands to gather comprehensive data, 3) Creat...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for d