licable to different agent classes\\n   - Consistent with existing achievement structure\\n\\n2. **System Integration**: Ensure new achievements:\\n   - Follow existing JSON schema format\\n   - Integrate with current achievement tracking system\\n   - Are properly categorized and triggered\\n   - Display correctly in the UI\\n\\n3. **Achievement Implementation**: \\n   - Add achievements to the existing achievement definition storage\\n   - Ensure trigger conditions are properly configured\\n   - Verify achievement icons and descriptions are appropriate\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content - 10 Favorite Tacos Achievements:**\\n\\n1. **\\"Al Pastor Perfectionist\\"**\\n   - Description: Executed 25 tasks with perfect timing and spice\\n   - Target: Code Writer, System Architect\\n   - Trigger: Complete 25 tasks with 100% success rate\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd50\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n2. **\\"Carnitas Coordinator\\"** \\n   - Description: Orchestrated a complex multi-agent task like slow-cooking perfection\\n   - Target: Development Manager, Executive Director\\n   - Trigger: Successfully coordinate 5+ agents in a single task\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc65\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n3. **\\"Fish Taco Fusion\\"**\\n   - Description: Seamlessly blended different technologies like coastal fusion cuisine\\n   - Target: System Architect, Code Writer\\n   - Trigger: Successfully integrate 3+ different tech stacks\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc1f\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n4. **\\"Breakfast Burrito Bootstrap\\"**\\n   - Description: Got the whole system up and running before the coffee kicked in\\n   - Target: Executive Director, Development Manager\\n   - Trigger: Complete a full project setup in under 10 minutes\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2f\\u2615\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n5. **\\"Crunchy Shell Stability\\"**\\n   - Description: Maintained system integrity despite multiple layers and pressure\\n   - Target: Bug Fixer, Code Tester\\n   - Trigger: Fix 10 bugs without introducing new ones\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcaa\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n6. **\\"Soft Shell Flexibility\\"**\\n   - Description: Adapted gracefully to changing requirements mid-task\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully pivot task approach based on user feedback\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83e\\udd38\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n7. **\\"Salsa Verde Validator\\"**\\n   - Description: Added that perfect tang to ensure quality standards\\n   - Target: Code Tester, Bug Fixer\\n   - Trigger: Achieve 95%+ test coverage on 5 projects\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\u2705\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n8. **\\"Hot Sauce Hero\\"**\\n   - Description: Brought the heat when things got challenging\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully recover from 3 failed executions in a row\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd25\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n9. **\\"Taco Tuesday Tradition\\"**\\n   - Description: Consistently delivered quality every single week\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Complete tasks successfully for 7 consecutive days\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcc5\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n10. **\\"Supreme Combination\\"**\\n    - Description: Loaded with everything - the ultimate multi-tool achievement\\n    - Target: Executive Director\\n    - Trigger: Use 10+ different tools in a single task execution\\n    - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83c\\udf1f\\n    - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changing the achievement system architecture\\n- Creating new achievement categories beyond \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n- UI changes beyond standard achievement display\\n- Achievement leaderboards or social features\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration**: Must work with existing:\\n   - Achievement tracking system (`/api/achievements` endpoints)\\n   - Backend achievement storage (JSON format)\\n   - Frontend achievement display components\\n   - Activity tracker for trigger detection\\n\\n2. **Format Compliance**: Follow existing schema:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"id\\": \\"achievement_id\\",\\n     \\"name\\": \\"Achievement Name\\", \\n     \\"description\\": \\"Achievement description\\",\\n     \\"agent_class\\": \\"target_agent_class\\",\\n     \\"category\\": \\"favorite_tacos\\",\\n     \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n     \\"trigger\\": {\\n       \\"event_type\\": \\"trigger_condition\\",\\n       \\"criteria\\": \\"specific_requirements\\"\\n     },\\n     \\"icon\\": \\"emoji_icon\\",\\n     \\"points\\": 10\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Storage**: Add to existing achievement definition files/database without disrupting current achievements\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 10 new achievements properly defined with \\"favorite_tacos\\" category\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions work correctly\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements display in UI with proper icons and descriptions\\n\\n2. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are humorous and taco-themed\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements span different agent classes appropriately\\n   - \\u2705 Difficulty levels are balanced (mix of common/rare/epic achievements)\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions are achievable but meaningful\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing achievement system\\n   - \\u2705 Proper JSON schema compliance\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement notifications work for new achievements\\n   - \\u2705 Data persists correctly\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Existing System**: Current achievement system is functional and can accept new achievements\\n2. **Schema Stability**: Existing achievement JSON schema will accommodate new entries\\n3. **Category Support**: System supports arbitrary category names like \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n4. **Icon Support**: Emoji icons are supported in the current UI\\n5. **Trigger Flexibility**: System can handle various trigger conditions for new achievements\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n1. **Analysis Phase**: Examine existing achievement definitions and storage structure\\n2. **Design Phase**: Create 10 achievement definitions following existing patterns\\n3. **Integration Phase**: Add achievements to the system storage\\n4. **Validation Phase**: Test that achievements trigger and display correctly\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Development Manager  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager to implement the favorite tacos achievements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R1fvJ1WjmrFUQQCYZqC4bo', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Favorite Tacos Achievements - Milestone Plan\n\n## Milestone 1: Achievement Design and Integration\n**Objective**: Define and integrate 10 new "Favorite Tacos" achievements\n**Deliverables**:\n- Achievement JSON definitions\n- Integration with existing achievement system\n- Preliminary testing of achievement triggers\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- 10 achievements created\n- Follows existing JSON schema\n- Compatible with current achievement tracking system\n\n## Milestone 2: Testing and Validation\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing of new achievements\n**Deliverables**:\n- Unit tests for achievement triggers\n- Integration tests with achievement system\n- UI display verification\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All achievements trigger correctly\n- Proper display in UI\n- No regressions in existing achievement system\n\n## Milestone 3: Documentation and Final Review\n**Objective**: Complete documentation and final system review\n**Deliverables**:\n- Updated system documentation\n- Achievement descriptions review\n- Final system sign-off\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Comprehensive documentation\n- All achievements meet humor and quality standards\n- Executive Director approval'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R1fvJ1WjmrFUQQCYZqC4bo', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_020559.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_020559.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01B5f4o83TahRjHBvcBgfTBD', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md', 'project_name': 'Favorite Tacos Achievements System', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01B5f4o83TahRjHBvcBgfTBD', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your 