{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:06:37", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-59ab5165-7cd1-4637-8815-54933b476394', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md",\n  "project_name": "Favorite Tacos Achievements System",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KfUFQxgYSkBWcNPXzEScM3', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KfUFQxgYSkBWcNPXzEScM3', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Favorite Tacos Achievements - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Favorite Tacos Achievements  \\n**Project ID:** 979fbaa1  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-15  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating achievement expansion\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the \\"Favorite Tacos\\" category to the existing ensemble agent achievements system. These achievements should be humorous, food-themed, and integrate seamlessly with the current achievement structure.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definition**: Create 10 new achievements themed around \\"Favorite Tacos\\" that are:\\n   - Humorous and entertaining\\n   - Themed around taco varieties, preparation, and enjoyment\\n   - Applicable to different agent classes\\n   - Consistent with existing achievement structure\\n\\n2. **System Integration**: Ensure new achievements:\\n   - Follow existing JSON schema format\\n   - Integrate with current achievement tracking system\\n   - Are properly categorized and triggered\\n   - Display correctly in the UI\\n\\n3. **Achievement Implementation**: \\n   - Add achievements to the existing achievement definition storage\\n   - Ensure trigger conditions are properly configured\\n   - Verify achievement icons and descriptions are appropriate\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content - 10 Favorite Tacos Achievements:**\\n\\n1. **\\"Al Pastor Perfectionist\\"**\\n   - Description: Executed 25 tasks with perfect timing and spice\\n   - Target: Code Writer, System Architect\\n   - Trigger: Complete 25 tasks with 100% success rate\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd50\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n2. **\\"Carnitas Coordinator\\"** \\n   - Description: Orchestrated a complex multi-agent task like slow-cooking perfection\\n   - Target: Development Manager, Executive Director\\n   - Trigger: Successfully coordinate 5+ agents in a single task\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc65\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n3. **\\"Fish Taco Fusion\\"**\\n   - Description: Seamlessly blended different technologies like coastal fusion cuisine\\n   - Target: System Architect, Code Writer\\n   - Trigger: Successfully integrate 3+ different tech stacks\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc1f\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n4. **\\"Breakfast Burrito Bootstrap\\"**\\n   - Description: Got the whole system up and running before the coffee kicked in\\n   - Target: Executive Director, Development Manager\\n   - Trigger: Complete a full project setup in under 10 minutes\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2f\\u2615\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n5. **\\"Crunchy Shell Stability\\"**\\n   - Description: Maintained system integrity despite multiple layers and pressure\\n   - Target: Bug Fixer, Code Tester\\n   - Trigger: Fix 10 bugs without introducing new ones\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcaa\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n6. **\\"Soft Shell Flexibility\\"**\\n   - Description: Adapted gracefully to changing requirements mid-task\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully pivot task approach based on user feedback\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83e\\udd38\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n7. **\\"Salsa Verde Validator\\"**\\n   - Description: Added that perfect tang to ensure quality standards\\n   - Target: Code Tester, Bug Fixer\\n   - Trigger: Achieve 95%+ test coverage on 5 projects\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\u2705\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n8. **\\"Hot Sauce Hero\\"**\\n   - Description: Brought the heat when things got challenging\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully recover from 3 failed executions in a row\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd25\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n9. **\\"Taco Tuesday Tradition\\"**\\n   - Description: Consistently delivered quality every single week\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Complete tasks successfully for 7 consecutive days\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcc5\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n10. **\\"Supreme Combination\\"**\\n    - Description: Loaded with everything - the ultimate multi-tool achievement\\n    - Target: Executive Director\\n    - Trigger: Use 10+ different tools in a single task execution\\n    - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83c\\udf1f\\n    - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changing the achievement system architecture\\n- Creating new achievement categories beyond \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n- UI changes beyond standard achievement display\\n- Achievement leaderboards or social features\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration**: Must work with existing:\\n   - Achievement tracking system (`/api/achievements` endpoints)\\n   - Backend achievement storage (JSON format)\\n   - Frontend achievement display components\\n   - Activity tracker for trigger detection\\n\\n2. **Format Compliance**: Follow existing schema:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"id\\": \\"achievement_id\\",\\n     \\"name\\": \\"Achievement Name\\", \\n     \\"description\\": \\"Achievement description\\",\\n     \\"agent_class\\": \\"target_agent_class\\",\\n     \\"category\\": \\"favorite_tacos\\",\\n     \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n     \\"trigger\\": {\\n       \\"event_type\\": \\"trigger_condition\\",\\n       \\"criteria\\": \\"specific_requirements\\"\\n     },\\n     \\"icon\\": \\"emoji_icon\\",\\n     \\"points\\": 10\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Storage**: Add to existing achievement definition files/database without disrupting current achievements\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 10 new achievements properly defined with \\"favorite_tacos\\" category\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions work correctly\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements display in UI with proper icons and descriptions\\n\\n2. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are humorous and taco-themed\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements span different agent classes appropriately\\n   - \\u2705 Difficulty levels are balanced (mix of common/rare/epic achievements)\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions are achievable but meaningful\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing achievement system\\n   - \\u2705 Proper JSON schema compliance\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement notifications work for new achievements\\n   - \\u2705 Data persists correctly\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Existing System**: Current achievement system is functional and can accept new achievements\\n2. **Schema Stability**: Existing achievement JSON schema will accommodate new entries\\n3. **Category Support**: System supports arbitrary category names like \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n4. **Icon Support**: Emoji icons are supported in the current UI\\n5. **Trigger Flexibility**: System can handle various trigger conditions for new achievements\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n1. **Analysis Phase**: Examine existing achievement definitions and storage structure\\n2. **Design Phase**: Create 10 achievement definitions following existing patterns\\n3. **Integration Phase**: Add achievements to the system storage\\n4. **Validation Phase**: Test that achievements trigger and display correctly\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Development Manager  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager to implement the favorite tacos achievements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QHizex1EuWZViGZJKqEJwx', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Favorite Tacos Achievements System - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A) Architecture Overview\n\n### High-Level Design\nThe Favorite Tacos Achievements System will be an extension of the existing achievements framework, focusing on seamlessly integrating 10 new taco-themed achievements with minimal system disruption. We\'ll use a modular, extensible approach that maintains the current system\'s architecture while allowing easy addition of new achievements.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n- **Pattern**: Modular Extension of Existing System\n- **Style**: Plugin/Extension Architecture\n- **Key Principle**: Minimize changes to existing infrastructure\n\n## B) Tech Stack\n\n### Existing System Components (to be preserved)\n- **Frontend**: React-based UI with achievement display components\n- **Backend**: Python-based API with JSON-driven achievement tracking\n- **Storage**: JSON-based achievement definition storage\n\n### New Components\n- **Achievement Definitions**: JSON files with new taco-themed achievements\n- **Validation Layer**: Lightweight JSON schema validator for new achievements\n\n## C) System Components\n\n### 1. Achievement Definition Module\n- **Responsibility**: Store and manage new taco-themed achievements\n- **Location**: `/achievements/definitions/favorite_tacos.json`\n- **Key Features**:\n  - Follows existing JSON schema\n  - Supports 10 new achievements\n  - Includes metadata like trigger conditions, icons, and descriptions\n\n### 2. Trigger Validation Service\n- **Responsibility**: Validate and track achievement triggers\n- **Implementation**: Extension of existing trigger detection logic\n- **Key Features**:\n  - Supports new trigger conditions (e.g., task completion, multi-agent coordination)\n  - Compatible with existing achievement tracking mechanism\n\n### 3. UI Integration Layer\n- **Responsibility**: Display new achievements consistently with existing UI\n- **Implementation**: Update existing React components to support new category\n- **Key Features**:\n  - Emoji icon support\n  - Consistent styling with existing achievements\n  - Category-based filtering\n\n## D) File/Directory Structure\n\n```\n/ensemble_achievements/\n│\n├── achievements/\n│   ├── definitions/\n│   │   ├── existing_achievements.json\n│   │   └── favorite_tacos.json     # NEW: Taco achievements\n│   │\n│   └── schemas/\n│       └── achievement_schema.json\n│\n├── services/\n│   └── trigger_validator.py\n│\n└── ui/\n    └── components/\n        └── AchievementDisplay.jsx\n```\n\n## E) Data Model\n\n### Achievement JSON Schema\n```json\n{\n  "id": "unique_achievement_id",\n  "name": "Achievement Name",\n  "description": "Humorous description",\n  "agent_class": ["target", "agent", "classes"],\n  "category": "favorite_tacos",\n  "rarity": "common|rare|epic|legendary",\n  "trigger": {\n    "event_type": "task_completion|coordination|integration",\n    "criteria": "specific_requirements"\n  },\n  "icon": "🌮 emoji_icon",\n  "points": 10\n}\n```\n\n## F) API Design\n\nNo new API endpoints required. System will use existing:\n- `/api/achievements/list`\n- `/api/achievements/trigger`\n- `/api/achievements/user`\n\n## G) Deployment Strategy\n\n### Deployment Approach\n- **Method**: Incremental update to existing achievement system\n- **Deployment Steps**:\n  1. Add new JSON definition file\n  2. Update trigger validation service\n  3. Deploy updated components\n  4. Validate achievement tracking\n\n### Environments\n- **Development**: Local testing with mock achievements\n- **Staging**: Full system integration testing\n- **Production**: Gradual rollout with feature flag\n\n## H) Testing Strategy\n\n### Validation Checklist\n- ✅ JSON schema validation\n- ✅ Trigger condition testing\n- ✅ UI rendering verification\n- ✅ Performance impact assessment\n\n### Test Coverage\n- **Unit Tests**: 95%+ coverage for new components\n- **Integration Tests**: Verify system-wide compatibility\n- **Edge Case Testing**: Unusual trigger scenarios\n\n## I) Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: Separate Achievement System\n- **Pros**: Complete isolation\n- **Cons**: Increased complexity, duplication of infrastructure\n- **Decision**: Rejected in favor of extension model\n\n### Alternative 2: Hardcoded Achievements\n- **Pros**: Simplest implementation\n- **Cons**: Lacks flexibility, harder to maintain\n- **Decision**: Rejected due to maintainability concerns\n\n## J) Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: Trigger Detection Failures\n- **Mitigation**: Comprehensive testing, gradual rollout\n- **Monitoring**: Log and alert on unexpected trigger behaviors\n\n### Risk 2: UI Compatibility Issues\n- **Mitigation**: Thorough cross-browser and responsive design testing\n- **Fallback**: Graceful degradation if rendering fails\n\n## K) Open Questions\n\n1. Performance impact of new achievements?\n2. User engagement with taco-themed achievements?\n3. Potential for future themed achievement expansions?\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe proposed architecture provides a lightweight, minimally invasive approach to adding taco-themed achievements to the existing system. By following the established patterns and maintaining strict compatibility, we ensure a smooth integration with low risk and high potential for user enjoyment.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QHizex1EuWZViGZJKqEJwx', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_020637.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_020637.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the project requirements by providing a robust, scalable solution that balances technical complexity with maintainability. By carefully selecting techn...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
