{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:07:27", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-799f751d-467c-461c-bac0-38b768033074', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Design and implement 10 new taco-themed achievements",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017yXTs7xCjZ6Sqpug1tmmpW', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017yXTs7xCjZ6Sqpug1tmmpW', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Favorite Tacos Achievements System - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A) Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level Design\\nThe Favorite Tacos Achievements System will be an extension of the existing achievements framework, focusing on seamlessly integrating 10 new taco-themed achievements with minimal system disruption. We\'ll use a modular, extensible approach that maintains the current system\'s architecture while allowing easy addition of new achievements.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Pattern**: Modular Extension of Existing System\\n- **Style**: Plugin/Extension Architecture\\n- **Key Principle**: Minimize changes to existing infrastructure\\n\\n## B) Tech Stack\\n\\n### Existing System Components (to be preserved)\\n- **Frontend**: React-based UI with achievement display components\\n- **Backend**: Python-based API with JSON-driven achievement tracking\\n- **Storage**: JSON-based achievement definition storage\\n\\n### New Components\\n- **Achievement Definitions**: JSON files with new taco-themed achievements\\n- **Validation Layer**: Lightweight JSON schema validator for new achievements\\n\\n## C) System Components\\n\\n### 1. Achievement Definition Module\\n- **Responsibility**: Store and manage new taco-themed achievements\\n- **Location**: `/achievements/definitions/favorite_tacos.json`\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Follows existing JSON schema\\n  - Supports 10 new achievements\\n  - Includes metadata like trigger conditions, icons, and descriptions\\n\\n### 2. Trigger Validation Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Validate and track achievement triggers\\n- **Implementation**: Extension of existing trigger detection logic\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Supports new trigger conditions (e.g., task completion, multi-agent coordination)\\n  - Compatible with existing achievement tracking mechanism\\n\\n### 3. UI Integration Layer\\n- **Responsibility**: Display new achievements consistently with existing UI\\n- **Implementation**: Update existing React components to support new category\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Emoji icon support\\n  - Consistent styling with existing achievements\\n  - Category-based filtering\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\n/ensemble_achievements/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 achievements/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 definitions/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 existing_achievements.json\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 favorite_tacos.json     # NEW: Taco achievements\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 schemas/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievement_schema.json\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 trigger_validator.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ui/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementDisplay.jsx\\n```\\n\\n## E) Data Model\\n\\n### Achievement JSON Schema\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"id\\": \\"unique_achievement_id\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"Achievement Name\\",\\n  \\"description\\": \\"Humorous description\\",\\n  \\"agent_class\\": [\\"target\\", \\"agent\\", \\"classes\\"],\\n  \\"category\\": \\"favorite_tacos\\",\\n  \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n  \\"trigger\\": {\\n    \\"event_type\\": \\"task_completion|coordination|integration\\",\\n    \\"criteria\\": \\"specific_requirements\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"icon\\": \\"\\ud83c\\udf2e emoji_icon\\",\\n  \\"points\\": 10\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## F) API Design\\n\\nNo new API endpoints required. System will use existing:\\n- `/api/achievements/list`\\n- `/api/achievements/trigger`\\n- `/api/achievements/user`\\n\\n## G) Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Deployment Approach\\n- **Method**: Incremental update to existing achievement system\\n- **Deployment Steps**:\\n  1. Add new JSON definition file\\n  2. Update trigger validation service\\n  3. Deploy updated components\\n  4. Validate achievement tracking\\n\\n### Environments\\n- **Development**: Local testing with mock achievements\\n- **Staging**: Full system integration testing\\n- **Production**: Gradual rollout with feature flag\\n\\n## H) Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Validation Checklist\\n- \\u2705 JSON schema validation\\n- \\u2705 Trigger condition testing\\n- \\u2705 UI rendering verification\\n- \\u2705 Performance impact assessment\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n- **Unit Tests**: 95%+ coverage for new components\\n- **Integration Tests**: Verify system-wide compatibility\\n- **Edge Case Testing**: Unusual trigger scenarios\\n\\n## I) Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Separate Achievement System\\n- **Pros**: Complete isolation\\n- **Cons**: Increased complexity, duplication of infrastructure\\n- **Decision**: Rejected in favor of extension model\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Hardcoded Achievements\\n- **Pros**: Simplest implementation\\n- **Cons**: Lacks flexibility, harder to maintain\\n- **Decision**: Rejected due to maintainability concerns\\n\\n## J) Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Trigger Detection Failures\\n- **Mitigation**: Comprehensive testing, gradual rollout\\n- **Monitoring**: Log and alert on unexpected trigger behaviors\\n\\n### Risk 2: UI Compatibility Issues\\n- **Mitigation**: Thorough cross-browser and responsive design testing\\n- **Fallback**: Graceful degradation if rendering fails\\n\\n## K) Open Questions\\n\\n1. Performance impact of new achievements?\\n2. User engagement with taco-themed achievements?\\n3. Potential for future themed achievement expansions?\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThe proposed architecture provides a lightweight, minimally invasive approach to adding taco-themed achievements to the existing system. By following the established patterns and maintaining strict compatibility, we ensure a smooth integration with low risk and high potential for user enjoyment."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MHde6645yPtvmDo96FPgEb', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MHde6645yPtvmDo96FPgEb', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Favorite Tacos Achievements - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Favorite Tacos Achievements  \\n**Project ID:** 979fbaa1  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-15  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating achievement expansion\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the \\"Favorite Tacos\\" category to the existing ensemble agent achievements system. These achievements should be humorous, food-themed, and integrate seamlessly with the current achievement structure.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definition**: Create 10 new achievements themed around \\"Favorite Tacos\\" that are:\\n   - Humorous and entertaining\\n   - Themed around taco varieties, preparation, and enjoyment\\n   - Applicable to different agent classes\\n   - Consistent with existing achievement structure\\n\\n2. **System Integration**: Ensure new achievements:\\n   - Follow existing JSON schema format\\n   - Integrate with current achievement tracking system\\n   - Are properly categorized and triggered\\n   - Display correctly in the UI\\n\\n3. **Achievement Implementation**: \\n   - Add achievements to the existing achievement definition storage\\n   - Ensure trigger conditions are properly configured\\n   - Verify achievement icons and descriptions are appropriate\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content - 10 Favorite Tacos Achievements:**\\n\\n1. **\\"Al Pastor Perfectionist\\"**\\n   - Description: Executed 25 tasks with perfect timing and spice\\n   - Target: Code Writer, System Architect\\n   - Trigger: Complete 25 tasks with 100% success rate\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd50\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n2. **\\"Carnitas Coordinator\\"** \\n   - Description: Orchestrated a complex multi-agent task like slow-cooking perfection\\n   - Target: Development Manager, Executive Director\\n   - Trigger: Successfully coordinate 5+ agents in a single task\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc65\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n3. **\\"Fish Taco Fusion\\"**\\n   - Description: Seamlessly blended different technologies like coastal fusion cuisine\\n   - Target: System Architect, Code Writer\\n   - Trigger: Successfully integrate 3+ different tech stacks\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc1f\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n4. **\\"Breakfast Burrito Bootstrap\\"**\\n   - Description: Got the whole system up and running before the coffee kicked in\\n   - Target: Executive Director, Development Manager\\n   - Trigger: Complete a full project setup in under 10 minutes\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2f\\u2615\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n5. **\\"Crunchy Shell Stability\\"**\\n   - Description: Maintained system integrity despite multiple layers and pressure\\n   - Target: Bug Fixer, Code Tester\\n   - Trigger: Fix 10 bugs without introducing new ones\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcaa\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n6. **\\"Soft Shell Flexibility\\"**\\n   - Description: Adapted gracefully to changing requirements mid-task\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully pivot task approach based on user feedback\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83e\\udd38\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n7. **\\"Salsa Verde Validator\\"**\\n   - Description: Added that perfect tang to ensure quality standards\\n   - Target: Code Tester, Bug Fixer\\n   - Trigger: Achieve 95%+ test coverage on 5 projects\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\u2705\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n8. **\\"Hot Sauce Hero\\"**\\n   - Description: Brought the heat when things got challenging\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully recover from 3 failed executions in a row\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd25\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n9. **\\"Taco Tuesday Tradition\\"**\\n   - Description: Consistently delivered quality every single week\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Complete tasks successfully for 7 consecutive days\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcc5\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n10. **\\"Supreme Combination\\"**\\n    - Description: Loaded with everything - the ultimate multi-tool achievement\\n    - Target: Executive Director\\n    - Trigger: Use 10+ different tools in a single task execution\\n    - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83c\\udf1f\\n    - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changing the achievement system architecture\\n- Creating new achievement categories beyond \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n- UI changes beyond standard achievement display\\n- Achievement leaderboards or social features\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration**: Must work with existing:\\n   - Achievement tracking system (`/api/achievements` endpoints)\\n   - Backend achievement storage (JSON format)\\n   - Frontend achievement display components\\n   - Activity tracker for trigger detection\\n\\n2. **Format Compliance**: Follow existing schema:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"id\\": \\"achievement_id\\",\\n     \\"name\\": \\"Achievement Name\\", \\n     \\"description\\": \\"Achievement description\\",\\n     \\"agent_class\\": \\"target_agent_class\\",\\n     \\"category\\": \\"favorite_tacos\\",\\n     \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n     \\"trigger\\": {\\n       \\"event_type\\": \\"trigger_condition\\",\\n       \\"criteria\\": \\"specific_requirements\\"\\n     },\\n     \\"icon\\": \\"emoji_icon\\",\\n     \\"points\\": 10\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Storage**: Add to existing achievement definition files/database without disrupting current achievements\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 10 new achievements properly defined with \\"favorite_tacos\\" category\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions work correctly\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements display in UI with proper icons and descriptions\\n\\n2. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are humorous and taco-themed\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements span different agent classes appropriately\\n   - \\u2705 Difficulty levels are balanced (mix of common/rare/epic achievements)\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions are achievable but meaningful\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing achievement system\\n   - \\u2705 Proper JSON schema compliance\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement notifications work for new achievements\\n   - \\u2705 Data persists correctly\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Existing System**: Current achievement system is functional and can accept new achievements\\n2. **Schema Stability**: Existing achievement JSON schema will accommodate new entries\\n3. **Category Support**: System supports arbitrary category names like \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n4. **Icon Support**: Emoji icons are supported in the current UI\\n5. **Trigger Flexibility**: System can handle various trigger conditions for new achievements\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n1. **Analysis Phase**: Examine existing achievement definitions and storage structure\\n2. **Design Phase**: Create 10 achievement definitions following existing patterns\\n3. **Integration Phase**: Add achievements to the system storage\\n4. **Validation Phase**: Test that achievements trigger and display correctly\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Development Manager  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager to implement the favorite tacos achievements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01U46orUfum3ctALWbrN6G9R', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Favorite Tacos Achievements\n\n## Overview\nImplementation of 10 new taco-themed achievements integrating with existing achievement system. Tasks focus on backend data models, API extensions, validation, and trigger logic.\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### 1. Achievement Schema Validation\n**Description**: Validate existing JSON achievement schema can accommodate new taco achievements\n**Acceptance Criteria**: \n- Schema supports "favorite_tacos" category\n- Schema accommodates emoji icons\n- Schema supports complex trigger conditions\n- Validation passes for all 10 new achievements\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 2. Achievement Definition Storage\n**Description**: Create `/achievements/definitions/favorite_tacos.json` with 10 taco achievements\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- JSON file contains all 10 achievements from requirements\n- Each achievement follows existing schema format\n- Proper agent class mappings (Code Writer, System Architect, etc.)\n- Correct trigger conditions and criteria\n- Emoji icons properly encoded\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 3. Trigger Validation Service Extension\n**Description**: Extend existing trigger detection to support new achievement conditions\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Supports "complete 25 tasks with 100% success rate" trigger\n- Supports "coordinate 5+ agents in single task" trigger  \n- Supports "integrate 3+ tech stacks" trigger\n- Supports "complete setup in under 10 minutes" trigger\n- Supports "fix 10 bugs without introducing new ones" trigger\n- Supports "pivot task approach based on feedback" trigger\n- Supports "achieve 95%+ test coverage on 5 projects" trigger\n- Supports "recover from 3 failed executions" trigger\n- Supports "complete tasks for 7 consecutive days" trigger\n- Supports "use 10+ tools in single task" trigger\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 4. Achievement Loading Service\n**Description**: Update achievement loading to include favorite_tacos.json file\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- System loads both existing and new achievement files\n- No conflicts between achievement IDs\n- Proper error handling if file missing/corrupted\n- Maintains existing achievement functionality\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 5. Category Filtering Support\n**Description**: Ensure API supports filtering achievements by "favorite_tacos" category\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- `/api/achievements/list?category=favorite_tacos` returns only taco achievements\n- Category filter works alongside existing filters\n- Maintains backward compatibility with existing API calls\n**Dependencies**: Task 4\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 6. Achievement Trigger API Enhancement\n**Description**: Update `/api/achievements/trigger` endpoint to handle new trigger types\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Endpoint accepts new trigger event types (task_completion, coordination, integration)\n- Proper validation of trigger criteria\n- Maintains existing trigger functionality\n- Returns appropriate responses for new achievement unlocks\n**Dependencies**: Task 3\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 7. Agent Class Validation\n**Description**: Validate achievement triggers respect agent class restrictions\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- "Al Pastor Perfectionist" only triggers for Code Writer, System Architect\n- "Carnitas Coordinator" only triggers for Development Manager, Executive Director\n- "Soft Shell Flexibility" triggers for all agent classes\n- Other achievements respect their specified agent class restrictions\n**Dependencies**: Task 3\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 8. Achievement Points System\n**Description**: Ensure point values are properly assigned and tracked for new achievements\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Each achievement awards correct point values\n- Points integrate with existing achievement scoring\n- User point totals update correctly when new achievements unlocked\n**Dependencies**: Task 6\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 9. Data Persistence Validation\n**Description**: Verify new achievements persist correctly in user achievement storage\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- User achievement records include new taco achievements\n- Achievement unlock timestamps saved correctly\n- Data persists across system restarts\n- No data corruption of existing achievements\n**Dependencies**: Task 8\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n### 10. Integration Testing Framework\n**Description**: Create comprehensive tests for new achievement system functionality\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Unit tests for each trigger condition\n- Integration tests for achievement loading\n- End-to-end tests for achievement unlock flow\n- Performance tests with full achievement set\n- 95%+ test coverage on new code\n**Dependencies**: All previous tasks\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Assigned To**: TDD Coordinator\n\n## Priority Order\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Tasks 1-4)\nEssential backend infrastructure for achievement loading and storage\n\n### Phase 2: Trigger Logic (Tasks 3, 6-7) \nCore achievement trigger detection and validation\n\n### Phase 3: Integration (Tasks 5, 8-9)\nAPI integration and data persistence\n\n### Phase 4: Validation (Task 10)\nComprehensive testing and quality assurance\n\n## Dependencies Map\n```\nTask 1 → Task 2 → Task 3 → Task 6 → Task 8 → Task 9\n       → Task 4 → Task 5                    ↓\n               → Task 7                      Task 10\n```\n\n## Estimated Timeline\n- **Phase 1**: 2-3 hours (foundation setup)\n- **Phase 2**: 4-5 hours (trigger logic implementation)  \n- **Phase 3**: 2-3 hours (integration and persistence)\n- **Phase 4**: 3-4 hours (comprehensive testing)\n- **Total**: 11-15 hours\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- Start with schema validation to catch incompatibilities early\n- Implement trigger detection incrementally with extensive testing\n- Maintain backward compatibility throughout implementation\n- Use feature flags for gradual rollout if needed'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01U46orUfum3ctALWbrN6G9R', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_020727.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_020727.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string'