{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:23:57", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-875404f1-2dfd-4c56-9fd7-60eeab1a4ae3', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/milestone_plan.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PZBonqozkE8UQW8KeA2DHb', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement', 'description': 'Implement agent cost tracking enhancement features as documented in milestone_plan.md using TDD methodology'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PZBonqozkE8UQW8KeA2DHb', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "b5140b8b", "message": "Created project: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement", "summary": {"project_id": "b5140b8b", "project_name": "Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement", "description": "Implement agent cost tracking enhancement features as documented in milestone_plan.md using TDD methodology", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:23:41.744090", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:23:41.744090", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:23:41.744090", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TRxA8xcTyztWovoTtVjGUA', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TRxA8xcTyztWovoTtVjGUA', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nEnhance the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task to provide better visibility into agent performance and resource usage.\\n\\n## Implementation Status: COMPLETE\\n**Completed**: 2026-01-15\\n**Implemented by**: Claude Opus 4.5 (manual implementation)\\n\\nAll core milestones (1-3) have been implemented. Milestone 4 (testing/docs) deferred for future work.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Backend Tracking Infrastructure - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Implement backend changes to capture and track agent execution metrics (cost, duration, model)\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Extended activity_tracker.py to capture new metrics (started_at, completed_at, duration_ms, model_used, cost_estimate)\\n2. Updated AgentRuntime to track start time and calculate costs\\n3. Cost calculation logic based on token usage and model pricing\\n4. Updated agent state data structures to include new fields\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- \\u2705 Activity tracker successfully records all new metrics for agent executions\\n- \\u2705 Cost estimates calculated accurately based on token usage and model pricing\\n- \\u2705 Execution duration captured in milliseconds\\n- \\u2705 Model identifier properly tracked from AgentRuntime\\n- \\u2705 Backend maintains backward compatibility with existing agent executions\\n- \\u2705 Unit tests pass for activity tracker and cost calculation\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None (starting milestone)\\n\\n**Estimated Scope**: Backend changes to activity_tracker.py, AgentRuntime metrics tracking\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: API and Data Flow Enhancement - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Update API endpoints to expose new metrics to frontend\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated API response structures in main.py to include new fields\\n2. WebSocket/polling endpoints return extended agent state data\\n3. API documentation updated with new fields\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- \\u2705 API endpoints return started_at, completed_at, duration_ms, model_used, cost_estimate\\n- \\u2705 Data format matches expected frontend structure\\n- \\u2705 Existing API consumers not broken by changes\\n- \\u2705 API integration tests pass\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (backend tracking must be implemented first)\\n\\n**Estimated Scope**: API endpoint updates in main.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Frontend Display Implementation - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Update UI to display new agent metrics in a user-friendly format\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Enhanced AgentSummaryPane.jsx component with new metric displays\\n2. Formatted cost display (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n3. Formatted duration display (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n4. Model tag/badge display with shortened model names\\n5. Execution timeline display (started \\u2192 completed)\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- \\u2705 Cost estimate displayed in readable format with $ prefix\\n- \\u2705 Duration shown in appropriate units (ms, seconds, minutes)\\n- \\u2705 Model tag displayed with shortened, readable name\\n- \\u2705 Execution timeline shows start and completion times\\n- \\u2705 UI remains compact and doesn\'t clutter the interface\\n- \\u2705 No performance degradation in UI rendering\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (API must provide data first)\\n\\n**Estimated Scope**: Frontend changes to AgentSummaryPane.jsx component\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Testing and Documentation - \\u23f3 DEFERRED\\n**Objective**: Ensure system reliability and provide documentation\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Comprehensive test suite for backend cost tracking\\n2. Integration tests for API data flow\\n3. Frontend component tests for display logic\\n4. User documentation for interpreting metrics\\n5. Developer documentation for maintenance\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- \\u2705 All unit tests pass (backend, API, frontend)\\n- \\u2705 Integration tests verify end-to-end data flow\\n- \\u2705 Code coverage meets project standards\\n- \\u2705 Documentation complete and accurate\\n- \\u2705 Manual testing confirms all success criteria met\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3 (requires all implementation complete)\\n\\n**Estimated Scope**: Testing and documentation across all components\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Success Criteria (Project Level)\\n\\n1. **Each completed agent shows**:\\n   - Start time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Completion time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n   - Cost estimate (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Model tag (e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\")\\n\\n2. **Data is captured reliably** from backend without errors\\n\\n3. **UI displays information** in a readable, compact format\\n\\n4. **No performance degradation** to existing functionality\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n\\n**Technical Risks**:\\n- Token usage data might not always be available from API responses\\n- Mitigation: Implement character-based estimation with \\"~\\" prefix for estimates\\n\\n**Integration Risks**:\\n- Changes might break existing activity tracker consumers\\n- Mitigation: Ensure backward compatibility, make new fields optional\\n\\n**Performance Risks**:\\n- Additional metrics might slow down agent execution tracking\\n- Mitigation: Keep calculations lightweight, use efficient data structures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation Order\\n\\n1. **Milestone 1** (Backend) - Foundation for all subsequent work\\n2. **Milestone 2** (API) - Enables frontend to access data\\n3. **Milestone 3** (Frontend) - User-facing implementation\\n4. **Milestone 4** (Testing/Docs) - Quality assurance and maintenance\\n\\nEach milestone must be completed and verified before proceeding to the next.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0185zkiautkmZ5rZaoBz2zpc', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'b5140b8b', 'category': 'decision', 'note': 'Requirements document found - milestone plan indicates implementation is COMPLETE. Milestones 1-3 already implemented, Milestone 4 (testing/docs) deferred. Need to verify current implementation status and determine if additional work needed.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0185zkiautkmZ5rZaoBz2zpc', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017MKe7LcnCB4jQGCDGkfkwm', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017MKe7LcnCB4jQGCDGkfkwm', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task. This will provide better visibility into agent performance and resource usage.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Display execution cost estimates for each agent in the agent summary\\n2. Show start time, completion time, and duration of execution\\n3. Tag each agent with the model it used during execution\\n4. Ensure data flows from backend tracking to frontend display\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n1. **Backend Enhancements**:\\n   - Capture start time, end time, and duration for agent executions\\n   - Track the model used by each agent (from AgentRuntime)\\n   - Calculate cost estimates based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Include this data in activity tracking and agent states\\n\\n2. **Frontend Enhancements**:\\n   - Display cost estimate in AgentSummaryPane component\\n   - Show execution duration (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Display model tag/badge for each agent\\n   - Format costs in a user-friendly way (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Format durations in appropriate units (ms, seconds, minutes)\\n\\n3. **Data Flow**:\\n   - Extend Activity Tracker to capture cost and model data\\n   - Update API endpoints to return this information\\n   - Update AgentSummaryPane to consume and display the data\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Historical cost aggregation/reporting (future feature)\\n- Budget alerts or limits (future feature)\\n- Per-tool cost breakdown (future feature)\\n- Real-time cost streaming during execution (will show on completion)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing activity_tracker.py system\\n- Should integrate with existing AgentRuntime metrics\\n- Frontend changes limited to AgentSummaryPane component\\n- Backend must be backward compatible with existing agent executions\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Each completed agent shows:\\n   - Start time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Completion time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n   - Cost estimate (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Model tag (e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\")\\n\\n2. \\u2705 Data is captured reliably from backend\\n3. \\u2705 UI displays information in a readable, compact format\\n4. \\u2705 No performance degradation to existing functionality\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. AgentRuntime already tracks token usage and model selection\\n2. Model pricing information is available (from model_selector.py or similar)\\n3. Activity tracker can be extended without breaking existing consumers\\n4. Frontend has access to activity data via WebSocket or polling\\n\\n## User Stories\\n1. **As a developer**, I want to see how much each agent execution costs so I can optimize expensive operations\\n2. **As a developer**, I want to see execution duration so I can identify slow agents\\n3. **As a developer**, I want to see which model was used so I can correlate performance with model choice\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Backend Changes\\n1. Extend `record_agent_completed()` in activity_tracker.py to accept:\\n   - `started_at`: ISO timestamp\\n   - `completed_at`: ISO timestamp  \\n   - `duration_ms`: milliseconds\\n   - `model_used`: model identifier\\n   - `cost_estimate`: float (USD)\\n\\n2. Update AgentRuntime to:\\n   - Track start time on initialization\\n   - Calculate cost based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Pass this data to activity tracker on completion\\n\\n3. Update API response in main.py to include these fields in agent state\\n\\n### Frontend Changes\\n1. Update AgentSummaryPane.jsx to:\\n   - Display execution timeline (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Show duration badge\\n   - Show cost estimate badge\\n   - Show model tag\\n   - Handle formatting for readability\\n\\n### Data Structure\\n```javascript\\n// Expected agent info structure\\n{\\n  agent_id: \\"exec_dir_1\\",\\n  type: \\"executive_director\\",\\n  status: \\"completed\\",\\n  started_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:00Z\\",\\n  completed_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:42Z\\",\\n  duration_ms: 42000,\\n  model_used: \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\",\\n  cost_estimate: 0.0042,\\n  // ... existing fields\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Cost calculation should use actual token counts from Claude API responses\\n- If token counts unavailable, estimate based on character counts with clear \\"~\\" prefix\\n- Duration should handle both running (show elapsed) and completed states\\n- Model tags should be shortened for display (e.g., \\"sonnet-3.5\\" instead of full name)\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RrE43AyLvkKiixasSYMBum', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'b5140b8b', 'category': 'decision', 'note': 'Requirements document confirms implementation is marked COMPLETE. However, user requests TDD implementation of all specified features. Need to assess if existing implementation meets TDD standards and requirements, or if additional work is needed.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RrE43AyLvkKiixasSYMBum', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KgK6ACe3pxCLbknBjzHxAX', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'b5140b8b', 'assigned_to': 'leadership/development_manager', 'description': 'Assess current implementation status of agent cost tracking enhancement and implement any missing features using TDD methodology. Milestone plan indicates implementation complete but user requests TDD implementation of all features.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KgK6ACe3pxCLbknBjzHxAX', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "1b6f4128", "message": "Added task: Assess current implementation status of agent cost tracking enhancement and implement any missing features using TDD methodology. Milestone plan indicates implementation complete but user requests TDD implementation of all features."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 75.7%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Conducting systematic directory analysis using multiple commands to gather comprehensive data, 3) Creat...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
