 and agent states\\n\\n2. **Frontend Enhancements**:\\n   - Display cost estimate in AgentSummaryPane component\\n   - Show execution duration (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Display model tag/badge for each agent\\n   - Format costs in a user-friendly way (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Format durations in appropriate units (ms, seconds, minutes)\\n\\n3. **Data Flow**:\\n   - Extend Activity Tracker to capture cost and model data\\n   - Update API endpoints to return this information\\n   - Update AgentSummaryPane to consume and display the data\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Historical cost aggregation/reporting (future feature)\\n- Budget alerts or limits (future feature)\\n- Per-tool cost breakdown (future feature)\\n- Real-time cost streaming during execution (will show on completion)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing activity_tracker.py system\\n- Should integrate with existing AgentRuntime metrics\\n- Frontend changes limited to AgentSummaryPane component\\n- Backend must be backward compatible with existing agent executions\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Each completed agent shows:\\n   - Start time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Completion time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n   - Cost estimate (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Model tag (e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\")\\n\\n2. \\u2705 Data is captured reliably from backend\\n3. \\u2705 UI displays information in a readable, compact format\\n4. \\u2705 No performance degradation to existing functionality\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. AgentRuntime already tracks token usage and model selection\\n2. Model pricing information is available (from model_selector.py or similar)\\n3. Activity tracker can be extended without breaking existing consumers\\n4. Frontend has access to activity data via WebSocket or polling\\n\\n## User Stories\\n1. **As a developer**, I want to see how much each agent execution costs so I can optimize expensive operations\\n2. **As a developer**, I want to see execution duration so I can identify slow agents\\n3. **As a developer**, I want to see which model was used so I can correlate performance with model choice\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Backend Changes\\n1. Extend `record_agent_completed()` in activity_tracker.py to accept:\\n   - `started_at`: ISO timestamp\\n   - `completed_at`: ISO timestamp  \\n   - `duration_ms`: milliseconds\\n   - `model_used`: model identifier\\n   - `cost_estimate`: float (USD)\\n\\n2. Update AgentRuntime to:\\n   - Track start time on initialization\\n   - Calculate cost based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Pass this data to activity tracker on completion\\n\\n3. Update API response in main.py to include these fields in agent state\\n\\n### Frontend Changes\\n1. Update AgentSummaryPane.jsx to:\\n   - Display execution timeline (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Show duration badge\\n   - Show cost estimate badge\\n   - Show model tag\\n   - Handle formatting for readability\\n\\n### Data Structure\\n```javascript\\n// Expected agent info structure\\n{\\n  agent_id: \\"exec_dir_1\\",\\n  type: \\"executive_director\\",\\n  status: \\"completed\\",\\n  started_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:00Z\\",\\n  completed_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:42Z\\",\\n  duration_ms: 42000,\\n  model_used: \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\",\\n  cost_estimate: 0.0042,\\n  // ... existing fields\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Cost calculation should use actual token counts from Claude API responses\\n- If token counts unavailable, estimate based on character counts with clear \\"~\\" prefix\\n- Duration should handle both running (show elapsed) and completed states\\n- Model tags should be shortened for display (e.g., \\"sonnet-3.5\\" instead of full name)\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MJRTZd43DCCXTVpNNxzDH9', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Design Pattern\n- **Architectural Style**: Layered Architecture with Event-Driven Updates\n- **Communication**: RESTful API + WebSocket for real-time updates\n- **Goal**: Extend existing agent tracking system with cost and performance metadata\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python (existing system)\n- **Web Framework**: FastAPI (for API endpoints)\n- **Database Integration**: SQLAlchemy (for activity tracking)\n- **Token Tracking**: Integrate with existing Claude API client\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React (existing system)\n- **State Management**: Context API or Redux (depending on complexity)\n- **Data Visualization**: Lightweight badges/components\n- **Formatting Libraries**: \n  - `date-fns` for time formatting\n  - `numeral.js` for currency formatting\n\n### Observability\n- **Logging**: Existing Python logging\n- **Performance Tracking**: Minimal overhead approach\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### Backend Components\n1. **ActivityTracker**\n   - Responsibility: Capture and store agent execution metadata\n   - Extends existing `activity_tracker.py`\n   - Captures: start time, end time, duration, model, cost\n\n2. **AgentRuntime**\n   - Responsibility: Calculate execution metrics\n   - Track token usage\n   - Estimate cost based on model pricing\n   - Generate execution metadata\n\n3. **CostEstimationService**\n   - Responsibility: Calculate precise agent execution costs\n   - Uses model pricing lookup\n   - Handles fallback estimation methods\n\n### Frontend Components\n1. **AgentSummaryPane**\n   - Responsibility: Display agent execution metadata\n   - Render cost, duration, model information\n   - Handle formatting of timestamps and costs\n\n2. **ExecutionBadge**\n   - Responsibility: Compact display of execution details\n   - Render cost, duration, model as small, informative badges\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n```\nAgentRuntime \n  → Calculate Metrics \n  → ActivityTracker.record_agent_completed() \n  → API Endpoint \n  → WebSocket/React State \n  → AgentSummaryPane\n```\n\n### Key Data Transformations\n- Convert raw milliseconds to human-readable duration\n- Format cost to currency with appropriate precision\n- Shorten model names for display\n- Handle edge cases (no cost data, incomplete execution)\n\n## 5. API Design\n\n### New/Modified Endpoints\n- `GET /agent/state/{agent_id}`\n  - Returns enhanced agent state with execution metadata\n  - Response includes: \n    ```json\n    {\n      "agent_id": "string",\n      "status": "string",\n      "started_at": "ISO8601 timestamp",\n      "completed_at": "ISO8601 timestamp",\n      "duration_ms": "number",\n      "model_used": "string",\n      "cost_estimate": "number",\n      "cost_currency": "USD"\n    }\n    ```\n\n## 6. Deployment Strategy\n- Containerized deployment (Docker)\n- No schema migrations required\n- Backward compatible with existing systems\n- Phased rollout possible\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Backend Tests\n- Unit tests for CostEstimationService\n- Integration tests for ActivityTracker extensions\n- Mock Claude API for consistent cost calculation tests\n\n### Frontend Tests\n- Component rendering tests\n- Snapshot tests for badge formatting\n- Edge case handling (incomplete data, zero cost)\n\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk: Performance Overhead\n- **Mitigation**: Lazy calculation of costs\n- **Mitigation**: Caching model pricing information\n\n### Risk: Inconsistent Cost Tracking\n- **Mitigation**: Provide clear visual indicators for estimated costs\n- **Mitigation**: Fallback mechanisms in cost calculation\n\n## 9. Open Questions\n- Precise method for token count estimation\n- Handling of multi-stage agent executions\n- Long-term storage of execution metadata\n\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\n1. Full historical cost tracking (rejected: out of scope)\n2. Real-time cost streaming (rejected: performance concerns)\n3. External cost tracking service (rejected: added complexity)\n\n## Conclusion\nThis architecture provides a lightweight, flexible approach to adding cost and performance metadata to the existing agent tracking system. By focusing on minimal changes and clear data flow, we can enhance developer insights without significant refactoring.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MJRTZd43DCCXTVpNNxzDH9', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "[Errno 30] Read-only file system: \'/src\'"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints 