{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:26:03", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-25041c14-4ea5-493b-8268-bc8bc0cda44e', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md",\n  "project_name": "Agent Completion Visibility Enhancement",\n  "project_id": "761acb42",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XHGNQpnXcsM4mc72uGq7uv', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XHGNQpnXcsM4mc72uGq7uv', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_requirements.md"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BLqQv8ctyUTeYMcvCzgoAq', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/agent_completion_visibility_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BLqQv8ctyUTeYMcvCzgoAq', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Completion Summary Visibility\\n\\n## Vision\\nMake agent completion results visible in the UI so users can see what each bot actually did. When agents complete, their summary should be prominently displayed - not hidden behind expandable sections.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nUser reports: \\"Bots show completed, but I don\'t see any UI changes. What was the status of the last task?\\"\\n\\nThe current system:\\n1. Agents produce structured outputs with `summary`, `self_analysis`, `deliverables` fields\\n2. These are stored in `result` data when agent completes  \\n3. BUT: The UI only shows \\"Completed\\" status - the actual summary is hidden in expandable detail sections\\n4. User cannot easily see what each agent accomplished without clicking through multiple levels\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Display agent completion summaries prominently in the Agent Tasks section\\n2. Show two-sentence summary of what each agent did when it completes\\n3. Make deliverables list visible for completed agents\\n4. Enhance Activity Feed to highlight completion summaries\\n5. Provide better communication between bots and user\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Agent Tasks Section Enhancement**\\n  - When agent status is \\"completed\\", show summary text prominently below the status\\n  - Display up to 2-3 key points from `result.summary` or `result.self_analysis`\\n  - Show count of deliverables (e.g., \\"Created 3 files\\") with option to expand\\n  - Add visual indication that detailed info is available (e.g., info icon)\\n\\n- **Activity Feed Enhancement**\\n  - For `agent_completed` activities, show summary text in the collapsed view\\n  - Make completion entries more informative without requiring expansion\\n  - Include deliverable count in activity entry\\n\\n- **Agent State Storage Enhancement**  \\n  - Ensure `summary`, `self_analysis`, and `deliverables` from agent output are stored in agent_states\\n  - These fields should be accessible via `/api/activity/states` endpoint\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time streaming of agent output (future enhancement)\\n- Notification system for completions\\n- Historical summary browsing\\n- Detailed cost/token display in summary\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n### Story 1: View Completion Summary\\n**As a** user monitoring agent progress  \\n**I want to** see a summary of what each agent accomplished when it completes  \\n**So that** I understand what happened without digging through logs\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- When agent status changes to \\"completed\\", a 1-2 sentence summary appears below the status badge\\n- Summary is visible without clicking or expanding anything\\n- If no summary is available, show \\"Completed successfully\\" or similar default\\n\\n### Story 2: See Deliverables at a Glance\\n**As a** user tracking project output  \\n**I want to** see what files/artifacts each agent produced  \\n**So that** I know what to look for in the Generated Files section\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Completed agents show deliverable count (e.g., \\"\\ud83d\\udcc1 3 deliverables\\")\\n- Clicking reveals the list of deliverable paths\\n- Links to corresponding entries in Generated Files section (if applicable)\\n\\n### Story 3: Activity Feed Context\\n**As a** user reviewing activity history  \\n**I want to** see completion context in the Activity Feed  \\n**So that** I can scan through and understand what happened without expanding each item\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- Agent completion activities show first line of summary in preview\\n- Still expandable for full details\\n- Clear visual distinction for completion events\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Data Flow (Existing - needs exposure to UI)\\n```\\nAgent Output \\u2192 {\\n  status: \\"success\\",\\n  summary: \\"What was accomplished\\",\\n  self_analysis: \\"Performance reflection\\",\\n  deliverables: [\\"path1.md\\", \\"path2.py\\"],\\n  ...\\n}\\n\\n\\u2193 stored in \\u2193\\n\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_completed(result={...})\\nagent_states[agent_id] = { status: \\"completed\\", ... }\\n\\n\\u2193 exposed via \\u2193\\n\\nGET /api/activity/states \\u2192 { agent_states: { agent_id: {...} } }\\n```\\n\\n### Frontend Changes Needed\\n\\n**App.jsx - Agent Tasks Section:**\\n```jsx\\n// After status badge, add:\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.summary && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'12px\', color: \'#9ca3af\', marginTop: \'6px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcdd {state.summary.slice(0, 150)}...\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#6b7280\', marginTop: \'4px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcc1 {state.deliverables.length} deliverable(s)\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n```\\n\\n**ActivityFeed.jsx - Completion Display:**\\n```jsx\\ncase \'agent_completed\':\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {data.result?.summary && (\\n        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n          <strong>Summary:</strong> {data.result.summary}\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      {data.result?.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n        <div>\\n          <strong>Deliverables:</strong> {data.result.deliverables.length} file(s)\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      // ...existing detail expansion\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n```\\n\\n### Backend Changes Needed\\n\\n**backend/main.py - _execute_agent_background():**\\nEnsure result fields are stored in active_agents state:\\n```python\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"result\\"] = result\\n# ADD: Extract key summary fields for easy access\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"self_analysis\\"] = result.get(\\"self_analysis\\", \\"\\")\\nself.active_agents[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", [])\\n```\\n\\n**activity_tracker.py - record_agent_completed():**\\nExtract and store summary in agent_states:\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_completed(self, agent_id, agent_name, request_id, result=None):\\n    # ... existing code ...\\n    \\n    # Update agent state with summary info\\n    if agent_id in self.agent_states:\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\") if result else \\"\\"\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", []) if result else []\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Visibility**: Agent completion summaries visible without any clicks\\n2. **Informativeness**: User can understand what happened at a glance\\n3. **Non-disruptive**: Changes don\'t break existing functionality\\n4. **Graceful degradation**: Works when summary fields are missing (shows default text)\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Start a task and let agents complete\\n2. Verify summary text appears in Agent Tasks section for completed agents\\n3. Verify Activity Feed shows summary in agent_completed entries\\n4. Verify deliverable count displays correctly\\n5. Test with agents that don\'t return summary (should show fallback)\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Keep changes minimal - enhance existing components rather than replacing\\n- Use existing styling patterns for consistency\\n- Summary text should truncate gracefully if too long\\n- Consider adding \\"Show more\\" link for full self_analysis\\n\\n## Related Files\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Agent Tasks section (~lines 400-460)\\n- `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx` - renderActivityDetails function\\n- `backend/main.py` - _execute_agent_background function\\n- `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - record_agent_completed function\\n\\n## Priority: HIGH\\nThis directly impacts user experience and understanding of system behavior.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019x2vzEuNmhdGfPeYizcGao', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: Agent Completion Visibility Enhancement\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### High-Level Design\nThe proposed architecture focuses on enhancing the visibility of agent completion results with minimal changes to the existing system. We\'ll implement a lightweight, non-disruptive approach that exposes agent completion summaries directly in the UI without fundamentally restructuring the current architecture.\n\n### Architectural Pattern\n- **Existing Pattern**: Microservices with event-driven communication\n- **Enhancement Approach**: Decorator/Interceptor pattern for adding visibility layers\n- **Core Philosophy**: Minimal invasive changes, maximum information exposure\n\n## B. Tech Stack \n- **Frontend**: \n  - React (existing framework)\n  - Context API for state management \n- **Backend**: \n  - Python (existing language)\n  - Minimal modifications to existing modules\n- **State Management**:\n  - Leverage existing `agent_states` dictionary\n  - Enhanced with summary and deliverables metadata\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### Frontend Components to Modify\n1. **AgentTasksSection**\n   - Responsibility: Display agent completion summaries\n   - Modifications:\n     * Add summary text rendering\n     * Show deliverable count\n     * Maintain existing layout and styling\n\n2. **ActivityFeed**\n   - Responsibility: Expose completion context in activity entries\n   - Modifications:\n     * Render summary in collapsed view\n     * Show deliverable metadata\n     * Preserve existing expandable behavior\n\n### Backend Components to Update\n1. **ActivityTracker**\n   - Enhanced to store and expose summary metadata\n   - No structural changes to existing tracking mechanism\n\n2. **Agent Execution Pipeline**\n   - Minimal modifications to `_execute_agent_background()`\n   - Ensure summary fields are captured and stored\n\n## D. Data Flow\n\n```\nAgent Completion Process:\n[Agent Output] -> \n  {summary, self_analysis, deliverables} \n  |\n  V\n[ActivityTracker.record_agent_completed()] \n  |\n  V\n[Update agent_states with summary metadata]\n  |\n  V\n[Frontend Renders Summary in UI Components]\n```\n\n## E. File/Directory Structure\n```\nensemble/\n│\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── App.jsx           # Main application component\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── AgentTasks.jsx\n│   │   │   └── ActivityFeed.jsx\n│\n├── backend/\n│   ├── main.py               # Core execution logic\n│   └── activity_tracker.py   # Activity tracking module\n```\n\n## F. API and State Management\n- **Existing Endpoint**: `/api/activity/states`\n- **No New Endpoints Required**\n- **State Modification**: \n  ```python\n  agent_states[agent_id] = {\n    "status": "completed",\n    "summary": "Two-sentence agent accomplishment",\n    "deliverables": ["file1.md", "file2.py"]\n  }\n  ```\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n- **Deployment Type**: Incremental update\n- **Risk Level**: Low\n- **Deployment Steps**:\n  1. Update frontend components\n  2. Modify backend metadata storage\n  3. No database schema changes\n  4. No runtime environment modifications\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n1. **Unit Tests**\n   - Frontend component rendering\n   - State update mechanisms\n2. **Integration Tests**\n   - Summary display across different agent types\n   - Deliverable metadata rendering\n3. **Edge Case Testing**\n   - Agents without summaries\n   - Empty deliverable lists\n   - Long summary text truncation\n\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\n1. **Risk**: Unexpected UI breaks\n   - **Mitigation**: Defensive rendering, fallback displays\n2. **Risk**: Performance overhead\n   - **Mitigation**: Lightweight metadata storage, minimal computation\n\n## J. Alternatives Considered\n1. **Full Redesign of Activity Tracking**\n   - Rejected: Too invasive, high implementation cost\n2. **Real-time Streaming of Agent Output**\n   - Postponed: Out of current scope, future enhancement\n\n## K. Open Questions for Stakeholder\n- Preferred summary length (currently set to ~150 characters)\n- Specific styling preferences for summary display\n- Future plans for more detailed agent output visualization\n\n## L. Implementation Effort\n- **Estimated Development Time**: 2-3 days\n- **Complexity**: Low\n- **Impact**: High user experience improvement\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019x2vzEuNmhdGfPeYizcGao', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_022603.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_022603.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
