{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:26:16", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1fe1b732-9b56-4d8b-9d80-ec9cd8e5e83a', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Implement backend cost tracking enhancements",\n  "architecture": "/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/backend_tasks.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01H7ruhKeSZ458Aefman9ysr', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01H7ruhKeSZ458Aefman9ysr', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "File not found: /src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XoxjZArWKixNVi4wkyqfRx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XoxjZArWKixNVi4wkyqfRx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task. This will provide better visibility into agent performance and resource usage.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Display execution cost estimates for each agent in the agent summary\\n2. Show start time, completion time, and duration of execution\\n3. Tag each agent with the model it used during execution\\n4. Ensure data flows from backend tracking to frontend display\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n1. **Backend Enhancements**:\\n   - Capture start time, end time, and duration for agent executions\\n   - Track the model used by each agent (from AgentRuntime)\\n   - Calculate cost estimates based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Include this data in activity tracking and agent states\\n\\n2. **Frontend Enhancements**:\\n   - Display cost estimate in AgentSummaryPane component\\n   - Show execution duration (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Display model tag/badge for each agent\\n   - Format costs in a user-friendly way (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Format durations in appropriate units (ms, seconds, minutes)\\n\\n3. **Data Flow**:\\n   - Extend Activity Tracker to capture cost and model data\\n   - Update API endpoints to return this information\\n   - Update AgentSummaryPane to consume and display the data\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Historical cost aggregation/reporting (future feature)\\n- Budget alerts or limits (future feature)\\n- Per-tool cost breakdown (future feature)\\n- Real-time cost streaming during execution (will show on completion)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing activity_tracker.py system\\n- Should integrate with existing AgentRuntime metrics\\n- Frontend changes limited to AgentSummaryPane component\\n- Backend must be backward compatible with existing agent executions\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Each completed agent shows:\\n   - Start time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Completion time (ISO format or relative time)\\n   - Duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n   - Cost estimate (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n   - Model tag (e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\")\\n\\n2. \\u2705 Data is captured reliably from backend\\n3. \\u2705 UI displays information in a readable, compact format\\n4. \\u2705 No performance degradation to existing functionality\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. AgentRuntime already tracks token usage and model selection\\n2. Model pricing information is available (from model_selector.py or similar)\\n3. Activity tracker can be extended without breaking existing consumers\\n4. Frontend has access to activity data via WebSocket or polling\\n\\n## User Stories\\n1. **As a developer**, I want to see how much each agent execution costs so I can optimize expensive operations\\n2. **As a developer**, I want to see execution duration so I can identify slow agents\\n3. **As a developer**, I want to see which model was used so I can correlate performance with model choice\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Backend Changes\\n1. Extend `record_agent_completed()` in activity_tracker.py to accept:\\n   - `started_at`: ISO timestamp\\n   - `completed_at`: ISO timestamp  \\n   - `duration_ms`: milliseconds\\n   - `model_used`: model identifier\\n   - `cost_estimate`: float (USD)\\n\\n2. Update AgentRuntime to:\\n   - Track start time on initialization\\n   - Calculate cost based on token usage and model pricing\\n   - Pass this data to activity tracker on completion\\n\\n3. Update API response in main.py to include these fields in agent state\\n\\n### Frontend Changes\\n1. Update AgentSummaryPane.jsx to:\\n   - Display execution timeline (started \\u2192 completed)\\n   - Show duration badge\\n   - Show cost estimate badge\\n   - Show model tag\\n   - Handle formatting for readability\\n\\n### Data Structure\\n```javascript\\n// Expected agent info structure\\n{\\n  agent_id: \\"exec_dir_1\\",\\n  type: \\"executive_director\\",\\n  status: \\"completed\\",\\n  started_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:00Z\\",\\n  completed_at: \\"2024-01-13T10:30:42Z\\",\\n  duration_ms: 42000,\\n  model_used: \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\",\\n  cost_estimate: 0.0042,\\n  // ... existing fields\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n- Cost calculation should use actual token counts from Claude API responses\\n- If token counts unavailable, estimate based on character counts with clear \\"~\\" prefix\\n- Duration should handle both running (show elapsed) and completed states\\n- Model tags should be shortened for display (e.g., \\"sonnet-3.5\\" instead of full name)\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GTNxFBc5VcDAtFtfGbKMj8', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement -name "architecture.md" 2>/dev/null || find src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement -name "architecture.md" 2>/dev/null || echo "architecture.md not found"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GTNxFBc5VcDAtFtfGbKMj8', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Q4te8EuB1B6kiYFGzd5dDC', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Q4te8EuB1B6kiYFGzd5dDC', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis document outlines the architecture for enhancing the ensemble UI to display cost estimates, execution duration, and model information for each agent task.\\n\\n## System Context\\n\\n### Current Architecture\\nThe system has:\\n- **Backend**: Activity tracking via `activity_tracker.py` that monitors agent execution\\n- **API Layer**: WebSocket/REST endpoints in `main.py` that expose agent state\\n- **Frontend**: React-based UI with `AgentSummaryPane.jsx` displaying agent information\\n- **Agent Runtime**: `AgentRuntime` managing agent execution with Claude API\\n\\n### Enhancement Goals\\nAdd cost and timing metrics to the existing activity tracking and display pipeline.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Component Architecture\\n\\n### 1. Backend Components\\n\\n#### 1.1 Activity Tracker Extension (`activity_tracker.py`)\\n**Current State**: Tracks agent lifecycle, tool usage, iterations, and status changes\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\n- Extend `record_agent_started()` to capture:\\n  - `started_at`: ISO timestamp\\n  - `model_used`: Model identifier from AgentRuntime\\n- Extend `record_agent_completed()` to capture:\\n  - `completed_at`: ISO timestamp\\n  - `duration_ms`: Calculated duration in milliseconds\\n  - `cost_estimate`: Calculated cost in USD\\n  - `token_usage`: Input/output tokens used\\n\\n**Data Structure Changes**:\\n```python\\n# Enhanced agent_hierarchy entry\\n{\\n    \\"agent_id\\": str,\\n    \\"agent_name\\": str,\\n    \\"agent_type\\": str,\\n    \\"status\\": str,\\n    \\"started_at\\": str,  # ISO timestamp\\n    \\"completed_at\\": str,  # ISO timestamp (optional)\\n    \\"duration_ms\\": int,  # milliseconds (optional)\\n    \\"model_used\\": str,  # e.g., \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\"\\n    \\"cost_estimate\\": float,  # USD (optional)\\n    \\"token_usage\\": {  # optional\\n        \\"input_tokens\\": int,\\n        \\"output_tokens\\": int,\\n        \\"total_tokens\\": int\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### 1.2 Cost Calculator (New Module: `cost_calculator.py`)\\n**Purpose**: Calculate cost estimates based on token usage and model pricing\\n\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Maintain model pricing table (per-token costs)\\n- Calculate cost from token usage\\n- Handle different model families (Sonnet, Opus, Haiku)\\n- Provide estimation when exact token counts unavailable\\n\\n**Interface**:\\n```python\\nclass CostCalculator:\\n    def calculate_cost(\\n        self,\\n        model: str,\\n        input_tokens: int,\\n        output_tokens: int\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\"\\"\\"Calculate cost in USD\\"\\"\\"\\n        pass\\n    \\n    def estimate_cost_from_chars(\\n        self,\\n        model: str,\\n        input_chars: int,\\n        output_chars: int\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\"\\"\\"Estimate cost when token counts unavailable\\"\\"\\"\\n        pass\\n```\\n\\n**Model Pricing Table** (as of Jan 2024):\\n```python\\nMODEL_PRICING = {\\n    \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\": {\\n        \\"input\\": 0.003 / 1000,  # $3 per million tokens\\n        \\"output\\": 0.015 / 1000   # $15 per million tokens\\n    },\\n    \\"claude-3-opus-20240229\\": {\\n        \\"input\\": 0.015 / 1000,\\n        \\"output\\": 0.075 / 1000\\n    },\\n    \\"claude-3-haiku-20240307\\": {\\n        \\"input\\": 0.00025 / 1000,\\n        \\"output\\": 0.00125 / 1000\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### 1.3 AgentRuntime Integration\\n**Current State**: Manages agent execution, tracks iterations and tool use\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\n- Capture start time on initialization\\n- Extract model identifier from configuration\\n- Extract token usage from Claude API responses\\n- Calculate cost using `CostCalculator`\\n- Pass metrics to `activity_tracker` on completion\\n\\n**Implementation Points**:\\n- In `__init__`: Record start time\\n- In `_process_response()`: Extract token usage from API response\\n- In completion/failure: Calculate duration and cost, pass to activity tracker\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. API Layer\\n\\n#### 2.1 WebSocket/REST Endpoints (`main.py`)\\n**Current State**: Provides endpoints for agent state and activity data\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\n- Include new fields in agent state responses:\\n  - `started_at`, `completed_at`, `duration_ms`\\n  - `model_used`, `cost_estimate`, `token_usage`\\n- Ensure backward compatibility (new fields optional)\\n\\n**Response Format**:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent_id\\": \\"exec_dir_1\\",\\n  \\"agent_name\\": \\"Executive Director\\",\\n  \\"agent_type\\": \\"executive_director\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n  \\"started_at\\": \\"2024-01-13T10:30:00.123Z\\",\\n  \\"completed_at\\": \\"2024-01-13T10:30:42.456Z\\",\\n  \\"duration_ms\\": 42333,\\n  \\"model_used\\": \\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\\",\\n  \\"cost_estimate\\": 0.0042,\\n  \\"token_usage\\": {\\n    \\"input_tokens\\": 1200,\\n    \\"output_tokens\\": 350,\\n    \\"total_tokens\\": 1550\\n  },\\n  \\"current_task\\": \\"Completed\\",\\n  \\"children\\": []\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Frontend Components\\n\\n#### 3.1 AgentSummaryPane Enhancement (`AgentSummaryPane.jsx`)\\n**Current State**: Displays agent name, type, status, current task\\n\\n**Enhancements**:\\nAdd display sections for:\\n1. **Execution Timeline**: Start \\u2192 End times (relative or absolute)\\n2. **Duration Badge**: Formatted duration (e.g., \\"2.3s\\", \\"1m 45s\\")\\n3. **Cost Badge**: Formatted cost (e.g., \\"$0.0042\\")\\n4. **Model Tag**: Shortened model name (e.g., \\"Sonnet 3.5\\")\\n\\n**Layout Design**:\\n```\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502 \\ud83e\\udd16 Executive Director                   \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Status: \\u2705 Completed                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502 \\u23f1\\ufe0f 2.3s  \\ud83d\\udcb0 $0.0042  \\ud83c\\udff7\\ufe0f Sonnet 3.5     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Started: 10:30:00                       \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Completed: 10:30:02                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502 Current Task: Completed                 \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n```\\n\\n**Utility Functions**:\\n```javascript\\n// Format duration\\nfunction formatDuration(durationMs) {\\n  if (durationMs < 1000) return `${durationMs}ms`;\\n  if (durationMs < 60000) return `${(durationMs / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`;\\n  const mins = Math.floor(durationMs / 60000);\\n  const secs = ((durationMs % 60000) / 1000).toFixed(0);\\n  return `${mins}m ${secs}s`;\\n}\\n\\n// Format cost\\nfunction formatCost(costUsd) {\\n  if (costUsd === null || costUsd === undefined) return \'N/A\';\\n  if (costUsd < 0.0001) return \'<$0.0001\';\\n  return `$${costUsd.toFixed(4)}`;\\n}\\n\\n// Shorten model name\\nfunction formatModelName(model) {\\n  if (model.includes(\'sonnet\')) return \'Sonnet 3.5\';\\n  if (model.includes(\'opus\')) return \'Opus\';\\n  if (model.includes(\'haiku\')) return \'Haiku\';\\n  return model;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n### 1. Agent Execution Start\\n```\\nAgentRuntime.__init__()\\n  \\u2193\\nRecord start_time\\n  \\u2193\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_started(\\n  agent_id, agent_name, agent_type, model_used, started_at\\n)\\n  \\u2193\\nUpdate agent_hierarchy and agent_states\\n  \\u2193\\nEmit to WebSocket\\n  \\u2193\\nFrontend receives agent state\\n  \\u2193\\nAgentSummaryPane displays \\"Running\\" with start time\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Agent Execution Completion\\n```\\nAgentRuntime completes\\n  \\u2193\\nExtract token_usage from API response\\n  \\u2193\\nCalculate duration_ms = now - start_time\\n  \\u2193\\nCostCalculator.calculate_cost(model, tokens)\\n  \\u2193\\nactivity_tracker.record_agent_completed(\\n  agent_id, completed_at, duration_ms, cost_estimate, token_usage\\n)\\n  \\u2193\\nUpdate agent_hierarchy and agent_states\\n  \\u2193\\nEmit to WebSocket\\n  \\u2193\\nFrontend receives updated agent state\\n  \\u2193\\nAgentSummaryPane displays metrics badges\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technology Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.11+\\n- **Framework**: Existing activity_tracker system\\n- **API**: WebSocket/REST (existing)\\n- **New Module**: `cost_calculator.py`\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n- **Component**: `AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n- **Styling**: Existing CSS/styling system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Design Decisions\\n\\n### 1. Cost Calculation Strategy\\n**Decision**: Calculate cost at agent completion time\\n**Rationale**: \\n- Token counts only available after API response\\n- Avoids streaming cost updates (complexity)\\n- Matches milestone scope (show on completion)\\n\\n### 2. Token Usage Source\\n**Decision**: Extract from Claude API response `usage` field\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Most accurate source\\n- Already available in API responses\\n- Fallback to estimation if unavailable\\n\\n### 3. Model Pricing Storage\\n**Decision**: Hardcode pricing in `cost_calculator.py`\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Pricing changes infrequently\\n- Simple to update\\n- Future: Could load from config file\\n\\n### 4. Duration Precision\\n**Decision**: Store in milliseconds, display with appropriate units\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Milliseconds provide precision\\n- Display formatting adapts to duration length\\n- Easy to aggregate for analytics later\\n\\n### 5. Backward Compatibility\\n**Decision**: All new fields optional in API responses\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Existing consumers won\'t break\\n- Graceful degradation if data missing\\n- Frontend checks for field existence\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Cost calculation: < 1ms per agent\\n- No impact on agent execution speed\\n- Activity tracker overhead: < 5% of execution time\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Handle missing token usage gracefully\\n- Fallback to estimation when needed\\n- Never crash agent execution due to tracking failures\\n\\n### Maintainability\\n- Model pricing centralized and easy to update\\n- Clear separation of concerns (tracking, calculation, display)\\n- Well-documented data structures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests\\n1. **CostCalculator**:\\n   - Test cost calculation for each model\\n   - Test estimation fallback\\n   - Test edge cases (zero tokens, unknown model)\\n\\n2. **ActivityTracker**:\\n   - Test new fields captured correctly\\n   - Test backward compatibility\\n   - Test data structure updates\\n\\n### Integration Tests\\n1. **End-to-End Flow**:\\n   - Agent execution \\u2192 cost calculation \\u2192 API \\u2192 Frontend\\n   - Verify metrics display correctly\\n   - Test with different models\\n\\n2. **API Tests**:\\n   - Verify new fields in responses\\n   - Test backward compatibility\\n   - Test WebSocket updates\\n\\n### Frontend Tests\\n1. **Component Tests**:\\n   - Test duration formatting\\n   - Test cost formatting\\n   - Test model name shortening\\n   - Test missing data handling\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Security Considerations\\n\\n### Data Privacy\\n- Cost data not sensitive but could reveal usage patterns\\n- No additional authentication required (existing auth applies)\\n\\n### Input Validation\\n- Validate token counts are non-negative\\n- Validate duration is non-negative\\n- Handle malformed model names gracefully\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Backend (Milestone 1)\\n- Deploy `cost_calculator.py`\\n- Update `activity_tracker.py`\\n- Update `AgentRuntime` integration\\n- Test with existing agents\\n\\n### Phase 2: API (Milestone 2)\\n- Update API responses\\n- Test backward compatibility\\n- Deploy to staging\\n\\n### Phase 3: Frontend (Milestone 3)\\n- Update `AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n- Test display formatting\\n- Deploy to production\\n\\n### Rollback Plan\\n- Backend changes backward compatible\\n- Frontend can gracefully handle missing fields\\n- Can rollback each phase independently\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Future Enhancements\\n\\n### Out of Current Scope\\n1. **Historical Analytics**:\\n   - Cost aggregation by agent type\\n   - Cost trends over time\\n   - Budget tracking\\n\\n2. **Budget Controls**:\\n   - Alert when cost exceeds threshold\\n   - Pause execution on budget limit\\n   - Per-project cost limits\\n\\n3. **Detailed Breakdown**:\\n   - Per-tool cost attribution\\n   - Cost by iteration\\n   - Cost heatmaps\\n\\n4. **Real-Time Streaming**:\\n   - Stream cost updates during execution\\n   - Live token counting\\n   - Incremental cost display\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Appendix\\n\\n### A. File Locations\\n- Backend: `/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n- New Module: `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py`\\n- AgentRuntime: `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` (or similar)\\n- API: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/main.py`\\n- Frontend: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AgentSummaryPane.jsx`\\n\\n### B. Model Pricing Reference\\nUpdated pricing at: https://www.anthropic.com/pricing\\n\\n### C. Claude API Token Usage Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"usage\\": {\\n    \\"input_tokens\\": 1200,\\n    \\"output_tokens\\": 350\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NUtzgzs4tYCPzqzDhCFG1X', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent-cost-tracking-enhancement/backend_tasks.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement\n\n## Overview\nThis document breaks down the backend implementation tasks for adding cost estimates, execution duration, and model information to agent tracking. The implementation follows a Test-Driven Development (TDD) approach through the TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Task Summary\n- **Total Tasks**: 12\n- **Complexity**: 3 simple, 6 medium, 3 complex\n- **Estimated Total**: 15-20 development cycles\n\n---\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (Foundation)\n\n#### Task 1: Create Cost Calculator Module\n**Description**: Implement the `CostCalculator` class that calculates costs based on token usage and model pricing.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ `CostCalculator` class with `calculate_cost()` method\n- ✅ Support for Sonnet, Opus, and Haiku pricing models\n- ✅ `estimate_cost_from_chars()` fallback method when token counts unavailable\n- ✅ Handle unknown models gracefully (return None or default estimation)\n- ✅ Model pricing constants easily updatable\n- ✅ Returns costs in USD (float)\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Create**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_cost_calculator.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Calculate cost for each supported model\n- Handle zero tokens\n- Handle unknown model\n- Estimation from character counts\n- Edge cases (negative inputs, None inputs)\n\n---\n\n#### Task 2: Extend Activity Tracker Data Structures\n**Description**: Update `activity_tracker.py` to include timing, cost, and model fields in agent tracking.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ `agent_hierarchy` includes new fields: `started_at`, `completed_at`, `duration_ms`, `model_used`, `cost_estimate`, `token_usage`\n- ✅ `record_agent_started()` accepts `model_used` and `started_at` parameters\n- ✅ `record_agent_completed()` accepts `completed_at`, `duration_ms`, `cost_estimate`, `token_usage` parameters\n- ✅ Backward compatibility maintained (new fields optional)\n- ✅ Data validation for new fields (non-negative duration, valid timestamps)\n- ✅ WebSocket emissions include new fields\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_activity_tracker.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Start agent with model tracking\n- Complete agent with cost metrics\n- Backward compatibility (omitted fields)\n- Invalid data handling\n- WebSocket emission format\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: AgentRuntime Integration\n\n#### Task 3: Add Timing Tracking to AgentRuntime\n**Description**: Modify `AgentRuntime` to capture start/end times and calculate duration.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Record `started_at` timestamp on initialization\n- ✅ Calculate `duration_ms` on completion/failure\n- ✅ Pass timing data to activity tracker\n- ✅ Handle timezone-aware timestamps (ISO format)\n- ✅ No performance impact on agent execution\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2 (Activity Tracker Extension)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` (or similar AgentRuntime file)\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_runtime.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Start time recorded correctly\n- Duration calculated correctly\n- Multiple agents have independent timing\n- Exception handling doesn\'t lose timing\n\n---\n\n#### Task 4: Extract Model Information from AgentRuntime\n**Description**: Capture model identifier from agent configuration and track it throughout execution.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Extract model name from agent configuration/setup\n- ✅ Pass model information to activity tracker on start\n- ✅ Handle cases where model is not specified (default/fallback)\n- ✅ Support different model naming conventions\n- ✅ Model name standardization (e.g., full names vs. short names)\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2 (Activity Tracker Extension)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_runtime.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Model extracted from config\n- Default model when not specified\n- Different model formats handled\n- Model passed to activity tracker\n\n---\n\n#### Task 5: Extract Token Usage from Claude API Responses\n**Description**: Parse token usage information from Claude API responses and track it.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Extract `input_tokens` and `output_tokens` from API response `usage` field\n- ✅ Calculate `total_tokens` = input + output\n- ✅ Handle missing usage data gracefully (no crash)\n- ✅ Accumulate tokens across multiple API calls in single agent execution\n- ✅ Store token data in appropriate data structure\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2 (Activity Tracker Extension)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_runtime.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Token extraction from standard API response\n- Missing usage field handling\n- Multiple API calls accumulation\n- Malformed usage data handling\n\n---\n\n#### Task 6: Integrate Cost Calculation in AgentRuntime\n**Description**: Calculate costs on agent completion using `CostCalculator` and pass to activity tracker.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Import and use `CostCalculator` in AgentRuntime\n- ✅ Calculate cost on agent completion using actual token usage\n- ✅ Fall back to character-based estimation if tokens unavailable\n- ✅ Pass cost data to `record_agent_completed()`\n- ✅ Handle cost calculation errors gracefully (log error, continue execution)\n- ✅ Include model used in cost calculation\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (Cost Calculator), Task 2 (Activity Tracker), Task 5 (Token Extraction)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_runtime.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Cost calculated with real tokens\n- Fallback to character estimation\n- Cost calculation errors handled\n- Multiple models cost calculation\n- Zero-cost scenarios\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: API Layer Updates\n\n#### Task 7: Update API Responses with Cost/Timing Data\n**Description**: Modify API endpoints to include new cost and timing fields in agent state responses.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ WebSocket responses include all new fields\n- ✅ REST API responses include all new fields\n- ✅ Backward compatibility maintained (new fields added, existing unchanged)\n- ✅ Null/undefined handling for incomplete agents\n- ✅ Proper JSON serialization of timestamps and floats\n- ✅ Response schema documentation updated\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2 (Activity Tracker Extension)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/field/ensemble_ui/main.py`\n- `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/test_main.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Complete agent data in API response\n- Running agent with partial data\n- Backward compatibility test\n- JSON serialization edge cases\n- WebSocket emission format\n\n---\n\n#### Task 8: Add Data Validation and Error Handling\n**Description**: Implement robust validation and error handling for cost/timing data in API layer.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Validate timestamp formats (ISO 8601)\n- ✅ Validate numeric fields (duration_ms >= 0, cost_estimate >= 0)\n- ✅ Handle missing model information gracefully\n- ✅ Sanitize data before API responses\n- ✅ Log validation errors appropriately\n- ✅ Default values for missing data\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 7 (API Updates)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/field/ensemble_ui/main.py`\n- `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/test_main.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Invalid timestamp handling\n- Negative values handling\n- Missing field handling\n- Data sanitization\n- Error logging verification\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Integration and Testing\n\n#### Task 9: End-to-End Integration Testing\n**Description**: Create comprehensive integration tests that verify the complete flow from agent execution to API response.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Test complete agent execution with cost tracking\n- ✅ Verify timing accuracy across full flow\n- ✅ Test multiple concurrent agents\n- ✅ Test different model types\n- ✅ Verify WebSocket updates in real-time\n- ✅ Performance impact assessment\n\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 1-8 (All previous tasks)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files to Create**:\n- `/tests/integration/test_cost_tracking_e2e.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Single agent full lifecycle\n- Multiple concurrent agents\n- Different model combinations\n- Error scenarios end-to-end\n- Performance benchmarks\n\n---\n\n#### Task 10: Add Character-Based Cost Estimation\n**Description**: Implement fallback cost estimation when token usage is unavailable.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Character-to-token ratio estimation for different content types\n- ✅ Reasonable estimation accuracy (within 20% when possible)\n- ✅ Clear indication when estimates are used (e.g., prefix with "~")\n- ✅ Different ratios for input vs output text\n- ✅ Handle code, markdown, and plain text appropriately\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (Cost Calculator)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_cost_calculator.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Estimation accuracy tests\n- Different content types\n- Edge cases (empty strings, very long text)\n- Estimation marking/flagging\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: Error Handling and Edge Cases\n\n#### Task 11: Handle Agent Execution Failures\n**Description**: Ensure cost and timing tracking works correctly when agents fail or are interrupted.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Track timing even when agent fails\n- ✅ Calculate partial costs for failed agents\n- ✅ Mark incomplete cost calculations appropriately\n- ✅ Handle agent timeouts gracefully\n- ✅ Log appropriate error information\n- ✅ Maintain activity tracker consistency\n\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 2, 6 (Activity Tracker, Cost Integration)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n- `/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n- `/tests/runtime/agents/test_runtime.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Agent exception during execution\n- Agent timeout scenarios\n- API failures during execution\n- Partial token usage scenarios\n\n---\n\n#### Task 12: Performance Optimization and Monitoring\n**Description**: Optimize cost tracking performance and add monitoring for system impact.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✅ Cost calculation overhead < 1ms per agent\n- ✅ Memory usage impact < 5% increase\n- ✅ No impact on agent execution speed\n- ✅ Efficient data structure updates\n- ✅ Optional detailed logging for debugging\n- ✅ Performance metrics collection\n\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 1-11 (All previous tasks)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n**Files to Modify**:\n- `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py`\n- `/src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n- `/tests/performance/test_cost_tracking_performance.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Memory usage tests\n- Concurrent agent performance\n- Large-scale execution tests\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies Map\n\n```\nTask 1 (Cost Calculator) → Task 6 (Cost Integration) → Task 9 (E2E Testing)\n                       ↓                           ↗\nTask 2 (Activity Tracker) → Task 3,4,5,7 → Task 8 → Task 12 (Performance)\n                                       ↓\n                           Task 11 (Error Handling)\n                                       ↓\nTask 10 (Estimation) ──────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Critical Path\n1. **Task 1**: Cost Calculator (Foundation)\n2. **Task 2**: Activity Tracker Extension (Foundation)\n3. **Task 6**: Cost Integration (Core Logic)\n4. **Task 7**: API Updates (Delivery)\n5. **Task 9**: E2E Testing (Verification)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### TDD Coordinator Delegation\nEach task will be handed to the TDD Coordinator with:\n- Detailed test specifications\n- Implementation requirements\n- Acceptance criteria\n- Dependencies verification\n\n### Technology Assumptions (per defaults)\n- **Framework**: FastAPI/Python backend\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy (if persistence needed)\n- **Testing**: pytest with coverage\n- **API**: REST with JSON, WebSocket for real-time updates\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n```\nAgent Start → Record Timing → Extract Model → Track in Activity\n           ↓\nAgent Execution → Collect Tokens → Calculate Cost → Record Completion\n                                              ↓\n                                   API Response ← Activity Data\n```\n\n### Quality Gates\n- All tasks must have >90% test coverage\n- Integration tests must pass\n- Performance requirements must be met\n- Backward compatibility verified'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0