{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:57:54", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a668ad88-c4b0-4181-8b98-e3fc745d7d83', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0177BZYpRD62Wc6yCTcu7qWW', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0177BZYpRD62Wc6yCTcu7qWW', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent System Analysis & Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nThis document analyzes the Ensemble multi-agent system architecture and identifies the top 3 improvements that would make agents more effective. The analysis is based on reviewing the codebase, agent definitions, and system architecture.\\n\\n## Project Vision\\n\\nAnalyze the ensemble agent system to identify and implement the three most impactful improvements that will enhance agent effectiveness, reduce coordination failures, and improve overall system reliability.\\n\\n## Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Architecture Overview\\n- **Agent Hierarchy**: 4 tiers (Leadership \\u2192 Coordinators \\u2192 Developers/Testers \\u2192 Writers)\\n- **Total Agents**: 16 agents (consolidated from 23, 30% reduction)\\n- **Core Technology**: Anthropic Claude API with hierarchical delegation\\n- **Key Features**: TDD workflow, permission system, state persistence\\n\\n### Identified Issues\\n\\nAfter analyzing the codebase and agent definitions, the following problems were identified:\\n\\n#### 1. **Lack of Real-Time Progress Feedback**\\n- **Problem**: Agents execute in background threads without granular progress updates\\n- **Impact**: Users don\'t know what agents are doing, causing uncertainty about system status\\n- **Evidence**: \\n  - `main.py` uses background threads for execution (line 79)\\n  - WebSocket broadcasts only top-level status changes\\n  - No intermediate progress reporting during long-running agent operations\\n  - No visibility into which sub-agents are currently active\\n\\n#### 2. **Inadequate Error Recovery & Context Preservation**\\n- **Problem**: When agents fail, there\'s no automatic retry logic or context preservation for resume\\n- **Impact**: Single failures cascade, wasting tokens and requiring manual intervention\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - State persistence exists (`state.py`) but resume logic is incomplete (line 64 in `runtime.py`: \\"Full resume with conversation history would need message reconstruction\\")\\n  - No retry logic in `runtime.py` when tool execution fails\\n  - Failed spawns don\'t preserve parent agent context for debugging\\n  - Agent state checkpoints exist but aren\'t used for automatic recovery\\n\\n#### 3. **Missing Agent Performance Metrics & Feedback Loops**\\n- **Problem**: No tracking of agent effectiveness, token usage, or success rates\\n- **Impact**: Can\'t identify which agents need improvement or optimization\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - No analytics collection in `AgentRuntime`\\n  - No metrics on spawn success/failure rates\\n  - No token usage tracking per agent type\\n  - No performance comparison between model tiers\\n  - README acknowledges this gap: \\"Phase 3: Self-Improvement\\" includes \\"Agent performance analytics\\"\\n\\n### Additional Observations\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: Strong permission system, clear hierarchy, rogue agent prevention working well\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: TDD workflow is well-designed\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Model selection is static (could be adaptive based on task success)\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Agent definitions in markdown could benefit from validation schema\\n\\n## Top 3 Improvements (Prioritized)\\n\\n### Improvement #1: Real-Time Agent Progress Streaming \\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: High (dramatically improves user experience)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement granular progress tracking and streaming for agent execution, allowing users to see:\\n- Current agent activity (which agent is thinking/executing)\\n- Tool invocations in real-time\\n- Sub-agent spawn events\\n- Iteration progress (current/max)\\n- Streaming responses from Claude API\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Enhance `AgentRuntime` to emit progress events during execution\\n2. Add event bus or callback system for progress notifications\\n3. Update WebSocket handler to stream progress events to frontend\\n4. Add progress tracking to spawned agent execution\\n5. Include tool execution progress (start/complete/fail)\\n6. Show model selection decisions in progress feed\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Users can see which agent is active at any moment\\n- Tool invocations appear in real-time\\n- Spawn events are visible with parent-child relationships\\n- WebSocket clients receive progress updates < 500ms after events\\n- No performance degradation (< 5% overhead)\\n\\n### Improvement #2: Automatic Error Recovery & Context Preservation\\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: High  \\n**Impact**: High (reduces wasted tokens, improves reliability)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement intelligent error recovery with automatic retries and full context preservation for resume after failures.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Complete state manager resume functionality (message reconstruction)\\n2. Add retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\\n3. Implement context preservation for spawned agents (parent context + partial results)\\n4. Add automatic checkpoint validation and rollback\\n5. Create error classification system (retryable vs. fatal)\\n6. Preserve tool execution results across retries\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Agents can resume from last checkpoint after crashes\\n- Transient API errors (rate limits, timeouts) trigger automatic retry\\n- Failed spawns preserve parent agent state for debugging\\n- Context includes: conversation history, tool results, spawned agent data\\n- Recovery success rate > 80% for retryable errors\\n- Zero token waste on successful recovery (resume from checkpoint)\\n\\n### Improvement #3: Agent Performance Analytics & Adaptive Optimization\\n**Priority**: MEDIUM  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: Medium-High (enables continuous improvement)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement comprehensive analytics tracking for agent performance with adaptive model selection based on historical success rates.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Track metrics per agent instance:\\n   - Token usage (input/output)\\n   - Execution time\\n   - Success/failure rates\\n   - Iteration count vs. max iterations\\n   - Tool invocation patterns\\n2. Aggregate metrics by agent type and model tier\\n3. Create analytics dashboard endpoint for reporting\\n4. Implement adaptive model selection:\\n   - Start with budget tier default\\n   - Upgrade model if agent fails repeatedly\\n   - Downgrade model if agent consistently succeeds quickly\\n5. Add performance comparison reports (model A vs. model B for same task)\\n6. Export metrics for analysis (JSON, CSV)\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- All agent executions tracked with complete metrics\\n- Analytics API returns per-agent and aggregate statistics\\n- Adaptive model selection improves success rate by 15%+\\n- Token usage optimization reduces costs by 10%+\\n- Reports identify underperforming agents for refinement\\n- Metrics persist across system restarts\\n\\n## Out of Scope (For This Phase)\\n\\nThe following are important but not in the top 3:\\n- Enhanced TDD workflow validation\\n- File exploration agents\\n- Multi-user support\\n- Agent definition schema validation\\n- Performance profiling tools\\n- Cost prediction before execution\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Must maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent definitions\\n2. **Must not break permission system** (can_write_code, can_write_tests enforcement)\\n3. **Must not increase API costs** by more than 10%\\n4. **Must support concurrent agent execution** (multi-user eventually)\\n5. **Must preserve existing state file format** (add extensions, don\'t replace)\\n\\n## Success Criteria (Overall)\\n\\n1. \\u2705 Real-time progress visible to users\\n2. \\u2705 Error recovery succeeds > 80% for retryable failures\\n3. \\u2705 Performance metrics tracked for all agents\\n4. \\u2705 All existing tests continue to pass\\n5. \\u2705 Documentation updated for new features\\n6. \\u2705 Zero breaking changes to agent definitions\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n**Phase 1: Progress Streaming** (Implement First)\\n- High user impact\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Foundation for other improvements\\n\\n**Phase 2: Error Recovery** (Implement Second)\\n- High reliability impact\\n- High complexity (needs Phase 1 for monitoring)\\n- Builds on state persistence system\\n\\n**Phase 3: Performance Analytics** (Implement Third)\\n- Enables long-term improvement\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Leverages data from Phase 1 & 2\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Updated `AgentRuntime` class with progress events\\n2. Enhanced `StateManager` with full resume capability\\n3. New `AgentAnalytics` module for metrics tracking\\n4. Updated WebSocket handlers for streaming\\n5. New API endpoints for analytics queries\\n6. Updated documentation (README, implementation guide)\\n7. Test suite covering new functionality\\n8. Performance benchmarks before/after\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n\\n- **Improvement #1**: 2-3 days (progress streaming)\\n- **Improvement #2**: 3-4 days (error recovery)\\n- **Improvement #3**: 2-3 days (analytics)\\n- **Testing & Documentation**: 1-2 days\\n- **Total**: 8-12 days for complete implementation\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis analysis prioritizes improvements that:\\n1. **Maximize user value** (progress feedback eliminates uncertainty)\\n2. **Improve system reliability** (error recovery reduces failures)\\n3. **Enable continuous improvement** (analytics identify what to optimize next)\\n\\nThe three improvements are complementary and build on each other, creating a more robust and observable agent system.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012QLEHZGj98t1NdrVm31Toc', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Ensemble Agent System Improvements', 'description': 'Implementing top 3 improvements for ensemble agent system: progress streaming, error recovery, and performance analytics'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012QLEHZGj98t1NdrVm31Toc', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "6d864741", "message": "Created project: Ensemble Agent System Improvements", "summary": {"project_id": "6d864741", "project_name": "Ensemble Agent System Improvements", "description": "Implementing top 3 improvements for ensemble agent system: progress streaming, error recovery, and performance analytics", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:57:54.726770", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:57:54.726770", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:57:54.726770", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Ensemble Agent System Improvements\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n 