{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:58:07", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3e69e217-29ad-4eae-aeee-3be1c924ad5f', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01C8LVUUzn3HDMhnszVmkDof', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01C8LVUUzn3HDMhnszVmkDof', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# AI Provider Enhancement System - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project ID**: 3cd35d78\\n**Created**: 2026-01-13\\n**Status**: Planning\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Highest\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `provider_manager.py` - AI provider abstraction and detection system\\n2. `cli_provider.py` - CLI provider implementations for Claude and ChatGPT\\n3. Updated `runtime.py` - Integration with provider manager\\n4. Unit tests for provider detection and execution\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` is detected automatically\\n- [ ] CLI provider executes prompts using `claude --print` flag\\n- [ ] Graceful fallback to Anthropic API when CLI unavailable\\n- [ ] Provider success/failure metrics tracked in database\\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Existing runtime.py infrastructure\\n- Claude CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution cost tracking with dashboard integration.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `cost_estimator.py` - Pre-execution cost estimation based on task complexity\\n2. Enhanced `cost_calculator.py` - Extended with estimation capabilities\\n3. Updated `metrics.py` - Cost tracking fields and aggregation queries\\n4. Cost API endpoints for dashboard\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Pre-execution cost estimates available before spawning agents\\n- [ ] Estimates within 50% of actual costs\\n- [ ] Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- [ ] Cost fields added to agent_executions table\\n- [ ] API endpoints expose cost data to dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (provider tracking needed for CLI vs API cost differentiation)\\n- Existing cost_calculator.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Smart Agent Router\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium-High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement intelligent agent-task routing based on historical performance metrics.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `agent_router.py` - Performance analysis and routing recommendations\\n2. Updated agent execution flow to use router recommendations\\n3. Routing analytics API endpoints\\n4. Dashboard widget for routing explanations\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Agent recommendations based on historical performance from metrics.db\\n- [ ] Routing considers success rate (50%), cost efficiency (30%), speed (20%)\\n- [ ] Agent specialization bonuses applied (e.g., code_writer +10% for code tasks)\\n- [ ] Override capability for manual agent selection\\n- [ ] 10% improvement in overall success rate (measurable after deployment)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (cost data needed for cost efficiency calculations)\\n- Populated metrics.db with historical data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Project Recovery & Dashboard Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium\\n\\n### Objective\\nRestart 10 stalled projects and integrate all new features into the dashboard.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `recovery_orchestrator.py` - Project recovery logic\\n2. Recovery execution report\\n3. Dashboard integration for provider, cost, and routing features\\n4. Updated frontend components\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] All 10 stalled projects attempted for restart\\n- [ ] Recovery report generated with outcomes per project\\n- [ ] Independent error boundaries (one failure doesn\'t stop others)\\n- [ ] Dashboard shows provider usage, cost trends, routing info\\n- [ ] Provider success rates visible in dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 1-3 completed\\n- Access to project tracking system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone Summary\\n\\n| Milestone | Objective | Duration | Dependencies |\\n|-----------|-----------|----------|--------------|\\n| 1 | CLI Provider Integration | 2-3 days | None |\\n| 2 | Cost Estimation Module | 2-3 days | Milestone 1 |\\n| 3 | Smart Agent Router | 2-3 days | Milestone 2 |\\n| 4 | Project Recovery & Dashboard | 2-3 days | Milestones 1-3 |\\n\\n**Total Estimated Duration**: 8-12 days\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### TD1: Provider Selection Strategy\\n- **Decision**: CLI preferred over API when available\\n- **Rationale**: CLI tools use user\'s existing subscription, avoiding API costs\\n\\n### TD2: Cost Estimation Approach\\n- **Decision**: Use task complexity heuristics for output token estimation\\n- **Rationale**: More accurate than fixed estimates, calibrated to task types\\n\\n### TD3: Routing Algorithm Weights\\n- **Decision**: 50% success rate, 30% cost efficiency, 20% speed\\n- **Rationale**: Reliability most important, then cost, then speed\\n\\n### TD4: Recovery Sequence\\n- **Decision**: Sequential processing, not parallel\\n- **Rationale**: Easier debugging, independent error boundaries, API rate limits\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cost_estimator.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/agent_router.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/recovery_orchestrator.py`\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Document Status**: Complete\\n**Next Step**: System Architecture\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AveHcGweFcBh1qNycYH9yC', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'AI Provider Enhancement System', 'description': 'Implement comprehensive enhancements to AI provider integration, cost estimation, agent routing, and project recovery systems.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AveHcGweFcBh1qNycYH9yC', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "326e1466", "message": "Created project: AI Provider Enhancement System", "summary": {"project_id": "326e1466", "project_name": "AI Provider Enhancement System", "description": "Implement comprehensive enhancements to AI provider integration, cost estimation, agent routing, and project recovery systems.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:04.443245", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:04.443245", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:58:04.443245", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'AI Provider Enhancement System\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FkZtWF1xUSscPoGVaupWYZ', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '326e1466', 'description': 'Implement milestone plan for AI Provider Enhancement System', 'assigned_to': 'development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FkZtWF1xUSscPoGVaupWYZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "b8702ba4", "message": "Added task: Implement milestone plan for AI Provider Enhancement System"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following form