{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:58:14", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-b4731ac0-fc48-4d71-b7a4-7d799460c5f7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "AI Provider Enhancement System",\n  "project_id": "326e1466",\n  "task_id": "b8702ba4"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FSHNXeLbmwHccLP26xq2aW', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FSHNXeLbmwHccLP26xq2aW', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# AI Provider Enhancement System - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project ID**: 3cd35d78\\n**Created**: 2026-01-13\\n**Status**: Planning\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Highest\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `provider_manager.py` - AI provider abstraction and detection system\\n2. `cli_provider.py` - CLI provider implementations for Claude and ChatGPT\\n3. Updated `runtime.py` - Integration with provider manager\\n4. Unit tests for provider detection and execution\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` is detected automatically\\n- [ ] CLI provider executes prompts using `claude --print` flag\\n- [ ] Graceful fallback to Anthropic API when CLI unavailable\\n- [ ] Provider success/failure metrics tracked in database\\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Existing runtime.py infrastructure\\n- Claude CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution cost tracking with dashboard integration.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `cost_estimator.py` - Pre-execution cost estimation based on task complexity\\n2. Enhanced `cost_calculator.py` - Extended with estimation capabilities\\n3. Updated `metrics.py` - Cost tracking fields and aggregation queries\\n4. Cost API endpoints for dashboard\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Pre-execution cost estimates available before spawning agents\\n- [ ] Estimates within 50% of actual costs\\n- [ ] Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- [ ] Cost fields added to agent_executions table\\n- [ ] API endpoints expose cost data to dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (provider tracking needed for CLI vs API cost differentiation)\\n- Existing cost_calculator.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Smart Agent Router\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium-High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement intelligent agent-task routing based on historical performance metrics.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `agent_router.py` - Performance analysis and routing recommendations\\n2. Updated agent execution flow to use router recommendations\\n3. Routing analytics API endpoints\\n4. Dashboard widget for routing explanations\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Agent recommendations based on historical performance from metrics.db\\n- [ ] Routing considers success rate (50%), cost efficiency (30%), speed (20%)\\n- [ ] Agent specialization bonuses applied (e.g., code_writer +10% for code tasks)\\n- [ ] Override capability for manual agent selection\\n- [ ] 10% improvement in overall success rate (measurable after deployment)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (cost data needed for cost efficiency calculations)\\n- Populated metrics.db with historical data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Project Recovery & Dashboard Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium\\n\\n### Objective\\nRestart 10 stalled projects and integrate all new features into the dashboard.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `recovery_orchestrator.py` - Project recovery logic\\n2. Recovery execution report\\n3. Dashboard integration for provider, cost, and routing features\\n4. Updated frontend components\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] All 10 stalled projects attempted for restart\\n- [ ] Recovery report generated with outcomes per project\\n- [ ] Independent error boundaries (one failure doesn\'t stop others)\\n- [ ] Dashboard shows provider usage, cost trends, routing info\\n- [ ] Provider success rates visible in dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 1-3 completed\\n- Access to project tracking system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone Summary\\n\\n| Milestone | Objective | Duration | Dependencies |\\n|-----------|-----------|----------|--------------|\\n| 1 | CLI Provider Integration | 2-3 days | None |\\n| 2 | Cost Estimation Module | 2-3 days | Milestone 1 |\\n| 3 | Smart Agent Router | 2-3 days | Milestone 2 |\\n| 4 | Project Recovery & Dashboard | 2-3 days | Milestones 1-3 |\\n\\n**Total Estimated Duration**: 8-12 days\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### TD1: Provider Selection Strategy\\n- **Decision**: CLI preferred over API when available\\n- **Rationale**: CLI tools use user\'s existing subscription, avoiding API costs\\n\\n### TD2: Cost Estimation Approach\\n- **Decision**: Use task complexity heuristics for output token estimation\\n- **Rationale**: More accurate than fixed estimates, calibrated to task types\\n\\n### TD3: Routing Algorithm Weights\\n- **Decision**: 50% success rate, 30% cost efficiency, 20% speed\\n- **Rationale**: Reliability most important, then cost, then speed\\n\\n### TD4: Recovery Sequence\\n- **Decision**: Sequential processing, not parallel\\n- **Rationale**: Easier debugging, independent error boundaries, API rate limits\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cost_estimator.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/agent_router.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/recovery_orchestrator.py`\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Document Status**: Complete\\n**Next Step**: System Architecture\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type