{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:58:19", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-168f0def-dc12-4248-91ad-3595f79c7e88', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015HWBczkUwiMJw94xXFkTzD', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'UI Enhancements Implementation', 'description': 'Implement all features specified in ui_enhancements_requirements.md using TDD methodology'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015HWBczkUwiMJw94xXFkTzD', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "3241c771", "message": "Created project: UI Enhancements Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "3241c771", "project_name": "UI Enhancements Implementation", "description": "Implement all features specified in ui_enhancements_requirements.md using TDD methodology", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:13.830822", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:13.830822", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:58:13.830822", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'UI Enhancements Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012mi1uNNqt1JLfDxhcC4GqH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012mi1uNNqt1JLfDxhcC4GqH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI Enhancement - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the existing Ensemble UI with several user experience improvements to better track agent hierarchies, manage completed items, and provide better visibility into system metrics and code changes.\\n\\n## Project Name\\nensemble-ui-enhancements\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Add question linking from agent hierarchy to original spawning question\\n2. Implement completed items section with collapsible/hideable functionality\\n3. Add two-word subject summaries to differentiate agent hierarchies at a glance\\n4. Improve layout: enlarge problem description section, make activity feed narrower\\n5. Make current agent tasks and activity feed collapsible\\n6. Add new metrics pane showing current models in use and code deltas\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n**Feature 1: Agent Hierarchy Question Links**\\n- Add links in the AgentHierarchyTree component to the question that spawned each hierarchy\\n- Ensure links scroll or navigate to the relevant question in the UI\\n- Visual indication that hierarchy is linked to a question\\n\\n**Feature 2: Completed Items Management**\\n- Create a \\"Completed\\" section for finished tasks/agents\\n- Make the completed section collapsible or hideable (either approach acceptable)\\n- Move completed items from active view to completed section automatically\\n- Maintain ability to view completed item details when needed\\n\\n**Feature 3: Agent Hierarchy Differentiation**\\n- Generate two-word subject summaries for each agent hierarchy\\n- Display summary prominently in hierarchy view\\n- Summaries should be derived from task/problem description\\n- Make hierarchies easily distinguishable at a glance\\n\\n**Feature 4: Layout Improvements**\\n- Enlarge problem description textarea (more height and width)\\n- Reduce width of activity feed column\\n- Redistribute space: more to problem input, less to activity feed\\n- Maintain responsive design principles\\n\\n**Feature 5: Collapsible Sections**\\n- Make \\"Current Agent Tasks\\" pane collapsible\\n- Make \\"Activity Feed\\" pane collapsible\\n- Preserve collapse state during updates\\n- Add clear visual indicators for collapsed/expanded state\\n\\n**Feature 6: Metrics Pane**\\n- New pane showing current models in use (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus counts)\\n- Display code delta metrics (lines added/removed, files changed)\\n- Real-time updates matching existing polling mechanism\\n- Clean, readable presentation of metrics\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Backend API changes (unless absolutely necessary for metrics)\\n- Authentication or user management\\n- Historical metrics or charting\\n- Export functionality for metrics\\n- Custom theme or color scheme changes beyond necessary UI adjustments\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing React + Bootstrap UI framework\\n- Must work with existing API endpoints in `/services/api.js`\\n- Must maintain current polling mechanism (configurable intervals)\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n- Responsive design must be preserved\\n\\n## Current Architecture Context\\n- **Frontend**: React with React-Bootstrap components\\n- **State Management**: Local React state with hooks\\n- **API Communication**: REST API via services/api.js\\n- **Polling**: 500ms-2s configurable intervals\\n- **Layout**: 3-column Bootstrap grid (currently 3-5-4 split)\\n\\n## Detailed Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Agent Hierarchy Question Links\\n- Add `question_id` or reference tracking to hierarchy data\\n- Implement clickable links in AgentHierarchyTree component\\n- Link should scroll to or highlight associated question\\n- Visual connection (icon, color coding) between hierarchy and question\\n\\n### 2. Completed Items Section\\n- Filter agents/tasks by status === \'completed\'\\n- Create separate collapsible section below active items\\n- Add \\"Show/Hide Completed\\" toggle button or collapse icon\\n- Maintain count badge showing number of completed items\\n- Default state: collapsed/hidden to reduce clutter\\n\\n### 3. Two-Word Subject Summaries\\n- Generate from problem description or task name\\n- Algorithm: extract key nouns/verbs, create 2-word summary\\n- Examples: \\"UI Enhancement\\", \\"API Integration\\", \\"Bug Fix\\"\\n- Display next to hierarchy title or as subtitle\\n- Make it prominent for quick scanning\\n\\n### 4. Layout Adjustments\\n**Current**: Col md={3} | md={5} | md={4}\\n**Proposed**: Col md={4} | md={4} | md={4} (or 4-3-5)\\n- Problem description textarea: increase rows from 4 to 6-8\\n- Make problem description card wider within its column\\n- Activity feed column should be narrower\\n- Ensure all content remains accessible and readable\\n\\n### 5. Collapsible Sections Implementation\\n- Use Bootstrap Collapse component or custom implementation\\n- Add chevron icons to indicate expand/collapse state\\n- Store collapse state in component state (preserve during re-renders)\\n- Smooth transitions when collapsing/expanding\\n- Sections affected:\\n  - Current Agent Tasks card\\n  - Activity Feed card\\n\\n### 6. Metrics Pane\\n**New section showing:**\\n- **Models in Use**:\\n  - Count of agents using Haiku\\n  - Count of agents using Sonnet\\n  - Count of agents using Opus\\n- **Code Delta Metrics**:\\n  - Total lines added (if available from API)\\n  - Total lines removed (if available from API)\\n  - Files changed count\\n  - Last updated timestamp\\n  \\n**Implementation**:\\n- Add new API endpoint or extend existing status endpoint\\n- Poll at same interval as other data\\n- Display in card format (similar to existing cards)\\n- Consider placement: below current tasks or as separate column section\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Question Links**: Click on hierarchy item navigates/scrolls to associated question\\n2. **Completed Section**: Completed items move to separate collapsible section automatically\\n3. **Summaries**: Each hierarchy displays clear 2-word summary\\n4. **Layout**: Problem description is noticeably larger, activity feed narrower but still functional\\n5. **Collapsible**: Both Current Tasks and Activity Feed can be collapsed/expanded smoothly\\n6. **Metrics**: New pane displays real-time model usage and code metrics\\n7. **No Regressions**: All existing functionality continues to work\\n8. **Performance**: UI remains responsive with no noticeable lag\\n9. **Tests**: New components have unit tests, existing tests still pass\\n\\n## Implementation Assumptions\\n- **Backend Support**: Assume backend can provide necessary data (question IDs, metrics)\\n  - If metrics not available from backend, display mock/placeholder with note\\n- **Summary Generation**: Frontend-based text processing acceptable for subject summaries\\n- **Persistence**: Collapse states don\'t need to persist across page reloads\\n- **Browser Support**: Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge - latest versions)\\n\\n## API Endpoint Assumptions\\nAssume these are available or can be added:\\n- Existing endpoints already provide sufficient data for features 1-5\\n- May need new endpoint for metrics: `GET /api/metrics` returning:\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\"models\\": {\\n      \\"haiku\\": 5,\\n      \\"sonnet\\": 3,\\n      \\"opus\\": 1\\n    },\\n    \\"code_delta\\": {\\n      \\"lines_added\\": 245,\\n      \\"lines_removed\\": 89,\\n      \\"files_changed\\": 12\\n    },\\n    \\"last_updated\\": \\"2024-01-11T02:56:00Z\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Updated React components:\\n   - AgentHierarchyTree.jsx (with question links)\\n   - App.jsx (layout changes, collapsible sections)\\n   - New MetricsPane.jsx component\\n   - Updated/new components for completed items management\\n2. Updated CSS/styling for layout changes\\n3. Unit tests for new components and modified functionality\\n4. Updated API service layer if new endpoints needed\\n5. README updates documenting new features\\n\\n## Future Considerations (Not in Current Scope)\\n- Persistent collapse state in localStorage\\n- Historical metrics charting\\n- Customizable column layouts\\n- Export metrics to CSV/JSON\\n- Advanced filtering for completed items\\n- Search functionality in hierarchies\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PkUKvGnVYEvfMqEdf5zmGo', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '3241c771', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements analysis complete. Found comprehensive UI enhancement requirements with 6 major features: question links, completed items management, two-word summaries, layout improvements, collapsible sections, and metrics pane. All requirements are well-defined and feasible.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PkUKvGnVYEvfMqEdf5zmGo', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 75.7%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Conducting systematic directory analysis using multiple commands to gather comprehensive data, 3) Creat...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all 