{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:58:49", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d75b3762-6d29-4df1-8b43-d514c66e617c', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md",\n  "project_name": "AI Provider Enhancement System",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TKDYg7buTP5fwv5iRj5ztR', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TKDYg7buTP5fwv5iRj5ztR', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# AI Provider Enhancement System - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project ID**: 3cd35d78\\n**Created**: 2026-01-13\\n**Status**: Planning\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Highest\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `provider_manager.py` - AI provider abstraction and detection system\\n2. `cli_provider.py` - CLI provider implementations for Claude and ChatGPT\\n3. Updated `runtime.py` - Integration with provider manager\\n4. Unit tests for provider detection and execution\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` is detected automatically\\n- [ ] CLI provider executes prompts using `claude --print` flag\\n- [ ] Graceful fallback to Anthropic API when CLI unavailable\\n- [ ] Provider success/failure metrics tracked in database\\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Existing runtime.py infrastructure\\n- Claude CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution cost tracking with dashboard integration.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `cost_estimator.py` - Pre-execution cost estimation based on task complexity\\n2. Enhanced `cost_calculator.py` - Extended with estimation capabilities\\n3. Updated `metrics.py` - Cost tracking fields and aggregation queries\\n4. Cost API endpoints for dashboard\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Pre-execution cost estimates available before spawning agents\\n- [ ] Estimates within 50% of actual costs\\n- [ ] Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- [ ] Cost fields added to agent_executions table\\n- [ ] API endpoints expose cost data to dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (provider tracking needed for CLI vs API cost differentiation)\\n- Existing cost_calculator.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Smart Agent Router\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium-High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement intelligent agent-task routing based on historical performance metrics.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `agent_router.py` - Performance analysis and routing recommendations\\n2. Updated agent execution flow to use router recommendations\\n3. Routing analytics API endpoints\\n4. Dashboard widget for routing explanations\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Agent recommendations based on historical performance from metrics.db\\n- [ ] Routing considers success rate (50%), cost efficiency (30%), speed (20%)\\n- [ ] Agent specialization bonuses applied (e.g., code_writer +10% for code tasks)\\n- [ ] Override capability for manual agent selection\\n- [ ] 10% improvement in overall success rate (measurable after deployment)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (cost data needed for cost efficiency calculations)\\n- Populated metrics.db with historical data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Project Recovery & Dashboard Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium\\n\\n### Objective\\nRestart 10 stalled projects and integrate all new features into the dashboard.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `recovery_orchestrator.py` - Project recovery logic\\n2. Recovery execution report\\n3. Dashboard integration for provider, cost, and routing features\\n4. Updated frontend components\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] All 10 stalled projects attempted for restart\\n- [ ] Recovery report generated with outcomes per project\\n- [ ] Independent error boundaries (one failure doesn\'t stop others)\\n- [ ] Dashboard shows provider usage, cost trends, routing info\\n- [ ] Provider success rates visible in dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 1-3 completed\\n- Access to project tracking system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone Summary\\n\\n| Milestone | Objective | Duration | Dependencies |\\n|-----------|-----------|----------|--------------|\\n| 1 | CLI Provider Integration | 2-3 days | None |\\n| 2 | Cost Estimation Module | 2-3 days | Milestone 1 |\\n| 3 | Smart Agent Router | 2-3 days | Milestone 2 |\\n| 4 | Project Recovery & Dashboard | 2-3 days | Milestones 1-3 |\\n\\n**Total Estimated Duration**: 8-12 days\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### TD1: Provider Selection Strategy\\n- **Decision**: CLI preferred over API when available\\n- **Rationale**: CLI tools use user\'s existing subscription, avoiding API costs\\n\\n### TD2: Cost Estimation Approach\\n- **Decision**: Use task complexity heuristics for output token estimation\\n- **Rationale**: More accurate than fixed estimates, calibrated to task types\\n\\n### TD3: Routing Algorithm Weights\\n- **Decision**: 50% success rate, 30% cost efficiency, 20% speed\\n- **Rationale**: Reliability most important, then cost, then speed\\n\\n### TD4: Recovery Sequence\\n- **Decision**: Sequential processing, not parallel\\n- **Rationale**: Easier debugging, independent error boundaries, API rate limits\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cost_estimator.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/agent_router.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/recovery_orchestrator.py`\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Document Status**: Complete\\n**Next Step**: System Architecture\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ACc3Q5wiH8KuTjJFXRWuhC', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# AI Provider Enhancement System - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### System Architecture Pattern: Modular Microservices with Event-Driven Design\n- Decoupled, extensible architecture focusing on provider flexibility\n- Event-driven communication between components\n- Microservices approach allows independent scaling and deployment\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ \n  - Rationale: Strong typing, excellent data processing, AI integration libraries\n- **Frameworks**: \n  - FastAPI for API layer (lightweight, async support)\n  - SQLAlchemy for database interactions\n  - Pydantic for data validation\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React 18 \n  - Rationale: Component-based, performance, rich ecosystem\n- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit\n  - For complex global state tracking of providers, costs, routing\n- **Charting**: Recharts for cost and performance visualizations\n\n### Database\n- **Primary Database**: PostgreSQL\n  - Rationale: ACID compliance, robust JSON support, advanced querying\n- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy with Alembic for migrations\n- **Key Collections**: \n  - `agent_executions`\n  - `provider_metrics`\n  - `project_tracking`\n\n### Infrastructure\n- **Containerization**: Docker\n- **Orchestration**: docker-compose for local, Kubernetes for production\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. Provider Management Service\n- **Responsibility**: Detect and manage AI provider interfaces\n- **Key Files**: \n  - `provider_manager.py`\n  - `cli_provider.py`\n- **Capabilities**:\n  - CLI tool detection\n  - Provider selection strategy\n  - Fallback mechanisms\n\n### 2. Cost Estimation Module\n- **Responsibility**: Pre and post-execution cost tracking\n- **Key Files**:\n  - `cost_estimator.py`\n  - `cost_calculator.py`\n- **Features**:\n  - Complexity-based estimation\n  - Historical cost analysis\n  - Per-project cost tracking\n\n### 3. Agent Router\n- **Responsibility**: Intelligent task routing\n- **Key Files**:\n  - `agent_router.py`\n- **Routing Criteria**:\n  - Success Rate (50%)\n  - Cost Efficiency (30%)\n  - Execution Speed (20%)\n  - Specialization Bonuses\n\n### 4. Recovery Orchestrator\n- **Responsibility**: Project restart and management\n- **Key Files**:\n  - `recovery_orchestrator.py`\n- **Features**:\n  - Sequential project recovery\n  - Independent error handling\n  - Comprehensive reporting\n\n## D. File/Directory Structure\n```\nensemble/\n│\n├── src/\n│   ├── runtime/\n│   │   └── agents/\n│   │       ├── provider_manager.py\n│   │       ├── cli_provider.py\n│   │       ├── cost_estimator.py\n│   │       ├── agent_router.py\n│   │       └── recovery_orchestrator.py\n│   │\n│   └── field/\n│       └── ensemble_ui/\n│           ├── backend/\n│           └── frontend/\n│\n├── tests/\n│   ├── unit/\n│   └── integration/\n│\n├── docs/\n└── deployment/\n    ├── docker/\n    └── kubernetes/\n```\n\n## E. Data Model\n\n### Agent Execution Tracking\n```sql\nTABLE agent_executions (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY,\n    agent_type VARCHAR,\n    provider VARCHAR,\n    status VARCHAR,\n    start_time TIMESTAMP,\n    end_time TIMESTAMP,\n    estimated_cost DECIMAL,\n    actual_cost DECIMAL,\n    success_rate FLOAT\n)\n```\n\n## F. API Design\n\n### Cost API Endpoints\n- `GET /api/costs/project/{project_id}`\n- `GET /api/costs/summary`\n- `GET /api/providers/metrics`\n\n### Authentication\n- JWT-based authentication\n- Role-based access control\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n\n### Local Development\n- Docker Compose\n- Hot reloading for backend/frontend\n- Isolated service containers\n\n### Production\n- Kubernetes Deployment\n- Horizontal Pod Autoscaling\n- Blue-Green Deployments\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Testing\n- pytest for backend\n- Jest for frontend components\n- 90%+ code coverage target\n\n### Integration Testing\n- End-to-end provider routing scenarios\n- Cost estimation accuracy validation\n- Recovery orchestration testing\n\n## I. Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: Monolithic Architecture\n- **Pros**: Simpler initial setup\n- **Cons**: Less scalable, harder to maintain\n- **Decision**: Rejected in favor of microservices\n\n### Alternative 2: Direct API Only\n- **Pros**: Fewer dependencies\n- **Cons**: Less flexible, higher cost\n- **Decision**: Rejected; CLI integration preferred\n\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\n\n1. **Provider Availability Risk**\n   - Mitigation: Robust fallback mechanisms\n   - Multi-provider support\n\n2. **Cost Estimation Accuracy**\n   - Mitigation: Machine learning model for estimation\n   - Continuous calibration\n\n3. **Performance Overhead**\n   - Mitigation: Lightweight implementations\n   - Caching strategies\n\n## K. Open Questions\n\n1. Preferred cloud provider for production\n2. Specific compliance requirements\n3. Expected scale of deployment\n\n## Conclusion\nThis architecture provides a flexible, scalable solution for AI provider management, with clear separation of concerns and extensible design.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ACc3Q5wiH8KuTjJFXRWuhC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025849.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025849.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
