{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:58:54", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e6b82507-3a57-41fa-81e4-71430561e8e5', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "UI Files 404 Error Fix"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CuQHmbmqjJysmisefKvCoQ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CuQHmbmqjJysmisefKvCoQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Files Endpoint 404 Error - Bug Fix Requirements\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nUsers are seeing 404 \\"Not Found\\" errors in the UI when the frontend attempts to fetch generated files from the backend API. The error message appears as:\\n\\n```\\n{\\"detail\\":\\"Not Found\\"}\\n```\\n\\nPreceded by a BOM character (`\\\\ufeff`), indicating potential encoding or response format issues.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n- **User Report**: \\"Seeing a bunch of these errors in the ui when pinging files UI\\"\\n- **Affected Endpoint**: `/api/activity/files`\\n- **Frontend Location**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/`\\n- **Backend Location**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/`\\n- **Output Directory**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/`\\n\\n## Technical Investigation Required\\n\\n### 1. Backend Status\\n- Verify backend server is running on expected port (8001)\\n- Check if endpoint registration is correct\\n- Validate endpoint handler function exists and is accessible\\n\\n### 2. Frontend API Calls\\n- Review `getGeneratedFiles()` function in `frontend/src/services/api.js`\\n- Verify correct URL construction and parameters\\n- Check polling interval and frequency (currently set to 1000ms in App.jsx)\\n\\n### 3. Potential Root Causes\\n- Backend server not running or crashed\\n- Endpoint URL mismatch between frontend and backend\\n- CORS configuration issues\\n- Activity tracker database connectivity problems\\n- Missing dependencies or import errors in backend\\n\\n## Files to Examine\\n\\n### Backend Files\\n1. `backend/main.py` - Main FastAPI application\\n   - Line 717: `@app.get(\\"/api/activity/files\\")` endpoint definition\\n   - Activity tracker integration\\n   - Error handling\\n\\n2. Backend runtime dependencies:\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Activity tracking system\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - AgentRuntime class\\n\\n### Frontend Files\\n1. `frontend/src/services/api.js` - API service layer\\n   - `getGeneratedFiles()` function\\n   - API_BASE_URL configuration\\n\\n2. `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Main application component\\n   - Polling logic for file updates\\n   - Error handling display\\n\\n3. `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx` - Files display component\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. Frontend polls `/api/activity/files` endpoint at configured interval\\n2. Backend returns JSON response with generated files:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"files\\": [...],\\n     \\"count\\": 0\\n   }\\n   ```\\n3. UI displays files in the \\"Generated Files\\" section without errors\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **No 404 errors** when frontend polls files endpoint\\n2. **Correct response format** - JSON without BOM characters\\n3. **Files displayed** in UI when agents generate outputs\\n4. **Error handling** - Graceful degradation if backend temporarily unavailable\\n5. **Logging** - Clear error messages in both frontend console and backend logs\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- **No breaking changes** to existing API contract\\n- **Maintain backwards compatibility** with current frontend implementation\\n- **Minimal code changes** - focus on fixing the specific 404 issue\\n- **Preserve existing functionality** - don\'t break other endpoints\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Adding new features to file display\\n- Redesigning the UI layout\\n- Changing polling architecture to WebSockets\\n- Performance optimization beyond fixing the bug\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Backend is intended to run on port 8001\\n- Frontend is configured to connect to localhost:8001\\n- Activity tracker database exists and is accessible at `~/.ensemble/metrics.db`\\n- All required Python dependencies are installed\\n\\n## Acceptance Tests\\n\\n1. **Backend health check**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/status` returns 200 OK\\n2. **Files endpoint test**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/activity/files` returns JSON (not 404)\\n3. **Frontend test**: Open UI in browser, verify no 404 errors in console for `/api/activity/files`\\n4. **Integration test**: Generate a file via agent execution, verify it appears in UI without errors\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Root cause analysis** - Document why 404 was occurring\\n2. **Code fixes** - Implement solution in backend/frontend as needed\\n3. **Verification** - Test all affected endpoints work correctly\\n4. **Documentation** - Update any relevant docs about endpoint usage\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'miles