{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:58:56", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-49dec424-7370-4bf1-8b2c-2824a0a38bbf', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "UI Enhancements Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CUS4qdVomMniL9aznLE6U5', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CUS4qdVomMniL9aznLE6U5', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI Enhancement - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the existing Ensemble UI with several user experience improvements to better track agent hierarchies, manage completed items, and provide better visibility into system metrics and code changes.\\n\\n## Project Name\\nensemble-ui-enhancements\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Add question linking from agent hierarchy to original spawning question\\n2. Implement completed items section with collapsible/hideable functionality\\n3. Add two-word subject summaries to differentiate agent hierarchies at a glance\\n4. Improve layout: enlarge problem description section, make activity feed narrower\\n5. Make current agent tasks and activity feed collapsible\\n6. Add new metrics pane showing current models in use and code deltas\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n**Feature 1: Agent Hierarchy Question Links**\\n- Add links in the AgentHierarchyTree component to the question that spawned each hierarchy\\n- Ensure links scroll or navigate to the relevant question in the UI\\n- Visual indication that hierarchy is linked to a question\\n\\n**Feature 2: Completed Items Management**\\n- Create a \\"Completed\\" section for finished tasks/agents\\n- Make the completed section collapsible or hideable (either approach acceptable)\\n- Move completed items from active view to completed section automatically\\n- Maintain ability to view completed item details when needed\\n\\n**Feature 3: Agent Hierarchy Differentiation**\\n- Generate two-word subject summaries for each agent hierarchy\\n- Display summary prominently in hierarchy view\\n- Summaries should be derived from task/problem description\\n- Make hierarchies easily distinguishable at a glance\\n\\n**Feature 4: Layout Improvements**\\n- Enlarge problem description textarea (more height and width)\\n- Reduce width of activity feed column\\n- Redistribute space: more to problem input, less to activity feed\\n- Maintain responsive design principles\\n\\n**Feature 5: Collapsible Sections**\\n- Make \\"Current Agent Tasks\\" pane collapsible\\n- Make \\"Activity Feed\\" pane collapsible\\n- Preserve collapse state during updates\\n- Add clear visual indicators for collapsed/expanded state\\n\\n**Feature 6: Metrics Pane**\\n- New pane showing current models in use (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus counts)\\n- Display code delta metrics (lines added/removed, files changed)\\n- Real-time updates matching existing polling mechanism\\n- Clean, readable presentation of metrics\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Backend API changes (unless absolutely necessary for metrics)\\n- Authentication or user management\\n- Historical metrics or charting\\n- Export functionality for metrics\\n- Custom theme or color scheme changes beyond necessary UI adjustments\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing React + Bootstrap UI framework\\n- Must work with existing API endpoints in `/services/api.js`\\n- Must maintain current polling mechanism (configurable intervals)\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n- Responsive design must be preserved\\n\\n## Current Architecture Context\\n- **Frontend**: React with React-Bootstrap components\\n- **State Management**: Local React state with hooks\\n- **API Communication**: REST API via services/api.js\\n- **Polling**: 500ms-2s configurable intervals\\n- **Layout**: 3-column Bootstrap grid (currently 3-5-4 split)\\n\\n## Detailed Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Agent Hierarchy Question Links\\n- Add `question_id` or reference tracking to hierarchy data\\n- Implement clickable links in AgentHierarchyTree component\\n- Link should scroll to or highlight associated question\\n- Visual connection (icon, color coding) between hierarchy and question\\n\\n### 2. Completed Items Section\\n- Filter agents/tasks by status === \'completed\'\\n- Create separate collapsible section below active items\\n- Add \\"Show/Hide Completed\\" toggle button or collapse icon\\n- Maintain count badge showing number of completed items\\n- Default state: collapsed/hidden to reduce clutter\\n\\n### 3. Two-Word Subject Summaries\\n- Generate from problem description or task name\\n- Algorithm: extract key nouns/verbs, create 2-word summary\\n- Examples: \\"UI Enhancement\\", \\"API Integration\\", \\"Bug Fix\\"\\n- Display next to hierarchy title or as subtitle\\n- Make it prominent for quick scanning\\n\\n### 4. Layout Adjustments\\n**Current**: Col md={3} | md={5} | md={4}\\n**Proposed**: Col md={4} | md={4} | md={4} (or 4-3-5)\\n- Problem description textarea: increase rows from 4 to 6-8\\n- Make problem description card wider within its column\\n- Activity feed column should be narrower\\n- Ensure all content remains accessible and readable\\n\\n### 5. Collapsible Sections Implementation\\n- Use Bootstrap Collapse component or custom implementation\\n- Add chevron icons to indicate expand/collapse state\\n- Store collapse state in component state (preserve during re-renders)\\n- Smooth transitions when collapsing/expanding\\n- Sections affected:\\n  - Current Agent Tasks card\\n  - Activity Feed card\\n\\n### 6. Metrics Pane\\n**New section showing:**\\n- **Models in Use**:\\n  - Count of agents using Haiku\\n  - Count of agents using Sonnet\\n  - Count of agents using Opus\\n- **Code Delta Metrics**:\\n  - Total lines added (if available from API)\\n  - Total lines removed (if available from API)\\n  - Files changed count\\n  - Last updated timestamp\\n  \\n**Implementation**:\\n- Add new API endpoint or extend existing status endpoint\\n- Poll at same interval as other data\\n- Display in card format (similar to existing cards)\\n- Consider placement: below current tasks or as separate column section\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Question Links**: Click on hierarchy item navigates/scrolls to associated question\\n2. **Completed Section**: Completed items move to separate collapsible section automatically\\n3. **Summaries**: Each hierarchy displays clear 2-word summary\\n4. **Layout**: Problem description is noticeably larger, activity feed narrower but still functional\\n5. **Collapsible**: Both Current Tasks and Activity Feed can be collapsed/expanded smoothly\\n6. **Metrics**: New pane displays real-time model usage and code metrics\\n7. **No Regressions**: All existing functionality continues to work\\n8. **Performance**: UI remains responsive with no noticeable lag\\n9. **Tests**: New components have unit tests, existing tests still pass\\n\\n## Implementation Assumptions\\n- **Backend Support**: Assume backend can provide necessary data (question IDs, metrics)\\n  - If metrics not available from backend, display mock/placeholder with note\\n- **Summary Generation**: Frontend-based text processing acceptable for subject summaries\\n- **Persistence**: Collapse states don\'t need to persist across page reloads\\n- **Browser Support**: Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge - latest versions)\\n\\n## API Endpoint Assumptions\\nAssume these are available or can be added:\\n- Existing endpoints already provide sufficient data for features 1-5\\n- May need new endpoint for metrics: `GET /api/metrics` returning:\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\"models\\": {\\n      \\"haiku\\": 5,\\n      \\"sonnet\\": 3,\\n      \\"opus\\": 1\\n    },\\n    \\"code_delta\\": {\\n      \\"lines_added\\": 245,\\n      \\"lines_removed\\": 89,\\n      \\"files_changed\\": 12\\n    },\\n    \\"last_updated\\": \\"2024-01-11T02:56:00Z\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Updated React components:\\n   - AgentHierarchyTree.jsx (with question links)\\n   - App.jsx (layout changes, collapsible sections)\\n   - New MetricsPane.jsx component\\n   - Updated/new components for completed items management\\n2. Updated CSS/styling for layout changes\\n3. Unit tests for new components and modified functionality\\n4. Updated API service layer if new endpoints needed\\n5. README updates documenting new features\\n\\n## Future Considerations (Not in Current Scope)\\n- Persistent collapse state in localStorage\\n- Historical metrics charting\\n- Customizable column layouts\\n- Export metrics to CSV/JSON\\n- Advanced filtering for completed items\\n- Search functionality in hierarchies\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Vx387itHY8nfp81KjMGfmf', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# UI Enhancements Implementation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project Name**: UI Enhancements Implementation\n**Duration Estimate**: 3-4 milestones over 1-2 weeks\n**Team**: Development Manager + System Architect + Frontend/Backend/Test Coordinators + TDD Coordinator\n\n## Milestone 1: Core UI Structure & Layout\n**Duration**: 3-5 days\n**Objective**: Establish foundation layout improvements and collapsible sections\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Layout restructuring (problem description enlargement, activity feed narrowing)\n2. Collapsible sections for Current Agent Tasks and Activity Feed\n3. Basic component structure for completed items section\n4. Updated responsive design\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Problem description textarea expanded (6-8 rows, wider)\n- Activity feed column narrower but functional\n- Current Agent Tasks pane can be collapsed/expanded\n- Activity Feed pane can be collapsed/expanded\n- Collapse state preserved during re-renders\n- All existing functionality remains intact\n- Responsive design maintained\n\n### Dependencies:\n- None (foundational work)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Agent Hierarchy Enhancements\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\n**Objective**: Implement question linking and two-word summaries for agent hierarchies\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Question linking functionality in AgentHierarchyTree\n2. Two-word subject summary generation and display\n3. Visual indicators for hierarchy-question connections\n4. Navigation/scrolling to linked questions\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Each hierarchy shows clear 2-word summary\n- Clicking hierarchy items navigates/scrolls to associated question\n- Visual connection between hierarchy and question is clear\n- Summary generation works reliably from task descriptions\n- No performance impact on hierarchy rendering\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestone 1 (layout foundation)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Completed Items & Metrics\n**Duration**: 3-4 days\n**Objective**: Complete the completed items management system and add metrics pane\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Completed items section with collapse/hide functionality\n2. Automatic movement of completed items from active view\n3. Metrics pane showing model usage and code deltas\n4. API integration for metrics (or mock implementation)\n5. Real-time metrics updates\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Completed items automatically move to separate collapsible section\n- Metrics pane displays model usage counts (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus)\n- Code delta metrics shown (lines added/removed, files changed)\n- Metrics update with same polling mechanism as other data\n- Completed section defaults to collapsed\n- Count badge shows number of completed items\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestone 2 (hierarchy work complete)\n- Backend API endpoint for metrics (or mock implementation)\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment & Mitigation\n\n### High Risk Items:\n1. **Metrics API availability**: Backend may not have metrics endpoint\n   - **Mitigation**: Implement mock/placeholder metrics first, note for future backend work\n\n2. **Layout responsiveness**: Changes might break mobile/tablet views\n   - **Mitigation**: Test on multiple screen sizes, use Bootstrap grid properly\n\n3. **Performance with many hierarchies**: Summaries and links might slow rendering\n   - **Mitigation**: Use memoization, efficient algorithms for summary generation\n\n### Medium Risk Items:\n1. **Question linking complexity**: May need complex DOM manipulation for scrolling\n   - **Mitigation**: Use React refs and standard scroll APIs\n\n2. **State management for collapse**: Multiple collapsible sections could complicate state\n   - **Mitigation**: Use proper React state patterns, consider context if needed\n\n## Resource Allocation\n- **Frontend Development**: 70% of effort\n- **Backend Integration**: 20% of effort\n- **Testing & QA**: 10% of effort\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. All 6 features implemented and functional\n2. No regressions in existing functionality\n3. Performance remains acceptable (no >100ms delays)\n4. Unit test coverage >80% for new components\n5. Code review approval from TDD process\n\n## Post-Implementation Tasks\n1. Documentation updates\n2. User acceptance testing\n3. Performance monitoring\n4. Future enhancement planning\n\n---\n\n*This milestone plan provides a logical progression from foundational changes to enhanced features, minimizing risk and ensuring stable incremental delivery.*'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Vx387itHY8nfp81KjMGfmf', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025853.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025853.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FpaxYPCvcJypcYSP6UQLU2', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'UI Enhancements Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FpaxYPCvcJypcYSP6UQLU2', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for 