{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8ae48f9d-61f1-4dd6-b6f7-c4b574f2d223', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Smart Task Decomposition System",\n  "project_id": "7f917a6b",\n  "task_id": "dab5e173"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01U2jTJYo3k2VUNkEUYc4hGa', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01U2jTJYo3k2VUNkEUYc4hGa', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nImplement a comprehensive Task Decomposition Engine for Ensemble AI that analyzes complex user requests, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and presents execution plans for user approval.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine\\n**Objective**: Build the core decomposition engine with task analysis and dependency graph generation.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_engine.py` - Core engine with:\\n   - Pydantic data models (TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate, AllocationPlan, Schedule)\\n   - `TaskDecompositionEngine` class with all core methods\\n   - NetworkX-based DAG generation and validation\\n   - Resource estimation and allocation optimization\\n   - Execution schedule generation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Can analyze task complexity and domain\\n- Generates valid DAGs (no cycles)\\n- Produces resource estimates with cost calculations\\n- Creates parallel execution waves\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Learning Module\\n**Objective**: Build the learning module for continuous improvement of estimates.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_learner.py` - Learning module with:\\n   - `DecompositionLearner` class\\n   - Execution recording and history storage\\n   - Estimate improvement based on historical data\\n   - Accuracy metrics tracking\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Records execution outcomes\\n- Improves estimates over time\\n- Provides accuracy metrics\\n- Suggests improvements based on patterns\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (uses DecompositionPlan models)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Executive Director Integration\\n**Objective**: Integrate decomposition engine into Executive Director workflow.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `leadership/executive_director.md` with:\\n   - New decomposition workflow\\n   - Extended output format with `decomposition_plan` field\\n   - User approval flow for plans\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Executive Director uses decomposition before spawning agents\\n- Output includes decomposition plan\\n- Supports plan approval workflow\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 4: API Endpoints\\n**Objective**: Add backend API endpoints for decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py` with:\\n   - `POST /api/decompose` - Decompose user request\\n   - `POST /api/approve-plan` - Accept/reject/modify plans\\n   - `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Historical accuracy\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All endpoints functional\\n- Proper error handling\\n- Integration with decomposition engine\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 5: Frontend Visualization\\n**Objective**: Build React component for task decomposition visualization.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx` with:\\n   - Mermaid diagram rendering\\n   - Resource estimates display\\n   - Execution wave visualization\\n   - Agent assignment table\\n   - Approve/Reject/Modify buttons\\n   - Plan modification interface\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Renders dependency graph with Mermaid\\n- Displays resource estimates\\n- Action buttons work correctly\\n- Responsive UI\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 4 (needs API endpoints)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 6: Test Suite\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing for all decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `tests/test_decomposition.py` with:\\n   - Unit tests for each method\\n   - Integration tests for full flow\\n   - Graph validity tests\\n   - Benchmark tests (simple, medium, complex)\\n   - Learning accuracy tests\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All unit tests pass\\n- Integration tests cover full workflow\\n- DAG validity verified\\n- Performance benchmarks documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2, 4\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 7: Documentation\\n**Objective**: Complete documentation for the decomposition engine.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md` with:\\n   - Architecture overview\\n   - Usage examples\\n   - API reference\\n   - Configuration options\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Clear architecture explanation\\n- Working code examples\\n- Complete API documentation\\n- Configuration fully documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Execution Order\\n1. Milestone 1 (Core Engine) - Foundation\\n2. Milestone 2 (Learning Module) - Builds on engine\\n3. Milestones 3, 4 (Integration + API) - Can run in parallel\\n4. Milestone 5 (Frontend) - Needs API\\n5. Milestone 6 (Tests) - Needs all code\\n6. Milestone 7 (Documentation) - Final\\n\\n## Estimated Timeline\\n- Milestones 1-2: Core implementation\\n- Milestones 3-5: Integration and UI\\n- Milestones 6-7: Quality and documentation\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n- **Medium Risk**: NetworkX/PuLP integration complexity\\n- **Low Risk**: Standard patterns for API/UI\\n- **Mitigation**: Use existing project patterns, fallback to simpler algorithms if needed\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01P4DvRovccG2QqKTysf6wgW', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Smart Task Decomposition System - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### System Purpose\nA sophisticated task decomposition engine that breaks down complex user requests into executable, optimized task plans with intelligent resource allocation and learning capabilities.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n- **Architectural Style**: Microservices with Event-Driven Architecture\n- **Primary Pattern**: Hexagonal (Ports and Adapters) Architecture\n- **Key Principles**: Modularity, Extensibility, Observability\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.11+\n- **Core Frameworks**:\n  - FastAPI (Web Framework)\n  - Pydantic (Data Validation)\n  - NetworkX (Graph Operations)\n  - PuLP (Optimization Calculations)\n- **Machine Learning**:\n  - scikit-learn (Learning & Predictions)\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React 18 with TypeScript\n- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit\n- **Visualization**: Mermaid.js (Dependency Graphs)\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS\n\n### Data & Persistence\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL 14\n- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy \n- **Migrations**: Alembic\n- **Caching**: Redis\n\n### Infrastructure\n- **Containerization**: Docker\n- **Orchestration**: Docker Compose (Development), Kubernetes (Production)\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\n- **Monitoring**: Prometheus + Grafana\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. Decomposition Engine (`decomposition_engine.py`)\n- **Responsibilities**:\n  - Analyze task complexity\n  - Generate dependency graphs\n  - Estimate resource requirements\n  - Create execution schedules\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `analyze_task()`\n  - `generate_dependency_graph()`\n  - `estimate_resources()`\n  - `create_execution_plan()`\n\n### 2. Learning Module (`decomposition_learner.py`)\n- **Responsibilities**:\n  - Record execution histories\n  - Improve future estimates\n  - Track accuracy metrics\n- **Key Methods**:\n  - `record_execution()`\n  - `update_estimates()`\n  - `calculate_accuracy()`\n\n### 3. API Layer (`main.py`)\n- **Endpoints**:\n  - `POST /api/decompose` - Initiate task decomposition\n  - `POST /api/approve-plan` - Validate and confirm plans\n  - `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Retrieve past decompositions\n\n### 4. Frontend Components\n- `TaskDecompositionViewer`\n- `PlanApprovalModal`\n- `ResourceEstimateDisplay`\n- `ExecutionWaveVisualizer`\n\n## D. Data Flow\n```\nUser Request \n→ Decomposition Engine \n→ Learning Module (Optional Refinement) \n→ Generate Dependency Graph \n→ Resource Estimation \n→ Execution Plan \n→ User Approval \n→ Execute/Modify\n```\n\n## E. File/Directory Structure\n```\nsmart_task_decomposition/\n│\n├── src/\n│   ├── runtime/\n│   │   ├── agents/\n│   │   │   ├── decomposition_engine.py\n│   │   │   └── decomposition_learner.py\n│   │   └── models/\n│   │       └── task_models.py\n│   │\n│   ├── field/\n│   │   └── ensemble_ui/\n│   │       ├── backend/\n│   │       │   └── main.py\n│   │       └── frontend/\n│   │           └── src/\n│   │               └── components/\n│   │                   └── TaskDecompositionViewer.tsx\n│   │\n│   └── tests/\n│       └── test_decomposition.py\n│\n├── docs/\n│   └── TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md\n│\n└── deployment/\n    ├── docker-compose.yml\n    └── kubernetes/\n```\n\n## F. Data Model\n\n### Key Models\n- `TaskAnalysis`: Detailed task breakdown\n- `SubTask`: Individual task components\n- `DecompositionPlan`: Complete execution strategy\n- `ResourceEstimate`: Computational & time requirements\n- `ExecutionSchedule`: Parallel task waves\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n- **Development**: Docker Compose with hot reloading\n- **Production**: Kubernetes with Helm charts\n- **Scaling**: Horizontal pod autoscaling\n- **Zero-Downtime Deployments**: Rolling updates\n\n## H. Testing Approach\n- **Unit Testing**: pytest for backend\n- **Integration Testing**: Full workflow simulations\n- **Performance Testing**: Benchmarks with various complexity levels\n- **Coverage Target**: 90%+ code coverage\n\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risks\n1. **Complex Graph Generation**\n   - *Mitigation*: Fallback to simpler algorithms\n   - *Approach*: Implement multiple graph generation strategies\n\n2. **Estimate Accuracy**\n   - *Mitigation*: Continuous learning module\n   - *Approach*: Track historical performance, implement adaptive estimation\n\n3. **Performance Bottlenecks**\n   - *Mitigation*: Caching, asynchronous processing\n   - *Approach*: Redis caching, task queue with Celery\n\n## J. Open Questions\n- Performance implications of learning module\n- Exact complexity scoring mechanism\n- User experience for plan modification\n\n## K. Decision Rationale\n- Chosen architecture optimizes for:\n  - Modularity\n  - Extensibility\n  - Observable performance\n  - Continuous improvement\n\n**Recommended Next Steps**:\n1. Validate architecture with stakeholders\n2. Prototype core decomposition engine\n3. Build MVP with minimal viable features'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01P4DvRovccG2QqKTysf6wgW', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025905.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025905.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
