n/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/`\\n- **Output Directory**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/`\\n\\n## Technical Investigation Required\\n\\n### 1. Backend Status\\n- Verify backend server is running on expected port (8001)\\n- Check if endpoint registration is correct\\n- Validate endpoint handler function exists and is accessible\\n\\n### 2. Frontend API Calls\\n- Review `getGeneratedFiles()` function in `frontend/src/services/api.js`\\n- Verify correct URL construction and parameters\\n- Check polling interval and frequency (currently set to 1000ms in App.jsx)\\n\\n### 3. Potential Root Causes\\n- Backend server not running or crashed\\n- Endpoint URL mismatch between frontend and backend\\n- CORS configuration issues\\n- Activity tracker database connectivity problems\\n- Missing dependencies or import errors in backend\\n\\n## Files to Examine\\n\\n### Backend Files\\n1. `backend/main.py` - Main FastAPI application\\n   - Line 717: `@app.get(\\"/api/activity/files\\")` endpoint definition\\n   - Activity tracker integration\\n   - Error handling\\n\\n2. Backend runtime dependencies:\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Activity tracking system\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - AgentRuntime class\\n\\n### Frontend Files\\n1. `frontend/src/services/api.js` - API service layer\\n   - `getGeneratedFiles()` function\\n   - API_BASE_URL configuration\\n\\n2. `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Main application component\\n   - Polling logic for file updates\\n   - Error handling display\\n\\n3. `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx` - Files display component\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. Frontend polls `/api/activity/files` endpoint at configured interval\\n2. Backend returns JSON response with generated files:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"files\\": [...],\\n     \\"count\\": 0\\n   }\\n   ```\\n3. UI displays files in the \\"Generated Files\\" section without errors\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **No 404 errors** when frontend polls files endpoint\\n2. **Correct response format** - JSON without BOM characters\\n3. **Files displayed** in UI when agents generate outputs\\n4. **Error handling** - Graceful degradation if backend temporarily unavailable\\n5. **Logging** - Clear error messages in both frontend console and backend logs\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- **No breaking changes** to existing API contract\\n- **Maintain backwards compatibility** with current frontend implementation\\n- **Minimal code changes** - focus on fixing the specific 404 issue\\n- **Preserve existing functionality** - don\'t break other endpoints\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Adding new features to file display\\n- Redesigning the UI layout\\n- Changing polling architecture to WebSockets\\n- Performance optimization beyond fixing the bug\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Backend is intended to run on port 8001\\n- Frontend is configured to connect to localhost:8001\\n- Activity tracker database exists and is accessible at `~/.ensemble/metrics.db`\\n- All required Python dependencies are installed\\n\\n## Acceptance Tests\\n\\n1. **Backend health check**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/status` returns 200 OK\\n2. **Files endpoint test**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/activity/files` returns JSON (not 404)\\n3. **Frontend test**: Open UI in browser, verify no 404 errors in console for `/api/activity/files`\\n4. **Integration test**: Generate a file via agent execution, verify it appears in UI without errors\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Root cause analysis** - Document why 404 was occurring\\n2. **Code fixes** - Implement solution in backend/frontend as needed\\n3. **Verification** - Test all affected endpoints work correctly\\n4. **Documentation** - Update any relevant docs about endpoint usage\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01J6A5zQ9qzcSeu5Gw1dR8LD', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: UI Files 404 Error Fix\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Problem Space\n- 404 errors when fetching generated files from `/api/activity/files` endpoint\n- Potential issues with backend endpoint registration, response handling, or frontend API calls\n\n### Architectural Goal\nCreate a robust, minimal-change solution to resolve 404 errors while maintaining existing system architecture and API contract.\n\n## 2. Tech Stack Analysis\n- **Backend**: FastAPI (Python)\n- **Frontend**: React.js\n- **Communication**: REST API\n- **Database**: SQLite (activity tracker metrics database)\n\n## 3. Proposed Solution Components\n\n### 3.1 Backend Modifications\n1. **Endpoint Validation**\n   - Confirm `/api/activity/files` endpoint is correctly registered\n   - Add explicit error handling in endpoint function\n   - Implement proper dependency injection for activity tracker\n\n**Code Sketch (main.py)**:\n```python\n@app.get("/api/activity/files")\nasync def get_generated_files(\n    activity_tracker: ActivityTracker = Depends(get_activity_tracker)\n):\n    try:\n        files = activity_tracker.get_generated_files()\n        return {\n            "files": files,\n            "count": len(files)\n        }\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f"Error fetching files: {e}")\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=500, \n            detail="Unable to retrieve generated files"\n        )\n```\n\n### 3.2 Frontend Modifications\n1. **API Service Resilience**\n   - Add error interceptors\n   - Implement retry logic\n   - Graceful error handling\n\n**Code Sketch (api.js)**:\n```javascript\nasync function getGeneratedFiles() {\n    try {\n        const response = await axios.get(\'/api/activity/files\', {\n            timeout: 5000,\n            retry: 3,\n            retryDelay: 1000\n        });\n        return response.data.files;\n    } catch (error) {\n        logger.error(\'File fetch error\', error);\n        return [];  // Graceful fallback\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## 4. Error Handling Strategy\n- **Backend**: \n  - Catch potential exceptions\n  - Return structured error responses\n  - Log detailed error information\n- **Frontend**: \n  - Implement retry mechanism\n  - Provide user-friendly error messages\n  - Fallback to empty state if retrieval fails\n\n## 5. Root Cause Hypotheses\n1. Potential BOM character causing parsing issues\n2. Incorrect endpoint registration\n3. Database connection problems\n4. Dependency injection errors\n\n## 6. Verification Approach\n1. Unit test endpoint handler\n2. Integration test API flow\n3. Frontend component testing\n4. Manual browser testing\n\n## 7. Risks and Mitigations\n- **Risk**: Introducing new bugs\n  - **Mitigation**: Comprehensive testing, minimal code changes\n- **Risk**: Performance degradation\n  - **Mitigation**: Implement efficient error handling, avoid heavy retry logic\n\n## 8. Implementation Steps\n1. Update backend endpoint handler\n2. Modify frontend API service\n3. Add logging and error tracking\n4. Comprehensive testing\n5. Gradual rollout and monitoring\n\n## 9. Open Questions\n- Confirm exact nature of BOM character issue\n- Verify current activity tracker implementation\n\n## 10. Out of Scope\n- Major refactoring\n- WebSocket implementation\n- UI redesign\n\n## Recommended Next Actions\n1. Reproduce 404 error in controlled environment\n2. Validate activity tracker database connection\n3. Implement proposed changes\n4. Conduct thorough regression testing'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01J6A5zQ9qzcSeu5Gw1dR8LD', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025913.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025913.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and w