{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:18", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-fcb8cf0a-7a8f-4b78-87cd-ff622318a4c4', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "focus": "Analyze current ensemble system architecture and design architecture for the top 3 improvements: real-time progress streaming, error recovery & context preservation, and performance analytics with adaptive optimization"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SF2W9UFnMmpPUVbGuy9Vru', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SF2W9UFnMmpPUVbGuy9Vru', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent System Analysis & Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nThis document analyzes the Ensemble multi-agent system architecture and identifies the top 3 improvements that would make agents more effective. The analysis is based on reviewing the codebase, agent definitions, and system architecture.\\n\\n## Project Vision\\n\\nAnalyze the ensemble agent system to identify and implement the three most impactful improvements that will enhance agent effectiveness, reduce coordination failures, and improve overall system reliability.\\n\\n## Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Architecture Overview\\n- **Agent Hierarchy**: 4 tiers (Leadership \\u2192 Coordinators \\u2192 Developers/Testers \\u2192 Writers)\\n- **Total Agents**: 16 agents (consolidated from 23, 30% reduction)\\n- **Core Technology**: Anthropic Claude API with hierarchical delegation\\n- **Key Features**: TDD workflow, permission system, state persistence\\n\\n### Identified Issues\\n\\nAfter analyzing the codebase and agent definitions, the following problems were identified:\\n\\n#### 1. **Lack of Real-Time Progress Feedback**\\n- **Problem**: Agents execute in background threads without granular progress updates\\n- **Impact**: Users don\'t know what agents are doing, causing uncertainty about system status\\n- **Evidence**: \\n  - `main.py` uses background threads for execution (line 79)\\n  - WebSocket broadcasts only top-level status changes\\n  - No intermediate progress reporting during long-running agent operations\\n  - No visibility into which sub-agents are currently active\\n\\n#### 2. **Inadequate Error Recovery & Context Preservation**\\n- **Problem**: When agents fail, there\'s no automatic retry logic or context preservation for resume\\n- **Impact**: Single failures cascade, wasting tokens and requiring manual intervention\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - State persistence exists (`state.py`) but resume logic is incomplete (line 64 in `runtime.py`: \\"Full resume with conversation history would need message reconstruction\\")\\n  - No retry logic in `runtime.py` when tool execution fails\\n  - Failed spawns don\'t preserve parent agent context for debugging\\n  - Agent state checkpoints exist but aren\'t used for automatic recovery\\n\\n#### 3. **Missing Agent Performance Metrics & Feedback Loops**\\n- **Problem**: No tracking of agent effectiveness, token usage, or success rates\\n- **Impact**: Can\'t identify which agents need improvement or optimization\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - No analytics collection in `AgentRuntime`\\n  - No metrics on spawn success/failure rates\\n  - No token usage tracking per agent type\\n  - No performance comparison between model tiers\\n  - README acknowledges this gap: \\"Phase 3: Self-Improvement\\" includes \\"Agent performance analytics\\"\\n\\n### Additional Observations\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: Strong permission system, clear hierarchy, rogue agent prevention working well\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: TDD workflow is well-designed\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Model selection is static (could be adaptive based on task success)\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Agent definitions in markdown could benefit from validation schema\\n\\n## Top 3 Improvements (Prioritized)\\n\\n### Improvement #1: Real-Time Agent Progress Streaming \\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: High (dramatically improves user experience)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement granular progress tracking and streaming for agent execution, allowing users to see:\\n- Current agent activity (which agent is thinking/executing)\\n- Tool invocations in real-time\\n- Sub-agent spawn events\\n- Iteration progress (current/max)\\n- Streaming responses from Claude API\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Enhance `AgentRuntime` to emit progress events during execution\\n2. Add event bus or callback system for progress notifications\\n3. Update WebSocket handler to stream progress events to frontend\\n4. Add progress tracking to spawned agent execution\\n5. Include tool execution progress (start/complete/fail)\\n6. Show model selection decisions in progress feed\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Users can see which agent is active at any moment\\n- Tool invocations appear in real-time\\n- Spawn events are visible with parent-child relationships\\n- WebSocket clients receive progress updates < 500ms after events\\n- No performance degradation (< 5% overhead)\\n\\n### Improvement #2: Automatic Error Recovery & Context Preservation\\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: High  \\n**Impact**: High (reduces wasted tokens, improves reliability)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement intelligent error recovery with automatic retries and full context preservation for resume after failures.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Complete state manager resume functionality (message reconstruction)\\n2. Add retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\\n3. Implement context preservation for spawned agents (parent context + partial results)\\n4. Add automatic checkpoint validation and rollback\\n5. Create error classification system (retryable vs. fatal)\\n6. Preserve tool execution results across retries\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Agents can resume from last checkpoint after crashes\\n- Transient API errors (rate limits, timeouts) trigger automatic retry\\n- Failed spawns preserve parent agent state for debugging\\n- Context includes: conversation history, tool results, spawned agent data\\n- Recovery success rate > 80% for retryable errors\\n- Zero token waste on successful recovery (resume from checkpoint)\\n\\n### Improvement #3: Agent Performance Analytics & Adaptive Optimization\\n**Priority**: MEDIUM  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: Medium-High (enables continuous improvement)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement comprehensive analytics tracking for agent performance with adaptive model selection based on historical success rates.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Track metrics per agent instance:\\n   - Token usage (input/output)\\n   - Execution time\\n   - Success/failure rates\\n   - Iteration count vs. max iterations\\n   - Tool invocation patterns\\n2. Aggregate metrics by agent type and model tier\\n3. Create analytics dashboard endpoint for reporting\\n4. Implement adaptive model selection:\\n   - Start with budget tier default\\n   - Upgrade model if agent fails repeatedly\\n   - Downgrade model if agent consistently succeeds quickly\\n5. Add performance comparison reports (model A vs. model B for same task)\\n6. Export metrics for analysis (JSON, CSV)\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- All agent executions tracked with complete metrics\\n- Analytics API returns per-agent and aggregate statistics\\n- Adaptive model selection improves success rate by 15%+\\n- Token usage optimization reduces costs by 10%+\\n- Reports identify underperforming agents for refinement\\n- Metrics persist across system restarts\\n\\n## Out of Scope (For This Phase)\\n\\nThe following are important but not in the top 3:\\n- Enhanced TDD workflow validation\\n- File exploration agents\\n- Multi-user support\\n- Agent definition schema validation\\n- Performance profiling tools\\n- Cost prediction before execution\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Must maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent definitions\\n2. **Must not break permission system** (can_write_code, can_write_tests enforcement)\\n3. **Must not increase API costs** by more than 10%\\n4. **Must support concurrent agent execution** (multi-user eventually)\\n5. **Must preserve existing state file format** (add extensions, don\'t replace)\\n\\n## Success Criteria (Overall)\\n\\n1. \\u2705 Real-time progress visible to users\\n2. \\u2705 Error recovery succeeds > 80% for retryable failures\\n3. \\u2705 Performance metrics tracked for all agents\\n4. \\u2705 All existing tests continue to pass\\n5. \\u2705 Documentation updated for new features\\n6. \\u2705 Zero breaking changes to agent definitions\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n**Phase 1: Progress Streaming** (Implement First)\\n- High user impact\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Foundation for other improvements\\n\\n**Phase 2: Error Recovery** (Implement Second)\\n- High reliability impact\\n- High complexity (needs Phase 1 for monitoring)\\n- Builds on state persistence system\\n\\n**Phase 3: Performance Analytics** (Implement Third)\\n- Enables long-term improvement\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Leverages data from Phase 1 & 2\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Updated `AgentRuntime` class with progress events\\n2. Enhanced `StateManager` with full resume capability\\n3. New `AgentAnalytics` module for metrics tracking\\n4. Updated WebSocket handlers for streaming\\n5. New API endpoints for analytics queries\\n6. Updated documentation (README, implementation guide)\\n7. Test suite covering new functionality\\n8. Performance benchmarks before/after\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n\\n- **Improvement #1**: 2-3 days (progress streaming)\\n- **Improvement #2**: 3-4 days (error recovery)\\n- **Improvement #3**: 2-3 days (analytics)\\n- **Testing & Documentation**: 1-2 days\\n- **Total**: 8-12 days for complete implementation\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis analysis prioritizes improvements that:\\n1. **Maximize user value** (progress feedback eliminates uncertainty)\\n2. **Improve system reliability** (error recovery reduces failures)\\n3. **Enable continuous improvement** (analytics identify what to optimize next)\\n\\nThe three improvements are complementary and build on each other, creating a more robust and observable agent system.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VPzfVfknnXXDxSxiY3Jeb8', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Ensemble Agent System Architecture Proposal\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Core Design Philosophy\n- **Observability First**: Enhance system transparency and reliability\n- **Adaptive Intelligence**: Build self-improving mechanisms\n- **Minimal Overhead**: Optimize performance while adding new capabilities\n\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\n- **Layered Microservices Architecture**\n- **Event-Driven Communication**\n- **Stateful Components with Checkpoint Recovery**\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Framework**: FastAPI (async, high-performance)\n- **Async Runtime**: asyncio\n- **WebSocket**: Starlette WebSocket support\n- **State Management**: Redis for distributed caching\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + Grafana\n\n### State & Messaging\n- **Event Bus**: RabbitMQ (reliable, scalable messaging)\n- **State Persistence**: Redis + Local Filesystem Checkpoints\n- **Metrics Database**: InfluxDB (time-series performance tracking)\n\n### Frontend (Optional Monitoring Dashboard)\n- **Framework**: Vue.js 3\n- **State Management**: Vuex\n- **Real-Time Updates**: Socket.IO\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### A. Progress Streaming Service\n```\n{\n    "responsibility": "Real-time agent execution tracking",\n    "features": [\n        "Granular event emission",\n        "WebSocket broadcast",\n        "Low-latency updates (<500ms)"\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### B. Error Recovery Manager\n```\n{\n    "responsibility": "Automatic failure detection and resume",\n    "features": [\n        "Exponential backoff retry",\n        "Context preservation",\n        "Error classification",\n        "Checkpoint validation"\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### C. Agent Analytics Engine\n```\n{\n    "responsibility": "Performance tracking and optimization",\n    "features": [\n        "Metrics collection",\n        "Model performance comparison",\n        "Adaptive model selection",\n        "Cost optimization tracking"\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\n\n```\nAgent Execution Flow:\n[User Request] → [Progress Streaming Service]\n             ↓\n    [Error Recovery Manager] ← [Checkpoint Store]\n             ↓\n    [Agent Analytics Engine] → [Metrics Database]\n             ↓\n    [Final Result Delivery]\n```\n\n## 5. Deployment Strategy\n\n### Containerization\n- **Docker Compose** for local development\n- **Kubernetes** for production scaling\n- **Helm Charts** for consistent deployment\n\n### CI/CD\n- **GitHub Actions** for testing\n- **Automated Deployment** to staging/production\n- **Blue-Green Deployment** for zero-downtime updates\n\n## 6. Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Testing\n- **pytest** for backend\n- **Coverage Target**: 95%\n- **Mocking**: Extensive use of `unittest.mock`\n\n### Integration Testing\n- **Docker Compose** test environments\n- **Chaos Testing**: Simulate failure scenarios\n- **Performance Benchmarks**\n\n## 7. Security Considerations\n- JWT Authentication\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n- Encrypted WebSocket connections\n- Rate limiting on all endpoints\n\n## 8. Performance Optimization\n\n### Caching Strategies\n- **L1 Cache**: In-memory (per-service)\n- **L2 Cache**: Distributed Redis\n- **Intelligent Eviction Policies**\n\n### Performance Targets\n- **Latency**: <100ms for most operations\n- **Throughput**: 100 concurrent agent executions\n- **Resource Efficiency**: < 10% overhead from new features\n\n## 9. Scalability Plan\n- Stateless service design\n- Horizontal scaling via Kubernetes\n- Dynamic resource allocation\n- Circuit breaker patterns\n\n## 10. Open Questions & User Input Needed\n1. Preferred monitoring dashboard design\n2. Acceptable performance overhead threshold\n3. Specific error recovery granularity\n\n## 11. Risks & Mitigations\n\n### Primary Risks\n- **Increased Complexity**: Mitigated by clear component boundaries\n- **Performance Overhead**: Extensive benchmarking\n- **Token Cost Increase**: Adaptive model selection\n\n## 12. Migration Path\n- **Phase 1**: Progress Streaming (Low Risk)\n- **Phase 2**: Error Recovery (Medium Risk)\n- **Phase 3**: Analytics Engine (Highest Risk)\n\n## Implementation Complexity\n- **Estimated Development Time**: 8-12 days\n- **Team Size Recommendation**: 2 senior engineers'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VPzfVfknnXXDxSxiY3Jeb8', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025915.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025915.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path