{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:25", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-266194d3-172c-417b-8603-4fbde921c6b5', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Project View Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XqbptKMAqYhh9SPbkCLUh7', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XqbptKMAqYhh9SPbkCLUh7', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Project View Dashboard\\n**Description**: Add a dedicated Project View to the Ensemble UI that displays project status, SDLC position, milestone progress, next steps, and includes a \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button to advance implementation.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend API Enhancement\\n**Objective**: Create and enhance backend endpoints to support project view functionality\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Enhanced `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` endpoint for detailed project view\\n2. New `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` endpoint to trigger project continuation\\n3. SDLC phase determination logic from project notes/status\\n4. Integration with existing project_tracker.py module\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` returns complete project state including SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n- POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` triggers a new Executive Director with appropriate context\\n- API handles missing/incomplete project data gracefully\\n- Endpoints respond within specified performance thresholds (<500ms for list, <1s for details)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None (uses existing project_tracker.py)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend Project View Components\\n**Objective**: Build React components for the Project View dashboard\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. ProjectView.jsx - Main container component with project list and details pane\\n2. ProjectStatusCard.jsx - Project header showing name, status, timestamps\\n3. SDLCIndicator.jsx - Visual SDLC phase progress indicator\\n4. MilestoneProgress.jsx - Milestone tracking with progress bar\\n5. NextStepsPanel.jsx - Actionable next steps display\\n6. Integration with App.jsx navigation (new \\"Projects\\" tab)\\n7. API service integration (api.js updates)\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Project list displays all projects with status badges\\n- Selected project shows detailed view with all required information\\n- SDLC indicator clearly shows current phase\\n- Milestone progress displays numerical counts and visual progress bar\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button triggers backend continuation endpoint\\n- UI follows existing dark theme and Bootstrap patterns\\n- Loading and error states handled appropriately\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (backend endpoints must be available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Testing and Polish\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing and UI refinement\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Backend unit tests for new endpoints\\n2. Frontend component tests (Jest/React Testing Library)\\n3. Integration testing for continue functionality\\n4. Error handling refinement\\n5. Loading state animations\\n6. Documentation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All new backend endpoints have unit test coverage\\n- Frontend components render correctly in tests\\n- Continue functionality works end-to-end\\n- Error states display user-friendly messages\\n- Documentation updated for new endpoints\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1 and 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### Architecture Decisions\\n1. **SDLC Phase Tracking**: Will infer SDLC phase from project notes by scanning for phase-related keywords (requirements, architecture, planning, implementation, testing). This is pragmatic given current data.\\n\\n2. **Milestone Data Source**: Will use project tracker tasks and notes to infer milestones. Tasks tagged as milestones or notes with category \\"milestone\\" will be used.\\n\\n3. **Continue Functionality**: Will spawn a new Executive Director agent with the project context, instructing it to continue to the next phase/milestone.\\n\\n4. **Component Structure**: Single ProjectView.jsx as main container with sub-components for modularity, following existing patterns like SelfImprovementDashboard.\\n\\n### Technical Stack (Following Existing Patterns)\\n- Backend: FastAPI (Python) with existing project_tracker integration\\n- Frontend: React with Bootstrap components\\n- State: Local React state (following App.jsx pattern)\\n- Styling: Inline styles with existing dark theme colors\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **SDLC Phase Detection**: If project notes don\'t contain phase information, default to \\"unknown\\" with graceful UI handling\\n2. **Milestone Data**: If no milestone data exists, show \\"No milestones defined\\" rather than empty state\\n3. **Continue Action**: Include confirmation dialog and proper error handling for failed continuation attempts\\n\\n## Estimated Scope\\n- **Milestone 1**: ~200-300 lines backend code\\n- **Milestone 2**: ~500-700 lines frontend code (5 components + api changes)\\n- **Milestone 3**: ~200-300 lines test code + documentation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ee6gxxSmKVr8EoDpkuh3CJ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Project View Implementation - Architecture Proposal\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n**Architectural Pattern**: Modular Single Page Application (SPA) with API-driven architecture\n**Key Goal**: Create a flexible, extensible project view dashboard that integrates with existing project tracking infrastructure\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\n  - Lightweight, high-performance\n  - Native OpenAPI/Swagger support\n  - Async capabilities for future scalability\n\n### Frontend\n- **Language**: JavaScript/TypeScript\n- **Framework**: React\n  - Component-based architecture\n  - Lightweight state management\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap with custom dark theme\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\n\n### Integration\n- **API Communication**: Axios for HTTP requests\n- **State Management**: Local React state (Context API)\n- **Authentication**: Inherit from existing app authentication\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### Backend Components\n1. **Project Details Endpoint** (`/api/projects/{project_id}/details`)\n   - Retrieve comprehensive project information\n   - Dynamically generate SDLC phase\n   - Aggregate milestone and task data\n\n2. **Project Continuation Endpoint** (`/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`)\n   - Trigger next phase of project\n   - Spawn Executive Director with project context\n   - Handle state transitions\n\n### Frontend Components\n1. **ProjectView.jsx** (Main Container)\n   - Manage project list and detail views\n   - Handle API interactions\n   - Coordinate sub-components\n\n2. **ProjectStatusCard.jsx**\n   - Display project metadata\n   - Show high-level status indicators\n\n3. **SDLCIndicator.jsx**\n   - Visual representation of current project phase\n   - Dynamic phase detection\n\n4. **MilestoneProgress.jsx**\n   - Track and visualize milestone completion\n   - Numerical and graphical progress\n\n5. **NextStepsPanel.jsx**\n   - Display actionable next steps\n   - "Continue to Next Step" functionality\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n```\n[Frontend: React Components]\n        ↓\n[Axios HTTP Requests]\n        ↓\n[FastAPI Endpoints]\n        ↓\n[project_tracker.py Module]\n        ↓\n[Project Notes/Tasks Database]\n```\n\n## 5. File/Directory Structure\n```\nsrc/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── projects.py         # Project-related endpoints\n│   │   └── continue_handler.py # Project continuation logic\n│   └── services/\n│       └── sdlc_detector.py    # SDLC phase inference\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── components/\n│   │   ├── ProjectView.jsx\n│   │   ├── ProjectStatusCard.jsx\n│   │   ├── SDLCIndicator.jsx\n│   │   ├── MilestoneProgress.jsx\n│   │   └── NextStepsPanel.jsx\n│   └── services/\n│       └── api.js              # API interaction methods\n```\n\n## 6. API Design\n### GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/details`\n**Response Schema**:\n```json\n{\n  "project_id": "string",\n  "name": "string",\n  "current_phase": "string",\n  "milestones": [\n    {\n      "name": "string",\n      "status": "string",\n      "progress": "number"\n    }\n  ],\n  "next_steps": ["string"]\n}\n```\n\n### POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`\n**Request**:\n```json\n{\n  "force": "boolean",\n  "context": "object"\n}\n```\n\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\n- **Containerization**: Docker for backend\n- **Frontend**: Static file hosting (Vercel/Netlify)\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions for automated testing and deployment\n\n## 8. Testing Strategy\n### Backend\n- **Unit Tests**: \n  - Endpoint response validation\n  - SDLC phase detection logic\n- **Integration Tests**: \n  - API endpoint interactions\n  - Project continuation workflow\n\n### Frontend\n- **Component Tests**: \n  - Render verification\n  - Interaction simulation\n- **Snapshot Testing**\n- **Mock API Responses**\n\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\n1. **SDLC Phase Detection**\n   - Mitigation: Graceful fallback to "unknown" phase\n   - Provide clear user guidance\n\n2. **Missing Project Data**\n   - Mitigation: Implement robust error handling\n   - Display helpful messages for incomplete data\n\n## 10. Open Questions\n- Precise definition of "Continue to Next Step" workflow\n- Specific UX for milestone tracking\n- Performance optimization for large project lists\n\n## 11. Alternatives Considered\n1. **Redux for State Management**\n   - Rejected: Overhead too high for current scope\n   - Local state sufficient for current requirements\n\n2. **GraphQL API**\n   - Rejected: Existing REST infrastructure more straightforward\n   - Future consideration for complex querying needs\n\n## Conclusion\nThis architecture provides a modular, extensible approach to project view implementation, leveraging existing infrastructure while introducing new capabilities with minimal disruption.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ee6gxxSmKVr8EoDpkuh3CJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025925.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025925.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
