{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:25", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4cbf85a7-8aa7-473d-b5f4-9d161af618d1', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "UI Enhancements Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WdvWqAaW6VqSefsdT24tA6', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WdvWqAaW6VqSefsdT24tA6', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI Enhancement - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the existing Ensemble UI with several user experience improvements to better track agent hierarchies, manage completed items, and provide better visibility into system metrics and code changes.\\n\\n## Project Name\\nensemble-ui-enhancements\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Add question linking from agent hierarchy to original spawning question\\n2. Implement completed items section with collapsible/hideable functionality\\n3. Add two-word subject summaries to differentiate agent hierarchies at a glance\\n4. Improve layout: enlarge problem description section, make activity feed narrower\\n5. Make current agent tasks and activity feed collapsible\\n6. Add new metrics pane showing current models in use and code deltas\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n**Feature 1: Agent Hierarchy Question Links**\\n- Add links in the AgentHierarchyTree component to the question that spawned each hierarchy\\n- Ensure links scroll or navigate to the relevant question in the UI\\n- Visual indication that hierarchy is linked to a question\\n\\n**Feature 2: Completed Items Management**\\n- Create a \\"Completed\\" section for finished tasks/agents\\n- Make the completed section collapsible or hideable (either approach acceptable)\\n- Move completed items from active view to completed section automatically\\n- Maintain ability to view completed item details when needed\\n\\n**Feature 3: Agent Hierarchy Differentiation**\\n- Generate two-word subject summaries for each agent hierarchy\\n- Display summary prominently in hierarchy view\\n- Summaries should be derived from task/problem description\\n- Make hierarchies easily distinguishable at a glance\\n\\n**Feature 4: Layout Improvements**\\n- Enlarge problem description textarea (more height and width)\\n- Reduce width of activity feed column\\n- Redistribute space: more to problem input, less to activity feed\\n- Maintain responsive design principles\\n\\n**Feature 5: Collapsible Sections**\\n- Make \\"Current Agent Tasks\\" pane collapsible\\n- Make \\"Activity Feed\\" pane collapsible\\n- Preserve collapse state during updates\\n- Add clear visual indicators for collapsed/expanded state\\n\\n**Feature 6: Metrics Pane**\\n- New pane showing current models in use (Haiku, Sonnet, Opus counts)\\n- Display code delta metrics (lines added/removed, files changed)\\n- Real-time updates matching existing polling mechanism\\n- Clean, readable presentation of metrics\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Backend API changes (unless absolutely necessary for metrics)\\n- Authentication or user management\\n- Historical metrics or charting\\n- Export functionality for metrics\\n- Custom theme or color scheme changes beyond necessary UI adjustments\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing React + Bootstrap UI framework\\n- Must work with existing API endpoints in `/services/api.js`\\n- Must maintain current polling mechanism (configurable intervals)\\n- No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n- Responsive design must be preserved\\n\\n## Current Architecture Context\\n- **Frontend**: React with React-Bootstrap components\\n- **State Management**: Local React state with hooks\\n- **API Communication**: REST API via services/api.js\\n- **Polling**: 500ms-2s configurable intervals\\n- **Layout**: 3-column Bootstrap grid (currently 3-5-4 split)\\n\\n## Detailed Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Agent Hierarchy Question Links\\n- Add `question_id` or reference tracking to hierarchy data\\n- Implement clickable links in AgentHierarchyTree component\\n- Link should scroll to or highlight associated question\\n- Visual connection (icon, color coding) between hierarchy and question\\n\\n### 2. Completed Items Section\\n- Filter agents/tasks by status === \'completed\'\\n- Create separate collapsible section below active items\\n- Add \\"Show/Hide Completed\\" toggle button or collapse icon\\n- Maintain count badge showing number of completed items\\n- Default state: collapsed/hidden to reduce clutter\\n\\n### 3. Two-Word Subject Summaries\\n- Generate from problem description or task name\\n- Algorithm: extract key nouns/verbs, create 2-word summary\\n- Examples: \\"UI Enhancement\\", \\"API Integration\\", \\"Bug Fix\\"\\n- Display next to hierarchy title or as subtitle\\n- Make it prominent for quick scanning\\n\\n### 4. Layout Adjustments\\n**Current**: Col md={3} | md={5} | md={4}\\n**Proposed**: Col md={4} | md={4} | md={4} (or 4-3-5)\\n- Problem description textarea: increase rows from 4 to 6-8\\n- Make problem description card wider within its column\\n- Activity feed column should be narrower\\n- Ensure all content remains accessible and readable\\n\\n### 5. Collapsible Sections Implementation\\n- Use Bootstrap Collapse component or custom implementation\\n- Add chevron icons to indicate expand/collapse state\\n- Store collapse state in component state (preserve during re-renders)\\n- Smooth transitions when collapsing/expanding\\n- Sections affected:\\n  - Current Agent Tasks card\\n  - Activity Feed card\\n\\n### 6. Metrics Pane\\n**New section showing:**\\n- **Models in Use**:\\n  - Count of agents using Haiku\\n  - Count of agents using Sonnet\\n  - Count of agents using Opus\\n- **Code Delta Metrics**:\\n  - Total lines added (if available from API)\\n  - Total lines removed (if available from API)\\n  - Files changed count\\n  - Last updated timestamp\\n  \\n**Implementation**:\\n- Add new API endpoint or extend existing status endpoint\\n- Poll at same interval as other data\\n- Display in card format (similar to existing cards)\\n- Consider placement: below current tasks or as separate column section\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Question Links**: Click on hierarchy item navigates/scrolls to associated question\\n2. **Completed Section**: Completed items move to separate collapsible section automatically\\n3. **Summaries**: Each hierarchy displays clear 2-word summary\\n4. **Layout**: Problem description is noticeably larger, activity feed narrower but still functional\\n5. **Collapsible**: Both Current Tasks and Activity Feed can be collapsed/expanded smoothly\\n6. **Metrics**: New pane displays real-time model usage and code metrics\\n7. **No Regressions**: All existing functionality continues to work\\n8. **Performance**: UI remains responsive with no noticeable lag\\n9. **Tests**: New components have unit tests, existing tests still pass\\n\\n## Implementation Assumptions\\n- **Backend Support**: Assume backend can provide necessary data (question IDs, metrics)\\n  - If metrics not available from backend, display mock/placeholder with note\\n- **Summary Generation**: Frontend-based text processing acceptable for subject summaries\\n- **Persistence**: Collapse states don\'t need to persist across page reloads\\n- **Browser Support**: Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge - latest versions)\\n\\n## API Endpoint Assumptions\\nAssume these are available or can be added:\\n- Existing endpoints already provide sufficient data for features 1-5\\n- May need new endpoint for metrics: `GET /api/metrics` returning:\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\"models\\": {\\n      \\"haiku\\": 5,\\n      \\"sonnet\\": 3,\\n      \\"opus\\": 1\\n    },\\n    \\"code_delta\\": {\\n      \\"lines_added\\": 245,\\n      \\"lines_removed\\": 89,\\n      \\"files_changed\\": 12\\n    },\\n    \\"last_updated\\": \\"2024-01-11T02:56:00Z\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Updated React components:\\n   - AgentHierarchyTree.jsx (with question links)\\n   - App.jsx (layout changes, collapsible sections)\\n   - New MetricsPane.jsx component\\n   - Updated/new components for completed items management\\n2. Updated CSS/styling for layout changes\\n3. Unit tests for new components and modified functionality\\n4. Updated API service layer if new endpoints needed\\n5. README updates documenting new features\\n\\n## Future Considerations (Not in Current Scope)\\n- Persistent collapse state in localStorage\\n- Historical metrics charting\\n- Customizable column layouts\\n- Export metrics to CSV/JSON\\n- Advanced filtering for completed items\\n- Search functionality in hierarchies\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019dDxYnwP2dG5siBiCpGgXu', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Ensemble UI Enhancements - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### Architectural Pattern: Feature-Driven Modular React Architecture\nThe proposed architecture maintains the existing React + Bootstrap framework while introducing modular, composable components that enhance the user interface with new features.\n\n**Key Architectural Goals:**\n- Minimal invasiveness to existing codebase\n- High modularity and reusability\n- Maintainable and testable component structure\n- Performance optimization\n- Responsive design preservation\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React (Existing)\n- **Styling**: React-Bootstrap\n- **State Management**: React Hooks (useState, useContext)\n- **Utility Libraries**: \n  - `lodash` for text processing\n  - `react-intersection-observer` for scrolling/visibility features\n\n### Development Tools\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\n- **Linting**: ESLint\n- **Code Formatting**: Prettier\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. AgentHierarchyTree (Enhanced)\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Render agent hierarchies\n- Add question linking\n- Generate and display two-word summaries\n- Support collapsible/expandable views\n\n### 2. CompletedItemsSection (New Component)\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Manage and display completed tasks/agents\n- Provide toggle for showing/hiding completed items\n- Maintain completed items count\n\n### 3. MetricsPane (New Component)\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Display model usage metrics\n- Show code delta information\n- Real-time updates via polling mechanism\n\n### 4. Layout Manager\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Implement responsive grid adjustments\n- Manage column width redistributions\n- Handle section collapsibility\n\n## D. File/Directory Structure\n```\nsrc/\n├── components/\n│   ├── AgentHierarchyTree/\n│   │   ├── index.jsx\n│   │   ├── QuestionLink.jsx\n│   │   └── SummaryGenerator.js\n│   ├── CompletedItemsSection/\n│   │   └── index.jsx\n│   ├── MetricsPane/\n│   │   └── index.jsx\n│   └── common/\n│       ├── CollapsibleSection.jsx\n│       └── ResponsiveGrid.jsx\n├── services/\n│   ├── api.js         # Existing API service\n│   └── metricsService.js  # New metrics data fetching\n├── utils/\n│   └── textProcessing.js  # Summary generation utilities\n└── App.jsx\n```\n\n## E. Data Flow & State Management\n\n### State Propagation\n- Use React Context for global state management\n- Lightweight hooks-based approach\n- Polling mechanism integrated into services\n\n### Data Fetching Strategy\n- Maintain existing 500ms-2s polling interval\n- Add new `/api/metrics` endpoint handler\n- Implement defensive error handling\n\n## F. API Design\n\n### New Metrics Endpoint\n```json\nGET /api/metrics\nResponse: {\n  "models": {\n    "haiku": 5,\n    "sonnet": 3,\n    "opus": 1\n  },\n  "code_delta": {\n    "lines_added": 245,\n    "lines_removed": 89,\n    "files_changed": 12\n  },\n  "last_updated": "2024-01-11T02:56:00Z"\n}\n```\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n- Existing React build process\n- No changes to deployment pipeline\n- Compatibility with current hosting infrastructure\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Component Testing\n- Jest snapshot testing\n- React Testing Library for interaction tests\n- 90%+ code coverage goal\n\n### Testing Focus Areas\n- Question link generation\n- Metrics display accuracy\n- Collapsible section behaviors\n- Responsive layout rendering\n\n## I. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### 1. Performance Overhead\n**Risk**: New components might slow rendering\n**Mitigation**: \n- Use React.memo\n- Implement lazy loading\n- Optimize polling intervals\n\n### 2. Browser Compatibility\n**Risk**: New features might break in older browsers\n**Mitigation**:\n- Test across modern browsers\n- Provide graceful degradation\n- Use well-supported React patterns\n\n## J. Open Questions for Stakeholder Review\n1. Preferred method of question linking (scroll vs. navigate)\n2. Desired default state for completed items section (collapsed/expanded)\n3. Specific preferences for two-word summary generation algorithm\n\n## K. Implementation Phases\n1. AgentHierarchyTree Enhancements\n2. Completed Items Section\n3. Metrics Pane\n4. Layout Adjustments\n5. Comprehensive Testing\n\n## Architecture Decision Record\n- Maintained existing React + Bootstrap stack\n- Chose modular, minimally invasive approach\n- Prioritized performance and user experience\n- Focused on flexible, extensible design'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019dDxYnwP2dG5siBiCpGgXu', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025925.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025925.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create 