ation with Agent Runtime\\n- Real-time Agent Status Display\\n- Agent Hierarchy Visualization\\n- Comprehensive Error Handling\\n- Responsive, Professional UI\\n\\n## Technical Stack\\n- Backend: Python 3.11+, FastAPI\\n- Frontend: React 18, Tailwind CSS\\n- WebSocket for real-time updates\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. User can submit problem description\\n2. Backend spawns Executive Director agent\\n3. Agent execution tracked in real-time\\n4. Agent hierarchy displays dynamically\\n5. Results displayed clearly\\n6. Errors handled professionally\\n7. All tests pass\\n8. Responsive, intuitive UI\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Use existing Ensemble agent runtime\\n- Follow Test-Driven Development\\n- Handle long-running tasks asynchronously\\n- Maintain clean, modular architecture"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016ufctdYUs8VpAF8trehpTv', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/requirements.md', 'milestone_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestones.md', 'project_name': 'Ensemble UI Requirements Implementation', 'specific_task': 'Update interval selector from high-frequency options (500ms, 1s, 2s) to production intervals (1s, 1m, 5m)', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016ufctdYUs8VpAF8trehpTv', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ju6x2NhFk7o2HEHQ6c9p6B', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ju6x2NhFk7o2HEHQ6c9p6B', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Names Integration: Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Decorator/Generator Integration\\n- **Core Approach:** Lightweight, non-invasive modification to existing agent runtime\\n- **Pattern:** Decorator pattern for name generation\\n- **Goal:** Minimal changes to existing system while adding significant UX improvement\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n- **Language:** Python 3.9+\\n- **Runtime:** Existing agent framework\\n- **Dependencies:** Standard library only (threading, random)\\n- **No external package dependencies**\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 3.1 Name Data Source\\n- **Module:** `name_data.py`\\n- **Responsibility:** Provide list of whimsical names\\n- **Location:** `src/runtime/agents/name_data.py`\\n\\n### 3.2 Name Generator\\n- **Class:** `AgentNameGenerator`\\n- **Responsibilities:**\\n  - Generate unique whimsical names\\n  - Handle name collisions\\n  - Ensure thread-safety\\n- **Location:** `src/runtime/agents/name_generator.py`\\n\\n### 3.3 Runtime Integration\\n- **Target:** `AgentRuntime.__init__` method\\n- **Modification:** Replace timestamp-based ID generation\\n- **Preservation:** Backward compatibility with explicit `agent_id`\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow\\n```\\n[Name Data Source] -> [Name Generator] -> [AgentRuntime] -> [Activity Tracker]\\n       \\u2191                   |                   |\\n       |                   |                   |\\n  1000 Whimsical    Thread-Safe Name     Unique Agent ID\\n     Names          Generation           Assigned\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\\n\\n### 5.1 Name Generation Strategy\\n- **Randomization:** Shuffle name pool on initialization\\n- **Uniqueness:** \\n  - Use thread-safe set to track used names\\n  - Add numeric suffix for collisions\\n- **Performance:** O(1) name generation\\n\\n### 5.2 Concurrency Handling\\n- **Mechanism:** Explicit threading lock\\n- **Approach:** Prevent race conditions during name generation\\n- **Performance Impact:** Minimal overhead, < 1ms per name generation\\n\\n## 6. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Name Collision\\n- **Mitigation:** \\n  - Numeric suffix system\\n  - Large initial name pool (1000 names)\\n  - Explicit collision resolution mechanism\\n\\n### Risk: Performance Degradation\\n- **Mitigation:**\\n  - Lightweight name generation algorithm\\n  - Minimal synchronization overhead\\n  - Constant-time name selection\\n\\n## 7. Testing Approach\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- Name uniqueness verification\\n- Collision handling\\n- Thread-safety validation\\n- Edge case handling (large number of agents)\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- Agent runtime integration\\n- Activity tracker compatibility\\n- UI rendering of new names\\n\\n## 8. Deployment Considerations\\n- **No database migrations**\\n- **No runtime environment changes**\\n- **Backward compatible**\\n- **Zero downtime deployment possible**\\n\\n## 9. Future Extensibility\\n- Easy to add more names\\n- Potential for theming or categorization\\n- Simple to modify name generation logic\\n\\n## 10. Alternative Approaches Considered\\n1. **UUID-based Names**: \\n   - Pros: Guaranteed uniqueness\\n   - Cons: Not human-readable\\n2. **Incremental Numbering**: \\n   - Pros: Simple\\n   - Cons: Less memorable\\n3. **External Name Service**: \\n   - Pros: Scalable\\n   - Cons: Added complexity\\n\\n**Chosen Approach:** Current implementation - lightweight, performant, human-friendly\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01D8T6Zrcm4pbq2Rj45U5fRZ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Ensemble UI Interval Options Update: Architecture\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Architectural Pattern: Component-Level Update\n- **Core Approach:** Modify existing interval selector UI component\n- **Pattern:** Direct component modification with backwards compatibility\n- **Goal:** Change interval options from high-frequency (500ms, 1s, 2s) to production-suitable (1s, 1m, 5m)\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n- **Frontend:** React 18+ with TypeScript\n- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS\n- **State Management:** React hooks (useState/useEffect)\n- **Testing:** Jest + React Testing Library\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### 3.1 Interval Selector Component\n- **Location:** `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/`\n- **Responsibility:** Display interval dropdown/selector\n- **Modification Required:** Update options array and conversion logic\n\n### 3.2 Interval Conversion Logic\n- **Location:** Within interval selector or utility module\n- **Responsibility:** Convert user-friendly labels to milliseconds\n- **Current:** 500ms, 1s, 2s → 500, 1000, 2000ms\n- **Target:** 1s, 1m, 5m → 1000, 60000, 300000ms\n\n### 3.3 Real-time Update Handler\n- **Location:** WebSocket or polling mechanism\n- **Responsibility:** Use selected interval for status updates\n- **Modification Required:** Accept new interval values\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n```\n[User Selects Interval] → [Convert to Milliseconds] → [Update Mechanism] → [Backend Polling/WebSocket]\n        ↓                          ↓                        ↓\n   "1s", "1m", "5m"         1000, 60000, 300000      Timer/Interval Update\n```\n\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\n\n### 5.1 Interval Options\n- **Previous:** 500ms, 1s, 2s (too frequent for production)\n- **New:** 1s, 1m, 5m (practical for monitoring)\n- **Default:** 1s (maintains reasonable responsiveness)\n\n### 5.2 Conversion Strategy\n```typescript\nconst INTERVAL_OPTIONS = [\n  { label: "1s", value: 1000 },\n  { label: "1m", value: 60000 }, \n  { label: "5m", value: 300000 }\n];\n```\n\n### 5.3 Backwards Compatibility\n- Handle any saved preferences gracefully\n- Default to 1s if invalid value encountered\n- No breaking changes to API contracts\n\n## 6. Component Architecture\n\n### File Structure\n```\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\n├── components/\n│   ├── IntervalSelector.tsx          (main component to modify)\n│   └── __tests__/\n│       └── IntervalSelector.test.tsx (test file to update)\n└── utils/\n    └── intervalUtils.ts              (conversion utilities)\n```\n\n## 7. Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Locate Components\n- Find interval selector UI component\n- Identify current options array\n- Locate conversion logic\n\n### Phase 2: Update Logic\n- Replace interval options\n- Update conversion mappings\n- Handle edge cases\n\n### Phase 3: Testing\n- Unit tests for conversion logic\n- Integration tests for UI behavior\n- Verify real-time updates work correctly\n\n## 8. Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests\n- Interval conversion accuracy\n- Option rendering\n- Default selection behavior\n- Invalid value handling\n\n### Integration Tests  \n- Full UI workflow\n- Real-time update frequency\n- WebSocket/polling integration\n- Error handling\n\n## 9. Risk Mitigation\n\n### Risk: Breaking Existing Functionality\n- **Mitigation:** Write tests first, comprehensive regression testing\n\n### Risk: Invalid Saved Preferences\n- **Mitigation:** Add fallback logic for invalid interval values\n\n### Risk: Performance Impact\n- **Mitigation:** New intervals are less frequent, should improve performance\n\n## 10. Success Criteria\n- UI shows only "1s", "1m", "5m" options\n- Each option applies correct millisecond interval\n- Real-time updates work at correct frequency\n- All tests pass\n- No console errors or warnings\n- Clean, maintainable code\n\n## 11. Deployment\n- No backend changes required\n- Frontend-only modification\n- Can be deployed independently\n- Backwards compatible with existing backend'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01D8T6Zrcm4pbq2Rj45U5fRZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/