:** Jest + React Testing Library\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 3.1 Interval Selector Component\\n- **Location:** `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/`\\n- **Responsibility:** Display interval dropdown/selector\\n- **Modification Required:** Update options array and conversion logic\\n\\n### 3.2 Interval Conversion Logic\\n- **Location:** Within interval selector or utility module\\n- **Responsibility:** Convert user-friendly labels to milliseconds\\n- **Current:** 500ms, 1s, 2s \\u2192 500, 1000, 2000ms\\n- **Target:** 1s, 1m, 5m \\u2192 1000, 60000, 300000ms\\n\\n### 3.3 Real-time Update Handler\\n- **Location:** WebSocket or polling mechanism\\n- **Responsibility:** Use selected interval for status updates\\n- **Modification Required:** Accept new interval values\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow\\n```\\n[User Selects Interval] \\u2192 [Convert to Milliseconds] \\u2192 [Update Mechanism] \\u2192 [Backend Polling/WebSocket]\\n        \\u2193                          \\u2193                        \\u2193\\n   \\"1s\\", \\"1m\\", \\"5m\\"         1000, 60000, 300000      Timer/Interval Update\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\\n\\n### 5.1 Interval Options\\n- **Previous:** 500ms, 1s, 2s (too frequent for production)\\n- **New:** 1s, 1m, 5m (practical for monitoring)\\n- **Default:** 1s (maintains reasonable responsiveness)\\n\\n### 5.2 Conversion Strategy\\n```typescript\\nconst INTERVAL_OPTIONS = [\\n  { label: \\"1s\\", value: 1000 },\\n  { label: \\"1m\\", value: 60000 }, \\n  { label: \\"5m\\", value: 300000 }\\n];\\n```\\n\\n### 5.3 Backwards Compatibility\\n- Handle any saved preferences gracefully\\n- Default to 1s if invalid value encountered\\n- No breaking changes to API contracts\\n\\n## 6. Component Architecture\\n\\n### File Structure\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 IntervalSelector.tsx          (main component to modify)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 IntervalSelector.test.tsx (test file to update)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 intervalUtils.ts              (conversion utilities)\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Phase 1: Locate Components\\n- Find interval selector UI component\\n- Identify current options array\\n- Locate conversion logic\\n\\n### Phase 2: Update Logic\\n- Replace interval options\\n- Update conversion mappings\\n- Handle edge cases\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing\\n- Unit tests for conversion logic\\n- Integration tests for UI behavior\\n- Verify real-time updates work correctly\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests\\n- Interval conversion accuracy\\n- Option rendering\\n- Default selection behavior\\n- Invalid value handling\\n\\n### Integration Tests  \\n- Full UI workflow\\n- Real-time update frequency\\n- WebSocket/polling integration\\n- Error handling\\n\\n## 9. Risk Mitigation\\n\\n### Risk: Breaking Existing Functionality\\n- **Mitigation:** Write tests first, comprehensive regression testing\\n\\n### Risk: Invalid Saved Preferences\\n- **Mitigation:** Add fallback logic for invalid interval values\\n\\n### Risk: Performance Impact\\n- **Mitigation:** New intervals are less frequent, should improve performance\\n\\n## 10. Success Criteria\\n- UI shows only \\"1s\\", \\"1m\\", \\"5m\\" options\\n- Each option applies correct millisecond interval\\n- Real-time updates work at correct frequency\\n- All tests pass\\n- No console errors or warnings\\n- Clean, maintainable code\\n\\n## 11. Deployment\\n- No backend changes required\\n- Frontend-only modification\\n- Can be deployed independently\\n- Backwards compatible with existing backend"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data